    "id": "63afde24-8057-4ee8-9e84-23895c400792",
    "title": "Colorado Statute and Guidance related to ELs (Part 1/2)",
    "content": "Colorado Statute and Guidance related to ELs\n\n“Colorado funds English Language Learners (ELLs) through a combination of federal and state sources, including Title III funds and state categorical programs like the English Language Proficiency Act (ELPA).” Additionally, some ELL students are included in the state's \"at-risk\" funding formula\n\nEnglish Language Proficiency Act: CDE Guidance/flyer (https://www.cde.state.co.us/cde_english/elpa-overview) This funding includes both a component to provide EL programs and a second component to provide professional development and student support.\n\nStatute: CO statute 22-24-101 through 22-24-108\n\nLink to statute language on Justia\n\nRegulations: https://www.sos.state.co.us/CCR/GenerateRulePdf.do?ruleVersionId=7752&amp;fileName=1%20CCR%20301-10\n\nState Board of Education Rules\n\nNOTE: Colorado uses the term “local education provider” instead of “local education agency”\n\nCO statute citations for supporting EL teacher professional development\n\n22-24-102(1)(d) “(d) The state and local education providers must enhance all educators' effectiveness in supporting English language development and in enabling English language learners to achieve and maintain grade-level performance in academic content areas;”\n\n22-24-102(1)(e) “(e) The state must develop an educator workforce that can support the educational approach and goals of local education providers to help ensure that English language learners are postsecondary and workforce ready at graduation;”\n\n22-24-102(1)(f) “(f) The state must appropriate and allocate moneys to local education providers to help ensure that English language learners are postsecondary and workforce ready at graduation;”\n\n22-24-108(1)(b) “(b) Provide effective professional development activities related to teaching English language learners for all educators who may work with English language learners in the classroom;”\n\nState Board of Education Educator Licensing Rule (see section 7)\n\nEnglish Learner Educator EL PD requirements for certain Content Teachers from the CO SBOE Rules: (https://ed.cde.state.co.us/educatortalent/elpdeducators) “educators with elementary, math, science, social studies and English language arts (and any middle-level) endorsements to complete Culturally and Linguistically Diverse (CLD) Education training or professional development (PD).” Requirement is 45 clock hours of professional learning aligned with CLD standards.\n\nCDE Professional Development: General Accepted Activities – see webpage (https://ed.cde.state.co.us/cdeprof/professional-development-general-accepted-activities)\n\nDocumenting clock hours: 1 semester hour of credit is equal to 15 clock hours (see In-service Education section). 90 hours (9 semesters hours) are needed for license renewal.\n\nIn-Service Education:\n\nSchool districts or BOCES are approved for in-service education programs. They must issue certificates for teachers to use as documentation of clock hour completion. If a district or BOCES contracts for CARE Coaching, it would be helpful for CARE Coaching to provide certificates for participants that indicates the number of clock hours per training. This could take some burden off the districts or BOCES.\n\nFrom the CDE website for In-Service Education documentation:\n\nDocumentation required:\n\nCompletion of the renewal summary portion of the online application.\n\nOptional: To support professional development entries, a certificate with participant’s name, name/title of in-service, name of agency providing in-service, location, dates and contact hours, signature of provider verifying participant attendance and completion of workshop may be uploaded. District “transcripts” are also accepted. Credit must be listed as contact hours. Should the evaluator have questions about the alignment of the professional development and educator standards, a full audit will be conducted and the educator will be asked to submit this back up documentation.\n\nInvolvement in School and/or District Performance:\n\nThis is generally related to accountability and school improvement, but “Professional development in the area of culturally and linguistically diverse education” is one of the activities listed in this section. Documentation required is a written log of meeting times and a signed letter from the committee chair verifying participation and the number of clock hours attended. Again, it would be helpful for CARE Coaching to provide certificates for participants that indicates the number of clock hours per training. If this could be adapted to include the written log of meeting times and a place for the committee chair to sign, that could be helpful.\n\nFrom the CDE website for Involved in School and/or District Performance:\n\n7.02(1)(d)(v) Professional development in the area of culturally and linguistically diverse education.\n\nDocumentation requires:\n\nCompletion of the renewal summary portion of the online application.\n\nSubmission of documentation that includes a written log of meetin",
