    "id": "022f37c3-33b0-4eab-81eb-be37361bd8c8",
    "title": "Potential Washington State Marketing Content (Part 1/2)",
    "content": "Potential Washington State Marketing Content\n\nWashington State Funding for CARE Coaching\n\nTransitional Bilingual Instruction Program Funding\n\nNOTE: TBIP funds can be used for alternate services to bilingual services (i.e. ESL or other services focused on only English language acquisition) if it isn’t feasible to implement a TBIP program. In targeting marketing, you should include all EL/ML programs, not just bilingual programs.\n\nExample email subject line: Check out CARE Coaching to meet your TBIP required PD\n\n[Dear Educator]\n\nChoose CARE Coaching to meet the professional learning requirements for Transitional Bilingual Instruction Programs (TBIP). Chapter 4 of the TBIP Washington State Policies and Practices Guide says, “Professional learning for ML teachers, classroom teachers, and paraeducators who work with multilingual learners is a critical part of every program and is required by state and federal law.” CARE Coaching tailors its PD to support your unique needs. Start with a CARE Coaching Needs Assessment (CCNA) to:\n\nIdentify strengths,\n\nPinpoint growth areas, and\n\nDrive data-informed professional learning plans to ignite sustainable instructional growth with measurable results\n\n[include a call to action, maybe something like – Check out what CARE Coaching has to offer – with a link to more information about the services CARE Coaching provides]\n\nTransitional Bilingual Instruction Program funds required Professional Learning\n\nWashington State law for TBIP programs includes a list of the duties of a school district board of directors. One of those duties is to, “Provide in-service training for teachers, counselors, and other staff, who are involved in the district's transitional bilingual program.” Consider using your TBIP funds to purchase CARE Coaching to satisfy this requirement.\n\n[then the ‘contact Yvonne’ call to action. This content can be adapted for flyers and brochures and targeted toward WA educators]\n\nLearning Assistance Program (LAP) –\n\nExample email subject line: Check out CARE Coaching for PD to support your LAP eligible ELs\n\nChoose CARE Coaching to provide professional learning for educators to support your Learning Assistance Program (LAP) eligible multilingual learners (MLs). One of the purposes of the LAP program, according to the LAP Guide, is to, “guide school districts in providing the most effective and efficient practices when implementing supplemental instruction and services to assist students who are not meeting academic standards.” The LAP FAQs document goes on to say, in Question A.4, that it is allowable to use LAP funds for professional learning and Question B.2 includes examples of the allowable types of professional learning that can be purchased with LAP funds.\n\nQuestions for you to Answer:\n\nAre there MLs in your schools that are eligible for LAP services?\n\nDo your educators need additional training to provide the ML interventions required by the LAP program to assist ML students who are not meeting academic standards?\n\nIf you answered YES to both of these questions, consider purchasing CARE Coaching with your LAP funds to provide the professional learning necessary to implement your LAP services effectively and efficiently.\n\n[then the ‘contact Yvonne’ call to action. This content can be adapted for flyers and brochures and targeted toward WA educators]\n\nTeacher certification maintenance / recertification Clock Hours\n\nNOTE: Before thinking about developing additional marketing content for teacher recertification clock hours, WCEPS should apply to become an Approved Provider. If WCEPS can become an approved provider, it would be lend additional weight to marketing content.\n\nALSO NOTE: It could be that LEAs and ESDs could purchase CARE Coaching and include the provision of clock hours for teacher recertification, but that needs to be confirmed.\n\nExample email subject line: Check out CARE Coaching for PD to provide required ‘Clock Hours’\n\nChoose CARE Coaching for teacher recertification Clock Hours. Educators in Washington State are required to complete 100 continuing education credits (clock hours) to maintain their teacher certification. CARE Coaching can help provide the needed clock hours for your educators working with multilingual learners (MLs). Chapter 4 of the TBIP Washington State Policies and Practices Guide says, “Professional learning for ML teachers, classroom teachers, and paraeducators who work with multilingual learners is a critical part of every program and is required by state and federal law.” CARE Coaching tailors its PD to support your unique needs. Start with a CARE Coaching Needs Assessment (CCNA) to:\n\nIdentify strengths,\n\nPinpoint growth areas, and\n\nDrive data-informed professional learning plans to ignite sustainable instructional growth with measurable results\n\n[include a call to action, maybe something like – Check out what CARE Coaching has to offer – with a link to more information about the services CARE Coaching provides]\n\n[then the ‘contact",
