  {
    "id": "42e3b403-e4c1-4713-86a0-46414c016c3b",
    "title": "Wisconsin Parental Choice Schools",
    "content": "File: Wisconsin Parental Choice Schools.pdf\nTitle: Wisconsin Parental Choice Schools\nTags: For selling to school choice schools in Wisconsin. This can serve as guidance.\nDescription: For selling to school choice schools in Wisconsin. This can serve as guidance. \n\nContent: Wisconsin Parental Choice Program List of schools: https://dpi.wi.gov/sites/default/files/imce/parental-education-options/Choice/Student_Application _Webpage/wpcp_2025-26_school_list.pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com Info for a PDF or LL post: CARE Coaching Professional Learning Support for Wisconsin Parental Choice Schools The Reality for Choice Schools Wisconsin Parental Choice schools are held to high expectations for student outcomes, instructional quality, and accountability — without access to the professional learning infrastructure available to public districts. Most Choice schools face: ● Limited funding flexibility for professional learning ● Small leadership teams carrying instructional, compliance, and staffing responsibilities ● Educator burnout and retention challenges ● A wide range of teacher experience levels in one building CARE Coaching exists to meet these realities head-on. What Is CARE Coaching? CARE Coaching is job-embedded, educator-centered professional learning that strengthens instructional practice, supports teacher retention, and builds internal capacity — without disrupting a school’s mission or autonomy. This is not one-size-fits-all PD. This is sustained support for the educators already serving your students. Why CARE Coaching Works for Choice Schools Mission-Aligned, Not Mandated CARE Coaching adapts to your school’s values, instructional approach, and culture. There is no prescribed curriculum and no compliance-driven agenda. Job-Embedded and Practical Coaching happens in the context of daily instruction — focused on what teachers are actually doing, not abstract theory or disconnected workshops. Strengthens Educator Retention Supported teachers stay longer. CARE Coaching reduces burnout, increases confidence, and helps schools retain effective educators in a competitive labor market. Builds Internal Capacity CARE develops instructional leadership within your school so growth continues beyond the coaching cycle. What CARE Coaching Supports ● Instructional clarity and consistency ● Reflective teaching practice ● Classroom management and student engagement ● Support for early-career and veteran educators ● Professional readiness and instructional confidence Demonstrate professionalism and instructional strength during DPI review processes — without adding paperwork or reporting burdens. Funding Fit for Choice Schools CARE Coaching is an allowable use of general Wisconsin Parental Choice Program funds as a professional learning and instructional support service. No new grants. No legislative changes. No complex reporting requirements. Simply a strategic investment in educator effectiveness and school stability. Who CARE Coaching Is For ● Wisconsin Parental Choice Program (WPCP) schools ● Schools participating in MPCP, RPCP, and/or SNSP ● Choice schools seeking sustainable, mission-aligned professional learning About WCEPS The Wisconsin Center for Education Products and Services (WCEPS) partners with schools to strengthen teaching and learning through high-quality professional learning and coaching. CARE Coaching reflects WCEPS’s commitment to: ● Educator growth ● Instructional excellence ● Sustainable school improvement Let’s Talk If your school is seeking professional learning that respects your autonomy, supports your educators, and aligns with Choice funding structures, CARE Coaching is designed for you. Learn more: https://www.wcepspathways.org/ Email text: Subject: Professional learning that fits Wisconsin Choice schools Hello [First Name], Leading a Wisconsin Parental Choice school means balancing instructional quality, educator support, and accountability — often without access to the professional learning infrastructure available to public districts. CARE Coaching from WCEPS was designed specifically for this reality. CARE Coaching provides job-embedded, mission-aligned professional learning that supports teachers in real classrooms, strengthens instructional practice, and improves educator retention — without adding reporting requirements or disrupting your school’s culture. Choice schools partner with CARE Coaching to: ● Support teachers through classroom-connected coaching ● Build instructional consistency across varied experience levels ● Reduce burnout that drives turnover ● Invest existing Choice program funds in educator effectiveness CARE Coaching is an allowable use of Wisconsin Parental Choice Program funds as a professional learning and instructional support service. No new grants. No added compliance. If you’re looking for professional learning that respects your autonomy and supports the educators already serving your students, CARE Coaching is designed for you. Learn more: https://www.wcepspathways.org/ If it’s helpful, I’d be glad to share a one-page overview or talk through whether CARE Coaching is a good fit for your school. I look forward to connecting with you. P",
