    "content": "he classroom level, such as the school or district level Terminology: Summative, Interim, &amp; Formative 1 -Summative 2 -Interim 3- Formative Usually used as part of an accountability program or to otherwise inform policy\n\nSummative, Interim, and Formative From  Perie , Marion, Gong &amp;  Wurtzel   (2007) Generally given once a year; typically ,  part of an accountability program or to otherwise inform policy Summative Interim  (instructional, evaluative, predictive) Formative  classroom (minute-by-minute, integrated into the lesson) Frequency of administration Scope and cycle duration Medium-scale, medium-cycle; designed to inform decision-making at multiple levels; results can be aggregated and reported at a broader level Occurs during instruction and is embedded within learning activities; provides feedback to adjust ongoing teaching and learning\n\nHow to select an interim assessment",
