    "title": "WIDA MODEL (Part 2/2)",
    "content": "ors and District Administrators to  monitor student testing progress to ensure anticipated completion rates ©️2024 Board of Regents of the University of Wisconsin System\n\nWIDA MODEL Interpretive Guide\n\nMODEL Online: Training &amp; Support Training Materials:  MODEL Online accounts house a library of training materials that can be used to prepare oneself to administer and score the MODEL Online assessment. MODEL Online Test Administration Webinar Series  ($200 person): This facilitator-led webinar series goes into detail regarding test administration procedures as well as scoring guidance and practice for the speaking and writing domains.\n\nWIDA MODEL Pricing &amp; Packaging\n\nMODEL Paper: Pricing and Packaging MODEL Paper is sold as grade level cluster kits.  The test administrator materials in each kit are reusable. The Replacement Parts are available for purchase in the WIDA Store. Kindergarten MODEL Kit  Includes 25 student response booklets/score sheets List Price:  $455 per kit Member Discount Price:  $374 Grade Level Cluster Kits  (1-2, 3-5, 6-8, 9-12) Includes 30 student response booklets     (15 Task 1 &amp; 15 Task 2)/ 30 score sheets List Price:  $390 per kit Member Discount Price:  $303\n\nGrounded in WIDA ELD Standards\n\nMODEL Online: Pricing and Packaging MODEL Online assessments are sold in sets of 10 tests.  Each test is good for one administration of all 4 domains Tests can be used with any student grades 1-12 MODEL tests have a 1yr expiration date List Price:  $200 per set Member Discount Price:  $160 per set\n\nWhat Educators Like about WIDA MODEL Part of the WIDA Assessment System Offers flexible administration No waiting for your students’ scores Test content has similar look and feel to ACCESS items MODEL scores predict performance on ACCESS for ELLs Score Reports provide scale &amp; proficiency level scores Online format has recently been updated with new content\n\nPurchasing WIDA MODEL https:// wceps.org /Store 2) Request a Quote 1) Buy from the WIDA Store Store@wceps.org\n\nThank you!\n\nA flexible, on-demand English language proficiency assessment that is part of WIDA’s comprehensive assessment system SCREENER INTERIM SUMMATIVE WIDA ACCESS (K-12) WIDA Alternate ACCESS WIDA MODEL (K-12) WIDA Screener (1-12) WIDA Screener for Kindergarten  or WIDA MODEL for Kindergarten Gather immediate English language proficiency level scores  Monitor students progress between annual summative assessments Inform instructional planning and other decisions related to students’ education Predict students’ performance on the WIDA ACCESS summative assessment Support formative assessment decision making Use WIDA MODEL to:\n\nAdministering Speaking Test Administrator Student\n\nSample Speaking Script Image displayed on student screen. Script is in bold. Instructions are  in parentheses. Multiple questions per task. Scoring guidance. Instructions for advancing the test.\n\nSample Listening Item\n\nGrades 1-5 Handwritten responses on Student Response Form \t Grades 6-12 Type responses in Secure Student Browser Writing Domain Test Format: Student-Constructed Responses 38\n\nFormat of Writing Task: Part A Part A:  Consists of a writing prompt that includes a picture. It is expected that students will produce  single words ,  phrases , or  simple sentences.\n\nLevels of English Proficiency\n\nFormat of Writing Task: Part B Part B:  Consists of a constructed response task designed to allow students to demonstrate their ability to write beyond single words and short phrases.   Grades 1-5 – handwritten response Grades  6-12 – typed  response\n\nSample Reading Item\n\nWIDA MODEL Implementation Interim Use:  Fall testing to gauge student progress between annual ACCESS administration Monitoring Student Progress:  Fall and spring testing to understand if students are making appropriate progress during the academic year Supplemental Use:   Administer as needed to make decisions related to a student’s education\n\nThe WIDA MODEL Team A collaborative partnership between three organizations:\n\nWIDA MODEL  Implementation &amp; Support\n\nKey Features of WIDA MODEL Available in an online and paper format for grades 1-12; K in paper format only Locally purchased, administered, and scored May be administered at any time during school year No waiting to get your scores back Provides meaningful insight into student language abilities Suite of flexible, on-demand English language proficiency assessments for grades K-12: MODEL scores can be used to predict student performance on ACCESS for ELLs ©️2024 Board of Regents of the University of Wisconsin System\n\nWIDA MODEL/ACCESS for ELLs  Predictive Study WIDA MODEL predicts results on ACCESS for ELLs – with empirical results from a study that tracked responses from students who took both WIDA MODEL and ACCESS for ELLs MODEL/ACCESS Concordance Table",
