    "id": "f7d7277d-192b-44b4-96e7-1fb753b7cd40",
    "title": "WIDA MODEL (Part 1/2)",
    "content": "WIDA MODEL\n\nOnline and Paper Test Modes Online Grades 1-12 All four domains needed to generate score report Larger group administration for listening, reading and writing Purchased in sets of 10; licenses can be used with any student grades 1-12 Scores are calculated by the test platform for Listening &amp; Reading Individual and group score reports Test content recently updated; more test item variation Paper Grades K-12 Possible to generate a domain-specific score Small group administration for reading and writing Purchased as a grade level cluster kit Use the score calculator to calculate scores and download score reports Individual score report\n\nGrade-level Clusters  *Kindergarten is only available as a paper-based kit with manipulatives\n\nTest Components and Sequence MODEL Online is a four domain assessment; all domains must be administered to generate a score report Speaking is 1:1 administered and Listening, Writing and Reading can be large group administered Listening and Reading domains are semi-adaptive Flexible domain administration order Speaking 1 student  PER TEST SESSION • Test Admin must        take scoring training • Scored while test is        in progress on TestNav • Student and Admin     view same screen. • Choose Set 1 or 2  Listening 1-20 students  PER TEST SESSION • Required: Headphones,     Test Nav app • Step 1 score informs    Step 2 difficulty track     placement  Step 2 difficulty tracks   Low Mid High Writing 1-20 students  PER TEST SESSION • Test Admin must        take scoring training • Choose Task 1, 2, or 3 Reading 1-20 students  PER TEST SESSION • Required: Headphones,     Test Nav app • Step 1 score informs    Step 2 difficulty track     placement  Step 2 difficulty tracks   Low Mid High\n\n10 Paper: Test Components and Sequence You may start with either  Speaking  or  Writing , but:  •  Speaking  must be administered to each student before their  Listening  Test  •  Writing  must be administered before their  Reading  Test\n\nENTERING EMERGING DEVELOPING EXPANDING BRIDGING 1 2 3 4 5 Listening/Reading Step 2: Low Listening/Reading Step 2: Mid Listening/Reading Step 2: High WIDA MODEL Test Items Adapt to   Student Proficiency\n\nSpeaking  1 on 1 Listening  1 on 1 Writing  varies by grade level K: 1 on 1 1-12: up to 5 Reading varies by grade level K, 1-2: 1 on 1 3-12: up to 5 How many? Paper:  Individual &amp; Small Group Administration 15\n\nApproximate Administration Times Test Administration Times Domain Test Approximate Administration Time Approx. 1h 40min Administrative Format Speaking Up to 15 minutes Individual Listening Up to 30 minutes Group or Individual** Writing Up to 30 minutes Group or Individual Reading Up to 25 minutes Group or Individual ** The paper listening domain test must be individually administered.\n\nMODEL Paper Materials Grade Level Cluster Kits:  K,  1-2,  3-5,  6-8,  9-12   The test administrator materials in each kit are reusable. Replacement/ Consumable parts are available in the WIDA Store.\n\nMODEL Online Platform LaunchPad  &amp; ADAM:  web-based interfaces that function as the control center for your MODEL Online account. Student Testing Platform:  All domain tests are delivered via TestNav, a Student Secure Browser app.\n\nMODEL Online Test Features Speaking Listening Writing Reading Computer Administered                                          Recorded Scripting Scored Locally Task Options ╫ ╫  Grades 1-5: Handwritten Response ╫  Grades 6-12: Typed Response\n\nThe WIDA Assessment System WIDA Screener (1-12) WIDA Screener for Kindergarten or WIDA MODEL for Kindergarten WIDA MODEL (K-12) WIDA ACCESS for ELLs (K-12) Alternate ACCESS for ELLs (1-12) A flexible, on-demand language proficiency assessment that  is part of WIDA’s comprehensive assessment system\n\nWIDA MODEL  Scores &amp; Reports\n\nStudent Response Score Sheet 21\n\nMODEL Paper: Score  Reports   Access student reports and data: Individual Student Report\n\nMODEL Online: Score Reports Individual Student Report  Available for download in 11 languages School &amp; District Roster Reports\n\nMODEL Online: Performance Dashboard The Performance Dashboard in ADAM offers a summary view of how a group of students is performing.  It provides aggregate scale score and proficiency level information for schools and districts at the domain and composite level.  Within the dashboard you can see:  Average Scale Scores  - average overall composite scale scores and average domain scale scores for each grade-level cluster are displayed for a school or district  Proficiency Level Frequency -  view the number and percentage of students (per grade-level cluster) who scored at each proficiency level  ©️2024 Board of Regents of the University of Wisconsin System\n\nMonitoring Progress &amp; Activity Reports Allows Account Administrators and District Administrators to  monitor student testing progress to ensure anticipated completion rates ©️2024 Board of Regents of the University of Wisconsin System\n\nWIDA MODEL Interpretive Guide",
