    "id": "fb5e8b7f-9a62-4af0-bebf-56a1b179beb3",
    "title": "Mock Example.docx (Part 1/2)",
    "content": "WCEPS Pathways Decision Guide for Educators Helping You Find the Right Program, Resource, or Partnership for Your Goals Navigating This Guide This guide helps educators and leaders identify which WCEPS program or pathway best supports their professional goals. Use the guiding questions under each section to reflect on your needs and follow the pathways that align best. You can explore by clicking on the section tabs (if in digital format) or scrolling through each focus area below. Section 1: Start with What You’re Looking For What are you hoping to accomplish through your professional learning? If you’re looking for... Start Here To deepen understanding of how rigor, relevance, and depth of knowledge connect to instruction and assessment DOK WebAlign To strengthen student talk and academic discourse for engagement and comprehension The Discussion Project To enhance multilingual learner instruction and align with WIDA frameworks WIDA Licensed Offerings / Planning with Purpose To engage teachers in examining authentic student work to improve instruction AIW (Authentic Intellectual Work) To build strong instructional coaching practices and educator collaboration Coaching for Impact To evaluate and strengthen leadership and school-wide systems CALL (Comprehensive Assessment of Leadership for Learning) Section 2: Guiding Questions by Focus Area Depth of Knowledge (DOK) and Alignment Looking for: Tools and frameworks to connect standards, instruction, and assessment through cognitive rigor. Ask Yourself: ● How do I know if my assessments and tasks align with the cognitive demands of my standards? ● Are students being challenged to think critically and apply knowledge in complex ways? Recommended Resource: DOK WebAlign Ideal For: Curriculum teams, instructional coaches, assessment leads Academic Discussion & Classroom Talk Looking for: Strategies to improve student participation, reasoning, and discourse. Ask Yourself: ● How can I help students use discussion to think deeply and learn collaboratively? ● Do all students have opportunities to share ideas and evidence in class? Recommended Resource: The Discussion Project Ideal For: Classroom teachers (grades 6–12), PD leaders, and teams focusing on engagement Supporting Multilingual Learners (WIDA Focus) Looking for: Professional learning that integrates WIDA principles into lesson planning, assessment, and instruction. Ask Yourself: ● Am I intentionally supporting language development within my content lessons? ● How can I use WIDA tools to make my teaching more equitable and inclusive? Recommended Resource: WIDA Licensed Offerings & Planning with Purpose Pathway Ideal For: K–12 teachers, ESL specialists, instructional coaches Analyzing and Elevating Student Work Looking for: A structured process for examining student work to promote authentic, equitable learning experiences. Ask Yourself: ● Are students producing work that shows deep understanding, critical thinking, and real-world application? ● How can collaboration around student work improve teaching quality? Recommended Resource: AIW (Authentic Intellectual Work) Ideal For: Instructional teams, PLCs, and school leaders Coaching and Professional Collaboration Looking for: Frameworks and strategies to build effective coaching systems and sustain professional learning communities. Ask Yourself: ● How can I create trust-based, reflective coaching conversations? ● How can our team sustain growth beyond a single PD session? Recommended Resource: Coaching for Impact Ideal For: Instructional coaches, mentors, administrators Leadership and School Systems Looking for: Tools to assess and strengthen leadership practices and school systems for learning. Ask Yourself: ● How do our leadership structures support teaching and learning? ● What evidence do we have of distributed leadership and teacher voice? Recommended Resource: CALL (Comprehensive Assessment of Leadership for Learning) Ideal For: District and school leaders, leadership teams Section 3: Quick Reference Matrix Focus Area Program/Pathway Ideal Audience Key Outcomes Format Instructional rigor & alignment DOK WebAlign Curriculum & assessment teams Ensure cognitive rigor alignment Workshop / Online Academic discussion The Discussion Project Teachers (6–12), PD leaders Strengthen talk for learning Multi-session course Multilingual learner support WIDA Licensed Offerings / Planning with Purpose K–12 educators Integrate WIDA frameworks Blended / Online Authentic student work AIW PLCs, school teams Improve rigor through collaboration Cohort model Coaching & collaboration Coaching for Impact Coaches, mentors Build sustainable coaching systems Series / Coaching model Leadership for learning CALL School & district leaders Assess and improve leadership capacity Diagnostic + Coaching Section 4: Implementation Support ● Use this guide in professional learning communities or leadership retreats. ● Combine multiple pathways (e.g., DOK WebAlign + AIW) for integrated improveme",
