    "content": "nd mainstream teachers will engage in regular collaboration and planning sessions to align instructional strategies and support ELLs' language and content learning. ● Teachers will share effective practices and resources related to ELL instruction to enhance professional growth and knowledge. Educators will demonstrate the use of ongoing assessment and progress monitoring to inform instruction. ● Teachers will use formative assessments to gauge ELLs' progress and adjust instruction accordingly. ● Teachers will use language proficiency assessments and data to track individual ELLs' language development and growth over time Full integration check-ins. Complete classroom observations, create surveys, needs assessments, and ongoing conversations to ensure implementation success. Phase 1: Year 2 Re-administer WIDA SIS or CCNA (# schools) Year Two: Following completion of the WIDA SIS or CCNA needs assessment survey, leadership teams from each school will engage in a Data Retreat facilitated by WCEPS CARE Coaches. In these sessions, the teams will explore and analyze their action-oriented WIDA SIS/CCNA data as well as additional data sources as a means of corroboration. During these sessions, school leadership teams will work collaboratively to target specific areas for improvement and professional growth and develop action steps for change initiatives. These sessions will take place annually following the completion of the full needs assessment survey. Each year, school leadership teams will have the opportunity to examine shifts in the data over time, which will further inform their planning efforts. In Phase 2, the Data Debrief Sessions will focus on changes in data from Phase 2. School leadership teams will determine which areas are still strengths and which still present opportunities for improvement. DATES: Leadership Team Data Retreat 20** Dates TBD Phase 2: WIDA SIS/CCNA Data Retreat (# school leadership teams) Following the implementation of WIDA SIS/CCNA in participating schools, leadership teams from each school will engage in WIDA SIS or CCNA Data Debrief sessions facilitated by WCEPS CARE Coaches. In these sessions, the teams will explore and analyze their action oriented WIDA SIS data, target specific areas for improvement and professional growth, and develop action steps for change initiatives. The Data Debrief sessions will take place each year following a full WIDA SIS implementation. Each year, the teams will have the opportunity to examine changes in WIDA SIS/CCNA data over time, which will further inform their planning efforts. ● Leadership Team Data Retreat- 20** Dates TBD Phase 3: Professional Development (from WIDA SIS data and other data collected during action planning) Effective Tier 1 Professional Development (PD) for English language learners (ELLs) refers to professional development programs and strategies aimed at equipping teachers with the knowledge and skills to effectively support ELLs in the mainstream classroom. This type of PD focuses on building educators' understanding of language acquisition, cultural responsiveness, and instructional strategies that promote language development and academic achievement for ELLs. Using data-driven action plan priorities, WCEPS will support school/district areas of need by providing PD specific to the areas specified in the data. Knowing that there are some foundational concepts that are necessary to provide a solid foundation for educator success, we are listing topics that may be adjusted based on action plan, educator surveys, and additional data points. By following these steps, using action plans can effectively guide professional development and ensure that it is purposeful, targeted, and responsive to the specific needs of educators Full PD days TBD by **/** School Calendar Potential Areas of Focus: Maintaining a School-Wide Focus on English Learner Success through Collaboration This session explores components of a collaborative culture that support partnerships across the school community. Promoting Equity through Reflective Professional Practice: Data-Driven Instructional Practices To maintain a school-wide focus on English learner success, school leaders need to create structured opportunities for teachers to examine their practice and its effect on student achievement. Classroom-based action research promotes equity through reflective pedagogical practice designed to improve teaching and learning. This session enables teachers to engage in purposeful reflection to identify changes that will promote growth that will positively impact outcomes for English learners. Additional PD Days TBD by **/** School Calendar Focus Topics: Follow up to each of the topics noted above, with a reflection session and culminating event that mirrors year 1. Learning walks/Observations with leadership teams- Cost not noted, based on number of classrooms and times per year. Cost for Year # TBD Based on menu of options Service Unit Costs Costs for Year #",
