    "title": "3-year Implementation NC Proposal.docx (Part 3/5)",
    "content": "which will further inform their planning efforts. ● Leadership Team Data Retreat- 20** Dates TBD Phase 3: Professional Development (from WIDA SIS data and other data collected during action planning) Effective Tier 1 Professional Development (PD) for English language learners (ELLs) refers to professional development programs and strategies aimed at equipping teachers with the knowledge and skills to effectively support ELLs in the mainstream classroom. This type of PD focuses on building educators' understanding of language acquisition, cultural responsiveness, and instructional strategies that promote language development and academic achievement for ELLs. Using data-driven action plan priorities, WCEPS will support school/district areas of need by providing PD specific to the areas specified in the data. Knowing that there are some foundational concepts that are necessary to provide a solid foundation for educator success, we are listing topics that may be adjusted based on action plan, educator surveys, and additional data points. By following these steps, using action plans can effectively guide professional development and ensure that it is purposeful, targeted, and responsive to the specific needs of educators. Full PD days TBD By **/** School Calendar Potential Focus Topics: Exploring Reading: Understanding Learners and Language Transfer Reading is essential for language learning and cognitive development. This workshop explores reading processes, learner needs, and literacy transfer between languages. Through discussions and activities, educators will gain strategies to support learners in developing reading skills in an additional language. Formative Assessment Practices to Promote Content Learning and Language Development Effective classroom-based formative assessments practices enable teachers to gauge student growth toward mastery based on learning goals and success criteria, which students can also use to monitor their progress and self-assess. The model of formative assessment used in this session is particularly effective for English learners since they often enter the classroom environment at various educational backgrounds and proficiency levels. Practical Approaches to Supporting English learners in Content Classrooms: Content specific (Science, Math, ELA, S.S., Electives) This interactive session offers participants approaches to combining English language development standards and disciplinary practices. Participants develop a common understanding of academic language expectations in content areas and explore strategies to foster a language-rich environment. Through hands-on experiments and analysis of language embedded within the content and practices, participants will have a deeper understanding of how to engage language learners of a variety of proficiency levels Bridging Oracy and Literacy for English Learners An apprenticeship approach to writing instruction known as the Teaching and Learning Cycle provides the foundation for this session. It is a framework designed to scaffold academic writing instruction through interactive reading, academic discussions, and language development. It can be adapted to different grade levels and content areas, enabling English learners to become effective and informed writers across the curriculum. Additional PD Days TBD By **/** School Calendar Focus Topics: Follow up to each of the topics noted above, with a reflection session and culminating event that mirrors year 1. Cost for Year #2: TBD Based on menu of options Service Unit Costs Costs for Year #1 Notes Year #3: Putting Tier 1 Instruction into Action Dates TBD Year 3 Goal: Ensure educators have a framework for demonstrating three years of learning and progress in Tier 1 instruction for English language learners. The goals encompass various aspects of language development, content knowledge, instructional strategies, cultural responsiveness, collaboration, and assessment, ensuring comprehensive support for ELLs in the mainstream classroom. Educators will reflect on instructional shifts and discuss challenges, successes and next steps for continued growth Year 3 Goal: General Description of Work: Educators will demonstrate effective instructional strategies for ELLs in the mainstream classroom. Demonstrated by: ● Differentiated instruction by providing ELLs with appropriate scaffolds, supports, and modified materials to access grade-level content. ● The use of explicit language instruction and modeling to develop ELLs' language skills in context. ● The use of visual aids, graphic organizers, and other visual supports to enhance understanding and comprehension for ELLs. Educators will demonstrate collaboration and communication between ESL/ELL teachers and mainstream classroom teachers. ● ESL/ELL and mainstream teachers will engage in regular collaboration and planning sessions to align instructional strategies and support ELLs' language and content learning. ● Teachers will share effective pra",
