    "title": "3-year Implementation NC Proposal.docx (Part 2/5)",
    "content": "lowing these steps, using action plans can effectively guide professional development and ensure that it is purposeful, targeted, and responsive to the specific needs of educators Full or half PD days Date Focus: Building Capacity to Bridge Content Learning and Language Development This session will support educators in exploring connections between grade-level content standards and language development standards. Participants will examine state content standards and make connections to language expectations. Educators will consider how to provide equity and access through a functional approach to language learning. Date Focus: Applying the Framework to Instructional Planning Participants build on their understanding of the components of an English language development framework, using an instructional planning template with guiding questions. They connect key language uses to culminating tasks and prioritize language functions and features to scaffold instruction. Extension PD day Tbd Focus: Follow up geared by survey results and teacher voice (Potential topic: Language Charts) Cost for Year #1:TBD Based on menu of options Service Unit Costs Costs for Year #1 Notes Year #2: Continued Focus on Tier 1 Instruction to Support Multilingual Learners Dates TBD Year 2 Goal: Implementation of instructional shifts that address the needs of language learners as they engage in Tier 1 instruction and language development. General Description of Work: 1. Scaffolded Support: Use scaffolding techniques to gradually build students' language skills and knowledge with a focus on Tier 1. Break down complex concepts and tasks into smaller, manageable steps, and provide ample support and guidance throughout the learning process. 2. Assessment and Feedback: Regularly assess students' language proficiency using formative and summative assessment tools. Provide constructive feedback that focuses on both strengths and areas for improvement, guiding students towards continuous growth. 3. Collaboration with Colleagues: Collaborate with other teachers, ESL specialists, and support staff to share strategies, resources, and insights related to working with English language learners. Engage in professional development opportunities to enhance my knowledge and skills in ESL instruction. 4. Parent and Community Involvement: Foster strong partnerships with parents and the local community to support English language learners outside the classroom. Communicate regularly with parents, provide resources for continued language development at home, and engage community members as cultural ambassadors or guest speakers 5. Differentiated Instruction: Differentiate Tier 1 instruction to address the varied learning styles, interests, and abilities of English language learners. Provide opportunities for collaborative learning, small-group activities, and one-on-one support to ensure all students can actively participate and progress. Phase 1: Year 2 Re-administer WIDA SIS or CCNA(# schools) Year Two:. Each year, schools will administer the full version of the WIDA SIS/CCNA survey. In between these full survey administrations, schools will have the opportunity to create custom, shorter surveys that contain specific items of their choosing targeted at maintaining existing strengths or improving areas of need. These “Quick CALL” surveys allow school leaders to monitor progress efficiently and to determine if changes need to be made in real-time.. ● Upon completion of the survey, users receive immediate targeted data and feedback designed to support school improvement and professional growth focused on teaching and supporting ELs. Each year, the schools will administer the full version of the WIDA SIS/CCNA survey. In between these full survey administrations, schools will have the opportunity to create custom, shorter surveys that contain specific items of their choosing targeted for improvement or maintaining strength. These “Quick CALL” surveys allow school leaders to monitor progress efficiently and to determine if changes need to be made in real time. ○ Provide survey to staff beginning of school year date: TBD Phase 2: WIDA SIS or CCNA Data Retreat (school leadership teams) Following the implementation of WIDA SIS/CCNA in participating schools, leadership teams from each school will engage in WIDA SIS or CCNA Data Debrief sessions facilitated by WCEPS CARE Coaches. In these sessions, the teams will explore and analyze their action oriented WIDA SIS data, target specific areas for improvement and professional growth, and develop action steps for change initiatives. The Data Debrief sessions will take place each year following a full WIDA SIS/CCNA implementation. Each year, the teams will have the opportunity to examine changes in WIDA SIS data over time, which will further inform their planning efforts. ● Leadership Team Data Retreat- 20** Dates TBD Phase 3: Professional Development (from WIDA SIS data and other data collected during action planning)",
