    "id": "dcb91c59-9dbc-4b9e-b0a6-9c697305e273",
    "title": "3-year Implementation NC Proposal.docx (Part 1/5)",
    "content": "*District* Collaboration with Wisconsin Center for Education Products & Services (WCEPS) to Serve Multilingual Learners Three-Year Collaboration: Start and End Dates Building on and Evolving With District’s Prior Work Objective: At the end of this three-year collaboration ** District will have an enhanced ability to ensure all students receive effective Tier 1 Instruction and have deep engagement in grade-appropriate assignments. This collaboration will build upon the prior work of Bensenville district to ensure a coherent and additive experience for all Bensenville district educators. Year #1: Building A Focus on Tier 1 Instruction to Support Multilingual Learners August 20** to July 20** Year 1 Goal: Ensure understanding among specialists and leaders of foundational concepts for educators to support English language learners at a Tier 1 level that will guide content understanding alongside language development General Description of Work: 1. Use data to inform areas of needs as well as collecting data that will guide direction of future professional development by honoring teacher voice and targeted action steps to meet those needs. 2. Enhance Language Proficiency: Improve proficiency in Tier 1 English language,with a focus on building capacity and applying the framework PD. 3. Change management support: District-wide consulting and check-ins for implementation plan, vision, and playbook development. Phase 1: Administer WIDA SIS or CCNA (# schools) WIDA School Improvement System -WIDA SIS is an online, school-wide leadership assessment that focuses on practices supporting the instruction of English Learners (ELs). Developed in collaboration with the CALL system from the University of Wisconsin– Madison, it uses a multi-source survey completed by teachers, administrators, and support staff to measure distributed leadership practices that influence EL teaching and learning. Care Coaching Needs Assessment (CCNA) -The Care Coaching Needs Assessment identifies an individual’s strengths, challenges, and support needs related to well-being and performance. Through structured questions or surveys, it helps care coaches understand key areas for growth and create personalized coaching plans that connect individuals with the right resources and strategies. ● Upon completion of the survey, users receive immediate targeted data and feedback designed to support school improvement and professional growth focused on teaching and supporting ELs. Each year, the schools will administer the full version of the WIDA SIS survey. In between these full survey administrations, schools will have the opportunity to create custom, shorter surveys that contain specific items of their choosing targeted for improvement or maintaining strength. These “Quick CALL” surveys allow school leaders to monitor progress efficiently and to determine if changes need to be made in real time. ○ Provide survey to staff beginning of school year date: TBD Phase 2: WIDA SIS or CCNA Data Retreat (# school leadership teams) Following the implementation of WIDA SIS/CCNA in participating schools, leadership teams from each school will engage in WIDA SIS or CCNA Data Debrief sessions facilitated by WCEPS CARE Coaches. In these sessions, the teams will explore and analyze their action oriented WIDA SIS data as well as analyze and make connections with other data sources. In these data analysis processes, the teams will work to target specific areas for improvement and professional growth and develop action steps for change initiatives. The Data Debrief sessions will take place each year following a full WIDA SIS/CCNA implementation. Each year, the teams will have the opportunity to examine changes in WIDA SIS/CCNA data over time, which will further inform their planning efforts. ● Leadership Team Data Retreat- Date Professional Development (from WIDA SIS data and other data collected during action planning and consulting) Effective Tier 1 Professional Development (PD) for English language learners (ELLs) refers to professional development programs and strategies aimed at equipping teachers with the knowledge and skills to effectively support ELLs in the mainstream classroom. This type of PD focuses on building educators' understanding of language acquisition, cultural responsiveness, and instructional strategies that promote language development and academic achievement for ELLs. Using data-driven action plan priorities, WCEPS will support school/district areas of need by providing PD specific to the areas specified in the data. Knowing that there are some foundational concepts that are necessary to provide a solid foundation for educator success, we are listing topics that may be adjusted based on action plan, educator surveys, and additional data points. By following these steps, using action plans can effectively guide professional development and ensure that it is purposeful, targeted, and responsive to the specific needs of educators Full or half PD days",
