    "content": "Pathways to Transformation The Pathways to Proficiency model aims to collaborate with districts to make systemic improvements in the educational experience of Multilingual Learners. Using research-informed and practice-proven methods, WCEPS guides districts through the pathway to change. Pathway 1 - Envision a Pathway to Success \"Through envisioning a pathway to success, teachers unite under a common goal, setting the foundation for impactful change.\" Goal Setting Planning Implementation Evaluation Outcome Initial goal meeting (Workshops and strategic planning sessions focused on creating and aligning a shared vision of instructional excellence) Design content for delivery of initial training to staff based on need/topic. Support creating conditions for success with administrators, coaches, or grade level chair Present the LEA topic to the selected audience. Three months 1-hour virtual follow-up – w/LEA or educators Plan for opportunities to reflect on mindshifts that support a vision, communication and cultural shift. Credit courses will require office hours to follow up on assignments. WCEPS administers a success metric tool- Qualtrics Survey ● Pre and Post WCEPS reviews survey results w/LEA ● Discuss next steps ● Determine priorities Schools develop a shared understanding, aligning all educators to a common purpose. Collect qualitative data and testimonials. For teachers, shared survey results will show increased knowledge in the targeted area. For administrators, survey results will show increased knowledge for observing effective practices in the target area. (If admin participates) ● Admin may use a shared Qualtrics learning walk tool to capture concepts from the session. For school districts, teachers will have a common understanding of the topic. Add-ons: Curriculum, State Standard, and Assessment Alignments (DOK, MLL) Add-ons: Needs Assessments Tool Add-ons: WCEPS Badges* Add-ons: Coaching, 1 to 3-year Plans Pathway 2 - Equip a Pathway to Readiness \"Equipping a pathway to readiness ensures that educators feel prepared and capable of navigating instructional shifts.\" Initial Goal Setting Planning Implementation & Follow-up Evaluation & Innovation Outcomes Initial goal meeting Schedule a follow-up meeting on the process. (Workshops and strategic planning sessions focused on creating and aligning a shared vision of instructional excellence) Design content for initial training delivery to staff based on need/topic. WCEPS or LEA plans for learning walks using the content tool. WCEPS creates a canvas course to collaborate with w/LEA (data, feedback, information) Support creating conditions for success with administrators, coaches, or grade level chair Present the LEA topic to the selected audience. Targeted professional learning opportunities to build teacher and leader skills, such as content-specific workshops, coaching, or model lesson demonstrations. Three months 1-hour virtual follow-up – w/LEA or educators Perform learning walks Analyze data from learning walks to measure progress. Plan for opportunities to reflect on mindshifts that support a vision, communication and cultural shift. Credit courses will require office hours to follow up on assignments. WCEPS administers a success metric tool- Qualtrics Survey ● Pre and Post ● Learning Walk data WCEPS reviews survey results w/LEA ● Discuss next steps ● Determine priorities Teachers and leaders are equipped with professional development, resources, and strategies to implement changes effectively. Collect qualitative data and testimonials. For teachers, survey results will show increased knowledge and skills in the targeted area. For administrators, survey results will show increased knowledge and skills in observing effective practices in the target area. ● Shared Qualtrics learning walk tool to capture concepts from the session For school districts, learning walk data will show an increased use of target skills in classrooms. Add-ons: Curriculum, State Standard, and Assessment Alignments (DOK, MLL) Add-ons: Needs Assessments Tool Add-ons: WCEPS Badges* Add-ons: Coaching, 1 to 3-year Plans Pathway 3 - Empower a Pathway to Sustainability \"Empowering a pathway to sustainability enables schools to build lasting momentum and a culture of continuous improvement.\" Initial Goal Setting Planning Implementation & Follow-up Evaluation & Innovation Outcome Initial goal meeting Schedule preparation of district-level leadership team (Workshops and strategic planning sessions focused on creating and aligning a shared vision of instructional excellence) Discuss the 3-year proposal and implementation. Conduct a needs assessment. Content for delivery of initial training to staff based on need/topic. WCEPS or LEA plans for learning walks using the content tool. WCEPS creates a canvas course to collaborate with w/LEA (data, feedback, information) Schedule initial training for staff based on the leadership action plan. Plan for coaching check-in with the leadership tea",
