    "content": "File: mm25_chunk_05.mp4\nTitle: mm25_chunk_05\nTags: multimodal workshop good content\n\nContent: us an idea of how scaffolding for multilingual learners is not just the teacher role. Yeah. Well, I've got one more picture for you, also made by ChatGPT, that kind of fits the other component of, or the last component of Vygotsky's framework. What do you think this image has to do with learning that has to do with scaffolding? It all starts in the home, background connection. Ashley said, I think it goes back to community. Involving parents. So I thought it was a little bit different. I'm glad it puts society and culture up there. But so society, the idea is that society and culture influence the attitudes and beliefs that influence the attitudes and beliefs of a student towards learning and education. So creating relationships provides a safe learning environment, and using language is the primary tool, including this transfer of sociocultural influences. So we have to look at where the students are coming from, their beliefs, and really tap into those things. Oh, and the chat's going back. I wanted to reference, oh, the chat moves so fast. Somebody said, we bring our culture and background with us to our learning. We don't get to engage in this conversation in this one-hour webinar, but this is where translanguaging comes in, because and not just translanguaging in regards to those that speak another language at home, even our English-speaking students, when they speak differently at home, how important\n",
