    "id": "c75d967b-fcff-4dae-9ddd-6314fe19b4cc",
    "title": "mm25_chunk_04",
    "content": "File: mm25_chunk_04.mp4\nTitle: mm25_chunk_04\nTags: multimodal workshop good content\n\nContent: I think what we're getting at was interaction, okay? So learning occurs through, it's a social process. It's something that happens with meaningful interactions with others, and the teacher is central to learning. And that language is a primary tool used in the development of learning. You know, so that part really stuck out to me, you know, when I dug deeper into this was that language is the primary tool used in the development of learning. And so everybody in that classroom is learning language and we have to use it. And then take that and think about, you know, how often are kids talking with each other in the classroom versus teacher talk? You know, if the kids aren't talking, the kids aren't learning. I just emphasize more started coming in the chat and I was really excited because you mentioned something that Leslie wrote. And Leslie, I just sent you a link to the first Amazon gift card. She wrote community learning. And I don't think I've heard that in a very long time when we're talking about scaffolding because that image is community learning. And there's others learning from peers, not just instructor, which you just mentioned. Repeating is very helpful. Some students need teacher support to communicate orally. This shows that scaffolding doesn't mean teacher and student interaction. It must include interaction between students as well. Getting to know what you know so far. Students can process at the level that they're at and get assistance from teacher as needed. Sometimes students need more support. We will develop the language that we need if the students feel like they have a voice. Candice, you're getting an Amazon gift card. I mean, they're all great. I wish I could give you all Amazon gift cards and I'll try to be as Oprah as I can in this situation. But this is like just this thread of information gives.\n",
