    "id": "eb586869-6d92-468a-aecc-7417c2e3e01a",
    "title": "Bridging Content and Language: A Cohesive Approach to Multilingual Learner Success (Part 3/3)",
    "content": "STUDENT LEARNING OUTCOMES:\n\nUpon completion of this course, the student will be able to:\n\nApply UDL principles to develop instruction that differentiates the presentation of content, the meaning-making process, and the means of demonstrating learning.\n\nAddress learner readiness by designing scaffolded instruction that meets students at their English proficiency levels while promoting growth toward grade-level expectations.\n\nLeverage students' strengths, interests, and preferences to create engaging and personalized learning experiences that empower English learners to succeed.\n\nDesign classroom environments that are inclusive and responsive to the needs of English learners, ensuring equitable access to learning opportunities.\n\nIntegrate flexible supports that foster student autonomy and build confidence in using English as a tool for learning and communication.\n\nTITLE: Promoting Autonomy through Formative Assessment Practices\n\nCOURSE DESCRIPTION: This course equips educators with practical strategies to implement formative assessment practices that support the diverse needs of multilingual learners. Participants will learn how to design and use learning goals, learning intentions, and success indicators to clarify expectations for content learning and academic language use. They will also explore ways to engage students in meaningful tasks that promote understanding and language development while fostering a classroom culture where constructive feedback builds student agency.\n\nSTUDENT LEARNING OUTCOMES:\n\nBy the end of the course, participants will be able to:\n\nExplain the purpose and principles of formative assessment for multilingual learners.\n\nCreate clear learning goals that integrate content and language.\n\nDesign student-friendly success indicators aligned with learning intentions.\n\nDevelop tasks to gather evidence.\n\nDeliver feedback that promotes growth and agency.\n\nSupport student self-assessment and goal-setting.",
