    "title": "chunk_28",
    "content": "File: chunk_28.mp4\nTitle: chunk_28\n\nContent: Definitely hashtag validation is important. Yeah, for our kids and for us as adults. Hashtag honor our differences. Respect each other language is culture. Diversity. Oh, diversity, culture, language is universal. Wonderful. We have some people who are already logging off. I'm going to very quickly go through the four activities you picked up tonight. Keep them in your toolkit there at arm's length. I am monologues, which we had a couple of those hashtags. Go figure. Remembering the power of figurative language, idioms, sayings, poetry, all of that brings culture into your classroom. My life map, which you can adapt to any anything that comes to mind at the moment that you need your kids to share a little bit about. And then, of course, hanging hashtags, which could be just verify what are they bringing? What knowledge are they bringing with them? Maybe you want to use it as I did. Right. As a closing to an activity. Very adaptable as way as well. OK, I saw a lot of you say you love this topic. I love this topic, too. And WIDA 2020 is coming up. So I'm going to give a shout out to WIDA. WIDA is one of my favorite conferences because of the focus on language and the power of language and how we can continue to have fun with language and being so inclusive about the cultures behind our language. So I want to make sure to personally invite you to two sessions we have on language and culture at WIDA. So if you're going to WIDA, check it out. I know you have to pre-register for your sessions. October 16th, we have our very own education solutions team. They're going to be presenting our updated strategy.\n",
