    "title": "chunk_29",
    "content": "File: chunk_29.mp4\nTitle: chunk_29\n\nContent: homepages and show you how you can curate specific content to your teacher's needs. On October 18th we have Dr. Latoya Facey-Walker who will be giving a session about unlocking the power of Elevation Strategies and Forms. She's going to be joined by a district administrator who's going to give firsthand stories and data. How did Elevation support her work and what's changed with her multilingual learners, right? Why are her teachers feeling so empowered? So if you're at WIDA, check us out because we will be there. Some of you asked for the QR code for the MyLifeMap. I'll go back to that, but in the meantime, if you are interested, if you're on social media, we do have a Facebook community group. I'm actually jumping off of this and jumping into Facebook community group. I'm going to host a quick Q&A at the close of this event. And if you like podcasts and you try to walk every morning as I do, you may want to QR the podcast. I'm actually the host now of our podcast. We have 12 seasons before me with some incredible guests, including our friends at YSEP. So feel free to join us at any one of those podcasts. We just released a new episode yesterday. It's all about youth empowerment. You guys are going to love it. And so, as all of you are saying good night and buenas noches, just a quick reminder. Seeing our kids what they don't see in themselves. Thank you for all that you do. Thank you for embracing all of the assets our kids bring linguistically as well as culturally and realizing that language, that the language that they bring is not a barrier, that it's another asset that they bring.\n",
