    "id": "5f701369-c5f0-4a1c-b647-73b0d1247728",
    "title": "chunk_23",
    "content": "File: chunk_23.mp4\nTitle: chunk_23\n\nContent: I had cognates in three different languages. Imagine how powerful that is for our kids. So I'm gonna open it up and just ask, has anybody used my life map before? I've missed a lot in this chat. Wordless short videos, excellent. That's some good resource sharing going on here. Thank you. Okay, so I don't see that anybody's used my life map before. I'm gonna go ahead, not yet, I love it. Dana, making life easier for you. Go ahead and scan this QR code. You're gonna be able to read the full blog, kind of a recap of what I just spoke about. But the wonderful thing is you're also going to have the template for my life map with some ideas that you can use in a future lesson. And I'll just leave that up for a couple seconds. Senya, you asked for the- I'll add it to the chat. Thank you very much, because the bit leads there. I'm just gonna give you another second or so to take that. I wanna keep my eye on time. Okay, all right. Okay, so multilingual learners, and those of you who are bilingual or learning, my Duolingo fans, that you're constantly moving through languages, right? We think we live in two or more linguistic worlds, and sometimes we don't even know which world we're in. Oftentimes, and I'm sure it happens to others, I will be responding to someone in Spanish and realize when I see their face.\n",
