    "content": "File: chunk_02.mp4\nTitle: chunk_02\nTags: Video use new API\n\nContent: participant names or anything that you share here. The recording is for our purposes, and if something is shared, it would be from us as presenters. So, I'm an associate director for WISEPS, Wisconsin Center for Educational Products and Services. I'm the associate director of CARE Coaching, and welcome to our monthly Tips and Dips webinar. We share a variety of topics about effective instruction for multilingual learners. We are a nonprofit, and through our CARE Coaching team, we offer WIDA-licensed workshops, as well as customized workshops and job-embedded professional learning to support schools and help districts address equity, access, and effective instruction for multilingual learners. So, we have a guest today from Elevation, one of our partners. Her name is Sandra Medrano Arroyo, and she's the national director of multilingual learner success. So, our topic today, she's going to talk about the role of language in fostering cross-cultural understandings and collaboration, and we're excited to have you all here today to engage in this discussion and help us all learn more about harnessing the power of language, celebrate students' cultural assets, and develop language and literacy skills. So, welcome everyone again. I will go ahead and turn the presentation over to Sandra. Hi, everyone. Thank you, Margie, and thank you, Amy, and thank you, everyone at WISENPS for this invitation. Welcome. Bienvenidos a todos. Thank you all for taking time out of your incredibly busy schedule to spend the evening with us. I truly appreciate it, and I know that everyone on the team does as well. We're going to get started today. Hmm, here we go. Hmm, here we go.\n",
