ormation, the chat, the slides, the certificate, and any resources that you all shared.\r\n\r\n579\r\n01:06:09.910 --> 01:06:15.280\r\nMargie Marrero: I think they might have also needed if those who are still here don't mind just a minute for the survey.\r\n\r\n580\r\n01:06:15.760 --> 01:06:17.319\r\nMargie Marrero: I couldn't get something.\r\n\r\n581\r\n01:06:17.320 --> 01:06:30.600\r\nYvonne Williams: The the survey helps us decide next topics. So if you wouldn't mind, it's a quick survey, it's it's not. Gonna take you a lot very long, and then we already trans languaging and scaffolding. But it'll help us to have also the survey.\r\n\r\n582\r\n01:06:30.890 --> 01:06:35.229\r\nMargie Marrero: Yes, okay. I'll get it in the chat here in just a second. It didn't come.\r\n\r\n583\r\n01:06:35.230 --> 01:06:38.820\r\nYvonne Williams: While we're waiting. How about sheltered instruction classes, Amy?\r\n\r\n584\r\n01:06:40.480 --> 01:06:43.330\r\nYvonne Williams: How about sheltered instruction classes?\r\n\r\n585\r\n01:06:44.616 --> 01:07:06.860\r\nAmy King: I think sheltered instruction classes are are great. I think it's a good opportunity for for newcomers to feel more successful. But I also think that to Yvonne's point earlier anytime, we can get students into mainstream classrooms, mainstream classrooms with their English proficient peers, I think the better.\r\n\r\n586\r\n01:07:09.310 --> 01:07:10.020\r\nAmy King: Yeah.\r\n\r\n587\r\n01:07:10.020 --> 01:07:16.839\r\nTanya Harmon: We're actually trying sheltered instruction in our district as well. I mean, mostly in our in our school, where.\r\n\r\n588\r\n01:07:16.850 --> 01:07:35.269\r\nTanya Harmon: or ell or Ml, I should say, population is growing significantly. So we kind of started that project this year, and all the administrators had about 3 or 4 different workshops. I'm talking about instruction. And we also had some of our Ml. Teachers\r\n\r\n589\r\n01:07:35.580 --> 01:07:41.499\r\nTanya Harmon: view those videos as well, and they have been presenting them doing our monthly pld to the staff.\r\n\r\n590\r\n01:07:41.730 --> 01:07:46.820\r\nTanya Harmon: So we're also trying to, you know, integrate that in our Ml. Classes as well.\r\n\r\n591\r\n01:07:47.100 --> 01:08:06.519\r\nAmy King: I also would just add to that, as a you know, like what what someone calls sheltered instruction class may be different than what somebody else calls it, too. I think the one thing, especially at the high school level, is whether or not you've got a dual, dually certified teacher, so that the students are getting credit for a content class\r\n\r\n592\r\n01:08:07.700 --> 01:08:09.970\r\nAmy King: delivered in a sheltered context.\r\n\r\n593\r\n01:08:11.140 --> 01:08:12.870\r\nYvonne Williams: Don? Did you have a question?\r\n\r\n594\r\n01:08:21.490 --> 01:08:22.180\r\nYvonne Williams: Good.\r\n\r\n595\r\n01:08:22.460 --> 01:08:23.200\r\nFawn Straus: That's our.\r\n\r\n596\r\n01:08:23.700 --> 01:08:39.699\r\nFawn Straus: I'm in my car. So I work at a dual language immersion school, and I am the ell teacher right now as well as the biliteracy coordinator as well as an English language arts teacher. Because we're very understaffed, currently.\r\n\r\n597\r\n01:08:40.960 --> 01:08:43.660\r\nFawn Straus: and I'm trying to\r\n\r\n598\r\n01:08:43.910 --> 01:09:00.380\r\nFawn Straus: help a lot of my teachers, because we have 15 newcomers right now to our district. Not district just to our grade levels right now. Sorry and a lot of them are struggling with how to get the content and make it approachable to their students in\r\n\r\n599\r\n01:09:00.430 --> 01:09:08.010\r\nFawn Straus: like a math class or a science class, when so many of the resources have been moved to a digital format.\r\n\r\n600\r\n01:09:08.621 --> 01:09:11.269\r\nFawn Straus: That offers no sort of like\r\n\r\n601\r\n01:09:11.810 --> 01:09:17.370\r\nFawn Straus: wiggle room for like adding in a lot of that Tpr stuff like that.\r\n\r\n602\r\n01:09:17.510 --> 01:09:30.420\r\nFawn Straus: and I was wondering if you have any suggestions on how I can best help these teachers in the classroom when cause we just. We don't have the Yale staff to be able to go in and help\r\n\r\n603\r\n01:09:30.430 --> 01:09:34.869\r\nFawn Straus: show our newer teachers how to help their students the best.\r\n\r\n604\r\n01:09:38.660 --> 01:09:40.860\r\nFawn Straus: I don't know if any of that made any sense.\r\n\r\n605\r\n01:09:41.130 --> 01:09:45.220\r\nYvonne Williams: It did. Sorry I'm trying to answer, but I'm in a coughing fit.\r\n\r\n606\r\n01:09:45.229 --> 01:09:48.960\r\nYvonne Williams: so just give me a few minutes, and I'll see if Margie and Amy have anything to add.\r\n\r\n607\r\n01:09:49.840 --> 01:09:50.889\r\nFawn Straus: Thank you.\r\n\r\n608\r\n01:09:53.830 --> 01:10:02.340\r\nyolanda chavez: I'm thinking about my at the high school. Everything is digital also, and in English.\r\n\r\n609\r\n01:10:02.480 --> 01:10:08.009\r\nyolanda chavez: And I have a handful like half a dozen monolinguals new numbers.\r\n\r\n610\r\n01:10:08.240 --> 01:10:12.869\r\nyolanda chavez: and the teachers have been sharing the lesson with me. Might be a Pdf.\r\n\r\n611\r\n01:10:13.040 --> 01:10:22.129\r\nyolanda chavez: And then I I'm translating it. I'm trying to translate it, using Google, translate where you can upload a document.\r\n\r\n612\r\n01:10:22.630 --> 01:10:34.259\r\nyolanda chavez: And in many instances, as long as it's not a big file, it'll just translate it, not a hundred percent. I try to look at it real quick, since I am buying people and kind of fix any\r\n\r\n613\r\n01:10:34.360 --> 01:10:38.599\r\nyolanda chavez: errors, but I feel like it's better than nothing.\r\n\r\n614\r\n01:10:38.820 --> 01:10:43.320\r\nyolanda chavez: Also I teach the kids how to use the Google translate\r\n\r\n615\r\n01:10:43.400 --> 01:10:47.420\r\nyolanda chavez: feature audio feature. So it has like a microphone.\r\n\r\n616\r\n01:10:47.630 --> 01:10:57.280\r\nyolanda chavez: And they could set it from English to their language, and then they can capture what the teacher saying and be reading what the teacher saying\r\n\r\n617\r\n01:10:57.730 --> 01:11:08.560\r\nyolanda chavez: to try to get an idea, at least get an idea of what's happening last and and empower them to and take that ownership where they're\r\n\r\n618\r\n01:11:08.830 --> 01:11:19.490\r\nyolanda chavez: turning on their computer. They're turning on the Google translate as soon as they get into class, so that they know what's happening, because I'm only one person also, and I have a big caseload.\r\n\r\n619\r\n01:11:20.260 --> 01:11:23.410\r\nyolanda chavez: So I'm trying to teach the kids how to do that.\r\n\r\n620\r\n01:11:24.003 --> 01:11:24.390\r\nYvonne Williams: That thing.\r\n\r\n621\r\n01:11:24.390 --> 01:11:30.629\r\nyolanda chavez: And little by little I'm trying to teach them how to translate. Also, because I can't do everything for them.\r\n\r\n622\r\n01:11:30.630 --> 01:11:31.190\r\nYvonne Williams: Just one.\r\n\r\n623\r\n01:11:31.190 --> 01:11:35.980\r\nyolanda chavez: Person, and then empowering them that way. So I hope that helps.\r\n\r\n624\r\n01:11:35.980 --> 01:11:41.630\r\nYvonne Williams: Yeah, thanks, Yolanda. There are, I think, the the most important will be number one.\r\n\r\n625\r\n01:11:42.170 --> 01:11:46.819\r\nYvonne Williams: We hear it often when teachers get students that are in the newcomer stage.\r\n\r\n626\r\n01:11:47.550 --> 01:12:09.349\r\nYvonne Williams: and brain research is on our side. That they will be fine, that they will overcome. Just the fact that they're worried is enough to say that they are developing a strong relationship with the students. Now that's not practical. So for the practical piece, we need to engage the students in self regulated learning. What does that mean? If you translate a document, or if you're giving them the\r\n\r\n627\r\n01:12:09.350 --> 01:12:25.520\r\nYvonne Williams: syllabus of the week as a preview review, we need to ask them, what did you need to understand? How do you need to work through this content? Is it with a group? Do you need additional supports. Do you need more time? We need to start asking students what they need.\r\n\r\n628\r\n01:12:25.520 --> 01:12:43.459\r\nYvonne Williams: And if you need to translate that kind of information where you're setting the foundation of how they're gonna learn. So then in the class, they can say Miss Williams, and they could just pull out a note card. We talked about this creating like note cards that say I need a partner, or I need clarification, and it's in English and in the back. It's in their home language.\r\n\r\n629\r\n01:12:43.460 --> 01:12:56.920\r\nYvonne Williams: so that they're saying what they need in the moment that they're in class. But the idea of translating and give it to them before will help them engage in the moment of the classroom, and then we need to have scaffolds there, and that's where scaffolds\r\n\r\n630\r\n01:12:57.430 --> 01:13:09.350\r\nYvonne Williams: are the key in this conversation for newcomers, and we have an entire workshop on it, so we'll try to condense it into the hour, tip and dip for the next one, after translanguaging, so that you have it\r\n\r\n631\r\n01:13:09.410 --> 01:13:15.730\r\nYvonne Williams: not say you need to use lesson plan. They give a lot of resources on how to embed. Oh, the psyop! Yes, thank you, Sophia.\r\n\r\n632\r\n01:13:16.000 --> 01:13:19.980\r\nYvonne Williams: and so I just wanted to answer that question on\r\n\r\n633\r\n01:13:20.300 --> 01:13:27.919\r\nYvonne Williams: how to take back to the teachers. Maybe the slides that we're gonna share will help you with some resources and the ones that I've shared here.\r\n\r\n634\r\n01:13:28.080 --> 01:13:45.839\r\nYvonne Williams: but really be intentional and telling them to create a a system where they're understanding in their home language, and then coming to class to hear the English with a partner, with support, with whatever we can do to help them engage and feel safe as they're learning and acquiring English.\r\n\r\n635\r\n01:13:47.110 --> 01:13:57.539\r\nAmy King: I also think engaging in conversations with your colleagues about. If you had to choose 3 things that you want students to know or be able to do from this particular unit. What would that be?\r\n\r\n636\r\n01:13:57.820 --> 01:14:06.359\r\nAmy King: And what are some ways that students can demonstrate that learning in more non linguistic ways? If there's a possibility for that.\r\n\r\n637\r\n01:14:08.540 --> 01:14:16.959\r\nMargie Marrero: Yes, that's what that's what I was also kind of thinking around is that I think the the fine balance with translating and and newcomers, and\r\n\r\n638\r\n01:14:17.040 --> 01:14:41.680\r\nMargie Marrero: that find balance to find around making sure that they have content. That's accessible. But that we're not enabling is just somehow depending on your context. If it's with collaboration depending on the setting of the instruction is how to collaborate, or if it's yourself lesson plan, so that you are keeping the students goals in mind, and you know what that next step is for their\r\n\r\n639\r\n01:14:41.680 --> 01:15:03.390\r\nMargie Marrero: for their language. And so with newcomers and and some of the rubrics like, whether you're weda consortium state, or I'm in Texas. They're kind of still aligned, especially at those very, very beginning levels we want to see like those simple sentences as output. So I think, having some some collaboration just like Amy is saying, based on your context.\r\n\r\n640\r\n01:15:03.990 --> 01:15:06.109\r\nMargie Marrero: Keep in mind that.\r\n\r\n641\r\n01:15:06.490 --> 01:15:11.306\r\nMargie Marrero: Just like Ryan mentioned earlier, too. We don't wanna live in translation world forever.\r\n\r\n642\r\n01:15:11.760 --> 01:15:27.310\r\nMargie Marrero: So we want to find that