u know. They're very\r\n\r\n303\r\n00:34:53.929 --> 00:35:03.690\r\nRyan Rumpf: storytelling was a big part of their, you know customs and and how they grew up, but reading it out of a book was a little bit different.\r\n\r\n304\r\n00:35:03.880 --> 00:35:11.890\r\nRyan Rumpf: And so sharing with families, you know what are some some cool routines for family letters or family family reading.\r\n\r\n305\r\n00:35:12.140 --> 00:35:16.449\r\nRyan Rumpf: and everybody's looked different at at what? What works for them.\r\n\r\n306\r\n00:35:17.180 --> 00:35:19.650\r\nRyan Rumpf: So, but that is the next step.\r\n\r\n307\r\n00:35:25.505 --> 00:35:31.600\r\nLuz Johnson: If I may. I have a quick question on like well, just title 3.\r\n\r\n308\r\n00:35:33.060 --> 00:35:35.619\r\nLuz Johnson: Funds are Federal, and\r\n\r\n309\r\n00:35:36.180 --> 00:35:40.969\r\nLuz Johnson: from what I understand, you can purchase bilingual books\r\n\r\n310\r\n00:35:41.030 --> 00:35:43.169\r\nLuz Johnson: under title 3. That's\r\n\r\n311\r\n00:35:43.510 --> 00:35:45.280\r\nLuz Johnson: what schools are given.\r\n\r\n312\r\n00:35:45.510 --> 00:35:50.569\r\nRyan Rumpf: That's supplemental. It's a matter of allocating it whenever you get it.\r\n\r\n313\r\n00:35:50.810 --> 00:35:53.680\r\nRyan Rumpf: allocating it to the right spot.\r\n\r\n314\r\n00:35:55.120 --> 00:35:56.519\r\nLuz Johnson: Right. So\r\n\r\n315\r\n00:35:56.540 --> 00:35:57.969\r\nLuz Johnson: depending on your\r\n\r\n316\r\n00:35:58.120 --> 00:36:03.380\r\nLuz Johnson: the amount of students that you have that are multilingual learners, you know, every school gets their\r\n\r\n317\r\n00:36:03.590 --> 00:36:06.989\r\nLuz Johnson: or it's allocated, and they have funds. But what I'm saying is like\r\n\r\n318\r\n00:36:07.040 --> 00:36:09.840\r\nLuz Johnson: you can use under title 3,\r\n\r\n319\r\n00:36:09.970 --> 00:36:14.759\r\nLuz Johnson: those those money those monies can. The money can be used to purchase\r\n\r\n320\r\n00:36:16.