nd we found out that at the district level, that they don't want them getting any part of the test in their 1st language, because it's not what they're going to see on Georgia milestones.\r\n\r\n744\r\n01:27:12.370 --> 01:27:25.489\r\nJulie Lowery: our state assessment. And so they're making them take everything in English across the board because they want the raw data. So these kids are like, and I mean they're lengthy. I mean, like my 5th graders were doing a test today. And it was\r\n\r\n745\r\n01:27:25.930 --> 01:27:35.150\r\nJulie Lowery: 18 different questions. And it was multiple passages with like comprehension questions that go with it. Some of them have more than one answer, which they totally don't get yet like it's just.\r\n\r\n746\r\n01:27:37.360 --> 01:27:38.184\r\nRosemary Trumbo: It's a lot.\r\n\r\n747\r\n01:27:38.460 --> 01:27:41.340\r\nJulie Lowery: It's a lot like I'm struggling. I told my boss.\r\n\r\n748\r\n01:27:41.340 --> 01:27:42.420\r\nMargie Marrero: Trying to.\r\n\r\n749\r\n01:27:42.420 --> 01:27:42.920\r\nJulie Lowery: Yeah. Go ahead.\r\n\r\n750\r\n01:27:42.920 --> 01:27:59.980\r\nMargie Marrero: That's kind of something happening here here in Texas as well, and I know something that does help. And it was mentioned a little bit in the chat as well is to, and it does involve a lot of planning because you're learning a new curriculum, as you're kind of going through it just barely staying above water and then trying to meet the needs of all kids.\r\n\r\n751\r\n01:27:59.980 --> 01:28:02.161\r\nJulie Lowery: I got bubbles right now. I'm not even above water.\r\n\r\n752\r\n01:28:03.450 --> 01:28:05.190\r\nMargie Marrero: Yeah, you're kind of like, oh.\r\n\r\n753\r\n01:28:05.190 --> 01:28:06.000\r\nJulie Lowery: Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!\r\n\r\n754\r\n01:28:07.470 --> 01:28:32.370\r\nMargie Marrero: So I know that something that that is helpful is to narrow down, and I think it's what Yvonne is referring to as well. Narrow down your standards and even