    "title": "The Discussion Project Overview for Higher Education",
    "content": "File: The Discussion Project Overview for Higher Education.pdf\nTitle: The Discussion Project Overview for Higher Education\n\nContent:  Why Discussion? To improve student learning. When students engage in high quality discussion, they grow and learn. Through discussion students… ● Learn the array of academic skills required for discussion: speaking, listening, organization, questioning… ● Learn course content and skills. ● Better understand complex text. ● Prepare to write. ● Practice vocabulary, both academic and discipline-specific. ● Articulate their thoughts –they think! ● Practice the skills of democracy. What is The Discussion Project? The Discussion Project is unique. It is a professional development series for higher education instructors that focuses entirely on designing, implementing, and facilitating small and large group classroom discussion. Instructors learn strategies to create equitable and inclusive classroom environments in which students learn to discuss and discuss to learn. Why does The Discussion Project exist? To improve student learning When students engage in high quality discussion, they grow and learn. ● They learn the array of academic skills required for discussion. ● They learn course content, vocabulary, and skills. All students benefit from discussion, but especially students who are working on their speaking skills. High quality discussion improves students’ engagement, sense of belonging, and learning. How do we learn together in The Discussion Project? Do not use or reproduce these slides without express permission of The Discussion Project. The Discussion Project is offered in two modalities ● In-person (3 full days) ● Online (seven 2-hour Zoom sessions) The Discussion Project works well for both interdisciplinary groups and subject-specific teams. Cohorts are between 15 and 30 participants to maximize participation. Teaching Team! (some of us) How do we learn together in The Discussion Project? Do not use or reproduce these slides without express permission of The Discussion Project. The Discussion Project is experiential / interactive Participants… ● Witness modeling ● Experience, practice, and apply ● Debrief to reflect Learning Objectives 1. Create an equitable and inclusive classroom climate conducive to high quality discussion. 2. Distinguish between discussion and other forms of student talk. 3. Learn different ways to structure and facilitate discussion. 4. Learn to craft questions that foster discussion. 5. Design, implement, and reflect on plans for discussion. 6. Implement strategies that develop students’ discussion skills. 7. Understand the purposes and methods of assessment for improving discussion skills. Modules 1. Building Community 2. Defining Discussion 3. Facilitating Whole Group Interactions 4. Structuring Discussion & Crafting Questions 5. Planning & Assessing Discussion 6. Critiquing Discussion Plans 7. Maintaining Community Three (3) Day: Pricing In-Person Course Online Course Three Days (Modules 1-7), School * $30,000 for up to 30 participants ** Seven two-hour Zoom sessions (Modules 1-7), School $24,000 for up to 30 participants Instructional Coaching We offer instructional coaching for individual teachers and consultations for teams. In addition, we facilitate Collaborative Classroom Visits with teacher teams. Please inquire for pricing. *For in-person delivery in an institution, room and catering costs covered by institution. **Minimum enrollment is 15 participants. Extra participants / $1,000 per thediscussionproject.org High quality classroom discussion improves students’ engagement, sense of belonging, and learning. Contact us through our website: thediscussionproject.org",
