  {
    "id": "1e566df3-6386-4e7c-9f89-90f732736e54",
    "title": "Observer:",
    "content": "Title: Observer:\n\nContent: Observer:  Teacher:  Grade:  Date:  Time:  Categories  Classroom Snapshot  Glows & Grows  Classroom Environment  Teacher builds rapport and positive relationships with all students, creating a classroom environment in which all students’ diverse backgrounds, languages, identities, strengths, and interests are respected and play an active role within the learning community  ●  Ts have created a safe environment for learning  ●  Ts have created a learning environment that reflects the languages, cultures, and experiences of all students  ●  Ts acknowledge the identifies of all students to create an inclusive learning environment  ●  Ts and Ss use active listening and respectful language to reference students/peers, their ideas, and their work  ●  Ts and Ss promote the use of translanguaging  Glows:  Grows:  Representation  (Input)  Learners differ in the ways that they perceive and comprehend information that is presented to them. There is not one means of representation that will be optimal for all learners, so providing options for multiple means of representation is essential.  Additional Notes:  ●  Ts present content through multiple modalities (so input does not depend on a single sense like sight, hearing, or touch)  ●  Ts provide content in a flexible format so perceptual features can be varied, including the:  ○  Size, contrast, and color used for visual input  ○  Font type and size used for linguistic input  ○  Layout and size of visual input  ○  Volume and rate of speech for aural input (that may also include visual input)  ●  Ts invite cross-linguistic connections and or use translanguaging practices  Glows:  Grows:  Multimodal Instruction: Professional Learning Series Follow-up Walkthrough  Action & Expression  (Output)  Learners differ in the ways that they can navigate a learning environment and express what they know. There is not one means of action and expression that will be optimal for all learners, so providing options for action and expression is essential.  ●  Ts provide choice related to ways in which Ss will demonstrate content learning and language development that cater to different learning styles, interests, and abilities, such as:  ○  Speaking: speech, conversation, demonstration, etc.  ○  Writing: poem, song, script, comic strip, journals, etc.  ○  Representing: drawing, visual, model, infographic, etc.  ●  Ts optimize access to tools and technologies that help Ss meet the goal of full participation  ●  Ts provide opportunities for peer interaction, including  ○  communities of learners engaged in common activities  ○  prompts to “show and explain your work” (e.g., portfolio review)  ○  peers as mentors to model and support  Glows:  Grows:  Engagement  (Uptake)  Affect represents a crucial element to learning, and learners differ markedly in the ways in which they can be engaged or motivated to learn. There is not one means of engagement that will be optimal for all learners in all contexts, so providing multiple options for engagement is essential.  ●  Ts recruit interest by optimizing individual choice and autonomy over such things as  ○  level of perceived challenge  ○  tools used for information gathering or production  ○  sequence or timing for completion of tasks  ●  Ts allow Ss to participate in the design of learning tasks  ●  Ts involve Ss in setting their own goals  ●  Ts promote active engagement by varying learning activities so they can be:  ○  contextualized to Ss lives  ○  culturally and socially relevant and responsive  ○  appropriate for different cultural, ethnic, & gender groups  ●  Ts design activities so that learning is authentic, shared with real audiences, and reflects a purpose that is clear  ●  Ts provide tasks that allow for active participation, exploration and experimentation  ●  Ts invite personal response, evaluation and self-reflection  ●  Ts include activities that foster the use of imagination to solve problems, or make sense of complex ideas in creative ways  Glows:  Grows:  Additional Notes:  Resources Referenced: CAST (2018). Universal Design for Learning Guidelines version 2.2. Retrieved from http://udlguidelines.cast.org ",
    "document_type": "pdf",
