  {
    "id": "d4d7fe74-0388-43af-8e40-971fbe875c7d",
    "title": "CARE Coaching Advancing Equitable Educational Opportunities",
    "content": "CARE Coaching Advancing Equitable Educational Opportunities  Program Overview  CARE Coaching, a professional learning program offered through the Wisconsin Center for Education Products and Services, is designed to ensure that district- and school-based educators provide equitable educational opportunities for multilingual learners. The CARE Coaching approach cultivates engagement in professional learning that is: Collaborative, Actionable, Responsive, and Empowering.  C  A  R  E  Collaborative  CARE coaches value a culture of collaboration within and across the learning community.  Actionable  CARE coaches focus on actionable changes in practices that can quickly enhance learning.  Responsive  CARE coaches are responsive to the needs of educators and the learners they serve.  Empowering  CARE coaches empower partners to be reflective, self-directed & responsive.  CARE Coaches foster meaningful relationships and develop productive partnerships that elicit the strengths, knowledge, and ...",
