  {
    "id": "7898df8b-f193-4c46-8dd9-00f51b31dddb",
    "title": "Multimodal Instruction: Professional Learning Series Follow-up Walkthrough",
    "content": "Title: Multimodal Instruction: Professional Learning Series Follow-up Walkthrough\n\nContent: Multimodal Instruction: Professional Learning Series Follow-up Walkthrough\n\nGrade-level\n\nEngaging\n\nAffirming\n\nMeaningful\n\nObserver:\n\nTeacher:\n\nGrade:\n\nDate:\n\nTime:\n\nLesson:\n\nContent:\n\nTotal # Sts\n\n# ML Sts:\n\n# Dual ID Sts\n\nCategories\n\nClassroom Snapshot\n\nGlows &amp; Grows\n\nClassroom Environment Teacher builds rapport and positive relationships with all\n\nstudents, creating a classroom\n\nenvironment in which all students’ diverse backgrounds, languages, identities, strengths, and interests are respected and play an active role within the learning community\n\nTs have created a safe environment for learning\n\nTs have created a learning environment that reflects the languages, cultures, and experiences of all students\n\nTs acknowledge the identifies of all students to create an inclusive learning environment\n\nTs and Ss use active listening and respectful language to reference students/peers, their ideas, and their work\n\nTs and Ss promote the use of translanguaging\n\nGlows:\n\nGrows:\n\nSketch of Classroom Layout\n\nComments:\n\nRationale: Please provide justification for the overall level assessed:\n\nNot at all evident\n\nSomewhat evident\n\nEvident\n\nExemplary\n\nAdditional Notes:\n\nRepresentation\n\n(Input)\n\nLearners differ in the ways that they perceive and comprehend information that is presented to them. There is not one means of representation that will be optimal for all learners, so providing options for multiple means of representation is essential.\n\nTs present content through multiple modalities (so input does not depend on a single sense like sight, hearing, or touch)\n\nTs provide content in a flexible format so perceptual features can be varied, including the:\n\nSize, contrast, and color used for visual input\n\nFont type and size used for linguistic input\n\nLayout and size of visual input\n\nVolume and rate of speech for aural input (that may also include visual input)\n\nTs invite cross-linguistic connections and or use translanguaging practices\n\nGlows:\n\nGrows:\n\nRationale: Please provide justification for the overall level assessed:\n\nNot at all evident\n\nSomewhat evident\n\nEvident\n\nExemplary\n\nAdditional Notes:\n\nAction &amp; Expression\n\n(Output)\n\nLearners differ in the ways that they can navigate a learning environment and express what they know. There is not one means of action and expression that will be optimal for all learners, so providing options for action and expressionis essential.\n\nTs provide choice related to ways in which Ss will demonstrate content learning and language development that cater to different learning styles, interests, and abilities, such as:\n\nSpeaking: speech, conversation, demonstration, etc.\n\nWriting: poem, song, script, comic strip, journals, etc.\n\nRepresenting: drawing, visual, model, infographic, etc.\n\nTs optimize access to tools and technologies that help Ss meet the goal of full participation\n\nTs provide opportunities for peer interaction, including\n\ncommunities of learners engaged in common activities\n\nprompts to “show and explain your work” (e.g., portfolio review)\n\npeers as mentors to model and support\n\nGlows:\n\nGrows:\n\nRationale: Please provide justification for the overall level assessed:\n\nNot at all evident\n\nSomewhat evident\n\nEvident\n\nExemplary\n\nAdditional Notes:\n\nEngagement\n\n(Uptake)\n\nAffect represents a crucial element to learning, and learners differ markedly in the ways in which they can be engaged or motivated to learn. There is not one means of engagement that will be optimal for all learners in all contexts, so providing multiple options for engagement is essential.\n\nTs recruit interest by optimizing individual choice and autonomy over such things as\n\nlevel of perceived challenge\n\ntools used for information gathering or production\n\nsequence or timing for completion of tasks\n\nTs allow Ss to participate in the design of learning tasks\n\nTs involve Ss in setting their own goals\n\nTs promote active engagement by varying learning activities so they can be:\n\ncontextualized to Ss lives\n\nculturally and socially relevant and responsive\n\nappropriate for different cultural, ethnic, &amp; gender groups\n\nTs design activities so that learning is authentic, shared with real audiences, and reflects a purpose that is clear\n\nTs provide tasks that allow for active participation, exploration and experimentation\n\nTs invite personal response, evaluation and self-reflection\n\nTs include activities that foster the use of imagination to solve problems, or make sense of complex ideas in creative ways\n\nGlows:\n\nGrows:\n\nRationale: Please provide justification for the overall level assessed:\n\nNot at all evident\n\nSomewhat evident\n\nEvident\n\nExemplary\n\nAdditional Notes:\n\nResources Referenced: CAST (2018). Universal Design for Learning Guidelines version 2.2. Retrieved from http://udlguidelines.cast.org",
