  {
    "id": "dfea62cd-6e57-4872-8986-2abd8514ef5b",
    "title": "Building Capacity to Bridge Content Learning and Language Development",
    "content": "Title: Building Capacity to Bridge Content Learning and Language Development\n\nContent: Building Capacity to Bridge Content Learning and Language Development\n\nLearning Walk Observation Tool\n\nTeacher Name\n\nDate of Observation\n\nObserver Name\n\nEquity of Opportunity and Access\n\nTo support equity of opportunity and access, the teacher\n\nComments\n\nPromotes high expectations through standards-aligned learning objectives\n\nScaffolds instruction up through the use of visual aids, sentence frames, differentiated resources, peer collaboration, and teacher modeling\n\nBalances scaffolding and supports with productive struggle and meaning-making\n\nContent and Language Integration\n\nTo support the integration of content learning and language development, the teacher\n\nComments\n\nClarifies expectations through content and language objectives\n\nMakes connections between content knowledge and language use\n\nEngages students in meaning-making activities through multiple modalities that blend content learning and language development\n\nModels and promotes the use of academic language within and across disciplines\n\nOffers flexibility in the ways students can demonstrate their learning\n\nProvides descriptive feedback on both content mastery and language development\n\nFunctional Approach to Language Development\n\nTo support a functional approach to language development, the teacher\n\nComments\n\nPromotes purposeful language use through mentor texts, think-alouds, anchor charts, modeling, etc.\n\nProvides explicit instruction of specific language functions and language features\n\nSupports students in recognizing how language changes based on context\n\nProvides opportunities for students to practice using language based on specific roles, purposes, and audiences\n\nCollaboration among Stakeholders\n\nTo support collaboration among stakeholders, the teacher\n\nComments\n\nCollaborates in instructional planning\n\nEngages families through home-school communication, conferences, joint goal-setting, and culturally relevant community resources",
