  {
    "id": "f4bb4cfd-f0b2-4815-8f40-df0fb93b2589",
    "title": "Applying the Framework to Instructional Planning",
    "content": "Title: Applying the Framework to Instructional Planning\n\nContent: Applying the Framework to Instructional Planning\n\nLearning Walk Observation Tool\n\nTeacher Name\n\nDate of Observation\n\nObserver Name\n\nStep 1: Identify the Relevant Standards\n\nAs evidenced by instructional planning and classroom artifacts, the teacher has…\n\nComments\n\nCreated content objectives based on identified content standard(s)\n\nCommunicated learning expectations to students by clarifying content objectives\n\nCreated language objectives based on identified ELD standards\n\nCommunicated language use expectations by clarifying language objectives\n\nIdentified the concepts and content-specific practices associated with the standards\n\nRecorded ways to activate prior knowledge and/or leverage students’ experiences, interests, and cultural and linguistic backgrounds\n\nStep 2: Identify the Key Language Uses Associated with the “Demonstration of Learning” Task\n\nAs evidenced by instructional planning and classroom instruction, the teacher has…\n\nComments\n\nIdentified the key language use aligned to the “demonstration of learning” task\n\nDesigned instructional tasks designed for meaning-making\n\nDetermined how instructional tasks will be used to monitor both content learning and language development\n\nDeveloped formative assessment tasks to monitor content and language\n\nStep 3: Use Language Expectations to Create a Unit Learning Goal, Learning Intentions, and Success Indicators\n\nAs evidenced by instructional planning and classroom instruction, the teacher has…\n\nComments\n\nUsed language expectation stems and content standards to develop a learning goal\n\nPrioritized language functions\n\nUsed prioritized language functions to develop learning intentions\n\nScaffolded instruction based on learning intentions\n\nPrioritized language features aligned to prioritized language functions\n\nClarified expectations using mentor texts\n\nStudents will: (construct) (standard) (key language use) that (language function(s)) using (language feature(s)).\n\nStep 4: Identify Appropriate Supports*\n\nAs evidenced by instructional planning and classroom instruction, the teacher has identified supports…\n\nSensory Supports\n\n(circle as identified)\n\nGeneral\n\nReal-life objects (realia)\n\nManipulatives\n\nPictures &amp; photographs\n\nIllustrations, diagrams &amp; drawings\n\nMagazines &amp; newspapers\n\nPhysical activities\n\nVideos &amp; Films\n\nBroadcasts\n\nModels &amp; figures\n\nLanguage Arts\n\nIllustrated word/phrase walls\n\nCards with story elements\n\nSequence blocks\n\nEnvironmental print\n\nPosters or displays\n\nBulletin boards\n\nPhotographs\n\nCartoons\n\nAudiobooks\n\nMath\n\nBlocks/Cubes\n\nClocks, sundials, and other timekeepers\n\nNumber lines\n\nModels of geometric figures\n\nCalculators\n\nProtractors\n\nRulers\n\nYard/meter sticks\n\nGeoboards\n\nCounters\n\nCompasses\n\nCalendars\n\nCoins\n\nScience\n\nScientific instruments\n\nMeasurement tools\n\nPhysical models\n\nNatural materials\n\nActual substances, organisms, or objects of investigation\n\nPosters/Illustrations of processes or cycles\n\nSocial Studies\n\nMaps\n\nGlobes\n\nAtlases\n\nCompasses\n\nTimelines\n\nMulticultural artifacts\n\nArial &amp; satellite photographs\n\nVideo Clips\n\nGraphic Supports\n\n(circle as identified)\n\nCharts\n\nGraphic organizers\n\nTables\n\nGraphs\n\nTimelines\n\nNumber lines\n\nInteractive Supports\n\n(circle as identified)\n\nIn pairs or partners\n\nIn triads or small groups\n\nIn a whole group\n\nUsing cooperative group structures\n\nUsing the Internet or software programs\n\nIn the native language (L1)\n\nWith mentors\n\n*Taken from: The WIDA English Language Proficiency Standards and Resource Guide, 2007 Edition, Pre-Kindergarten through Grade 12, page RG-21.\n\nStudents will: (construct) (standard) (key language use) that (language function(s)) using (language feature(s)) reinforced by ((a) (support(s)).",
