  {
    "id": "473e4789-8a1d-40a2-8809-02e642e54641",
    "title": "Framework Learning Walk Tool",
    "content": "Title: Framework Learning Walk Tool\n\nContent: Framework Learning Walk Tool\n\nTeacher Name\n\nDate of Observation\n\nObserver Name\n\nRequired System Structures to Support Teacher Implementation:\n\nSchool structures to support teacher implementation include:\n\nComments\n\nProcesses or schedules to allow for Content and ELD Teachers to collaborate\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nRoles for ELD teachers to support the planning process\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nELD Teachers teaching language functions &amp; features  in direct support of content\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nStudents will: (construct) (standard) (key language use) that (language function(s)) using (language feature(s)) supported by (a) (support(s)).\n\nStep 1: Identify Relevant Content Concepts and Practices\n\nAs evidenced by planning and instruction, the teacher has…\n\nComments\n\nIdentified content standard\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nIdentified content concepts or content topics to support the content standard\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nListed relevant ELD Standards Statements\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nActivated prior knowledge and/or leveraged students’ experiences, interests, cultural and linguistic backgrounds\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nStep 2: Identify Key Language Uses\n\nDuring a given lesson, the teacher has…\n\nComments\n\nIdentified the Key Language Use most closely aligned to the summative task\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nImplemented instructional tasks designed for meaning-making\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nImplemented formative tasks to monitor progress\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nIdentified Key Language Uses associated with implemented formative tasks\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nStep 3: Organize and Prioritize Functions and Features of Language\n\nDuring a given lesson, the teacher has…\n\nComments\n\nIdentified and Prioritized a language function to determine which to introduce first\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nUsed a prioritized language function to scaffold instruction\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nIdentified and Prioritized one/a few language features to support language function\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nUsed one/a few language features to support a language function\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nStep 4: Provide Appropriate Supports*\n\nDuring a given lesson, the teacher has implemented linguistic supports to scaffold language features and functions through…\n\nComments\n\nSensory Supports\n\n(circle as identified)\n\nGeneral\n\nReal-life objects (realia)\n\nManipulatives\n\nPictures &amp; photographs\n\nIllustrations, diagrams &amp; drawings\n\nMagazines &amp; newspapers\n\nPhysical activities\n\nVideos &amp; Films\n\nBroadcasts\n\nModels &amp; figures\n\nLanguage Arts\n\nIllustrated word/phrase walls\n\nFelt or magnetic figures of story elements\n\nSequence blocks\n\nEnvironmental print\n\nPosters or displays\n\nBulletin boards\n\nPhotographs\n\nCartoons\n\nAudiobooks\n\nSongs/Chants\n\nMath\n\nBlocks/Cubes\n\nClocks, sundials, and other timekeepers\n\nNumber lines\n\nModels of geometric figures\n\nCalculators\n\nProtractors\n\nRulers\n\nYard/meter sticks\n\nGeoboards\n\nCounters\n\nCompasses\n\nCalendars\n\nCoins\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nScience\n\nScientific instruments\n\nMeasurement tools\n\nPhysical models\n\nNatural materials\n\nActual substances, organisms, or objects     of investigation\n\nPosters/Illustrations of processes or cycles\n\nSocial Studies\n\nMaps\n\nGlobes\n\nAtlases\n\nCompasses\n\nTimelines\n\nMulticultural artifacts\n\nArial &amp; satellite photographs\n\nVideo Clips\n\nGraphic Supports\n\n(circle as identified)\n\nCharts\n\nGraphic organizers\n\nTables\n\nGraphs\n\nTimelines\n\nNumber lines\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nInteractive Supports\n\n(circle as identified)\n\nIn pairs or partners\n\nIn triads or small groups\n\nIn a whole group\n\nUsing cooperative group structures\n\nUsing the Internet or software programs\n\nIn the native language (L1)\n\nWith mentors\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nSelected scaffolds directly support the language function and features found in the formative/summative tasks discussed in Step 3.\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\n*Taken from: The WIDA English Language Proficiency Standards and Resource Guide, 2007 Edition, Pre-Kindergarten through Grade 12, page RG-21.\n\n1",
