  {
    "id": "12f40ff8-546c-4916-9d3d-bbe520341ce7",
    "title": "Learning Walk Tool - Checklist Version",
    "content": "Title: Learning Walk Tool - Checklist Version\n\nContent: Learning Walk Tool - Checklist Version  Classroom Environment  Observable  Concept  Comments  ■  Teacher builds rapport and positive relationships with all students.  ■  Classroom reflects students’ languages, cultures, experiences, and identities.  ■  Students feel safe, respected, and included.  ■  Active listening, respectful interactions, and translanguaging practices are evident.  Representation (Input)  Observable  Concept  Comments  ■  Content is provided through multiple modalities (visual, auditory, kinesthetic).  ■  Materials are flexible in font, color, contrast, and layout.  ■  Visuals, scaffolds, and cognates are used to increase accessibility.  ■  Opportunities for cross-linguistic connections and multimodal supports.  Action & Expression (Output)  Observable  Concept  Comments  ■  Students have choice in how they demonstrate learning (speak, write, create, perform).  ■  Tools and technologies are available to support accessibility.  ■  Peer interaction and modeling are encouraged.  ■  Student responses are scaffolded (sentence frames, visuals, multiple formats).  Engagement (Uptake)  Observable  Concept  Comments  ■  Students exercise voice, choice, and autonomy in tasks.  ■  Learning activities are authentic, relevant, and culturally responsive.  ■  Students set personal goals and reflect on progress.  ■  Lessons foster motivation through connections to interests, trust, and learner agency.  Universal Design for Learning (UDL) Alignment  Observable  Concept  Comments  ■  Access, Support, and Executive Function strategies are evident.  ■  Instruction integrates content and language scaffolds.  ■  Students’ strengths, interests, and preferences are leveraged to enhance outcomes.  ■  Student agency is intentionally cultivated. ",
