  {
    "id": "181f2099-4646-4f33-92f6-f8016a14b53d",
    "title": "CARE Coaching Newcomer Learning Walk Tool",
    "content": "Title: CARE Coaching Newcomer Learning Walk Tool\n\nContent: CARE Coaching Newcomer Learning Walk Tool\n\nTeacher:\n\nSubject:\n\nGrade:\n\nDate:\n\nEstablishes Partnerships with Families\n\nAction\n\nImpact\n\nYes?\n\nThe teacher…\n\nPromotes regular communication with families via newsletters, emails, or other channels that support two-way communication\n\nEncourages family members to volunteer in the classroom or to participate in class projects, presentations, or cultural-sharing activities\n\nDisplays student work that includes family involvement, family photos, stories, and cultural artifacts\n\nWelcomes families into the classroom to observe or participate\n\nCreates a Safe and Thriving Environment\n\nAction\n\nImpact\n\nYes?\n\nThe teacher…\n\nPronounces students’ names correctly\n\nLabels classroom in students’ languages\n\nDisplays items that represent students' linguistic and cultural heritage\n\nPromotes an inclusive and protected learning community\n\nShapes positive relationships with and among students\n\nSets challenging yet achievable goals\n\nPromotes monitoring and self-assessment\n\nEngages in Effective Instructional Practices\n\nAction\n\nImpact\n\nYes?\n\nThe teacher…\n\nUses clear, simple, and concise language to explain concepts.\n\nEmploys visual supports such as images, charts, and diagrams to enhance understanding.\n\nProvides resources in students' native languages, when possible, to support comprehension\n\nAcknowledges comprehensible input- rate of speech, visuals, builds background,\n\nScaffolds Content, Process &amp; Environment, and Product\n\nAction\n\nImpact\n\nYes?\n\nThe teacher…\n\nImplements orientation sessions to familiarize newcomers with the school environment, routines, and expectations.\n\nPairs newcomers with peer mentors who can guide them through social and academic aspects of school life\n\nUses a range of visuals, videos, and real-life objects to make the content accessible and instructional tasks understandable\n\nConnects everyday language to academic language\n\nDevelops Effective Lessons\n\nAction\n\nImpact\n\nYes?\n\nThe teacher…\n\nDevelops personalized learning plans that address the specific needs, strengths, and learning styles of each newcomer\n\nPlans for providing step-by-step support and gradually increasing the complexity of tasks to build confidence and competence\n\nConsiders using activities such as role-playing, group discussions, and language games to enhance language acquisition in plans\n\nClarifies content and language objectives\n\nAdditional Notes\n\n© 2024 CARE Coaching 2",
