    "id": "15b333c4-6a79-4c59-93a6-a92a56ca5530",
    "title": "Universal Design for Learning for English Learners",
    "content": "Title: Universal Design for Learning for English Learners\n\nContent: Universal Design for Learning for English Learners  Learning Walk Observation Tool  Observer: ___________________  Class/Grade: _________________  Date/Time: ___________________  Teacher: _____________________  Multiple Means of Engagement  Observed? (✓/✗)  Look-fors  Notes/Evidence  Students have opportunities for choice and autonomy.  Learning is connected to relevant ideas, value, and/or the unit or project has authenticity, such as with an authentic audience.  Joy, play, or curiosity is encouraged.  Classroom environment reduces stress. Students are safe to take risks and ask questions.  Students are supported to sustain effort & persistence.  Collaboration and belonging are evident.  Multiple languages/dialects are acknowledged and respected.  Students reflect on beliefs, motivations, language choices, and/or identity.  Observed?  Multiple Means of Representation  Look-fors  (✓/✗)  Notes/Evidence  Information is presented in multiple formats (visual, auditory, tactile, etc.).  Vocabulary, symbols, and language are clarified or scaffolded.  Key Language Uses, functions, and features for word, sentence, and discourse level texts are evident.  Patterns, big ideas, concepts, and relationships are highlighted.  Students connect new content to prior knowledge.  Multiple media/tools are available for communication & creation by students.  Multiple Means of Action & Expression  Observed? (✓/✗)  Look-fors  Notes/Evidence  Students use varied methods to respond or show learning of measurable goals and/or success criteria.  Students are supported to practice and build fluency with speaking and writing.  Goals and expectations for both content and language are made clear.  Executive function strategies and metalinguistic awareness are explicit and transparent. Students use strategies to plan, organize, monitor progress and self-assess  Actionable feedback is provided for content and language.  Overall Reflections  Strengths observed:  Opportunities for growth:  Next steps/feedback for teacher: ",
