    "id": "3338f90c-bf70-461e-9c19-c78cdb861e7b",
    "title": "Building Capacity to Bridge Content Learning and Language Development",
    "content": "Title: Building Capacity to Bridge Content Learning and Language Development\n\nContent: Building Capacity to Bridge Content Learning and Language Development  Learning Walk Observation Tool  Teacher Name  Date of Observation  Observer Name  Equity of Opportunity and Access  To support equity of opportunity and access, the teacher promotes high expectations through standards-aligned learning objectives. The teacher scaffolds instruction through:  Comments  The use of visual aids  The use of sentence frames and/or anchor charts for Key Language Uses  Facilitating students' engagement in peer collaboration with structured Listening, Speaking, Reading, and Writing opportunities  Content and Language Integration  To support the integration of content learning and language development, the teacher  Comments  Clarifies expectations through content and language objectives. For example  Students will: (construct) (content standard) (key language use) that (language function(s)) using (language feature(s)).  Engages students in meaning-making activities through multiple modalities that blend content learning and language development  Models and promotes the use of academic language  Provides descriptive and actionable feedback on both content mastery and language development  Functional Approach to Language Development  To support a functional approach to language development, the teacher promotes purposeful language use and development through:  Comments  Promotes purposeful language use through mentor texts  Modeling think-alouds for both content and language decision-making, problem-solving solving or other metacognitive/linguistic reasoning  Providing explicit instruction of specific language functions and language features  Provides opportunities for students to practice using language based on specific roles, purposes, and audiences ",
