  {
    "id": "268ac1e8-85f1-4f0d-9b1a-941b116d6312",
    "title": "Promoting Autonomy through Formative Assessment Practices",
    "content": "Title: Promoting Autonomy through Formative Assessment Practices\n\nContent: Promoting Autonomy through Formative Assessment Practices\n\nLearning Walk Observation Tool\n\nTeacher Name\n\nDate of Observation\n\nObserver Name\n\nLearning Goals, Learning Intentions, and Success Indicators\n\nExpectations for content learning and language use are clear.\n\nComments\n\nLearning expectations for both content and language are explicitly highlighted.\n\nLearning intentions are scaffolded toward the learning goal.\n\nSuccess indicators provide specific examples of the language needed to meet the learning intentions.\n\nStudents use learning expectations to monitor their progress.\n\nTeacher models effective language use\n\nMeaning-Making Tasks\n\nStudents are actively engaging in learning through meaning-making tasks.\n\nComments\n\nInstructional tasks…\n\nengage students with content and language.\n\nare scaffolded to meet the diverse educational experiences and proficiency levels of students.\n\npromote interaction and collaborative problem-solving.\n\nrequire students to analyze, synthesize, or evaluate information.\n\nare supported by sentence frames, word banks, or graphic organizers.\n\nprovide opportunities for peer discussion and collaborative work.\n\nConstructive Feedback\n\nTeacher and peers provide feedback that improves performance.\n\nComments\n\nteacher and peers provide feedback that is specific, actionable, and connected to the success indicators.\n\nstudents are given opportunities to use feedback to revise their work.\n\nfeedback, oral or written, point to specific improvements or strengths.\n\nthere structures for peer feedback or self-assessment.\n\nstudents use feedback to make corrections or enhancements.\n\nrubrics or checklists are used by students to self-assess or peer-assess.\n\nStudent Agency\n\nStudents take ownership of their learning.\n\nComments\n\nstudents are encouraged to monitor their own progress using the learning intentions and success indicators.\n\nstudents reflect on their learning and identify next steps\n\nstudents have opportunities to make choices in how they demonstrate their understanding",
