  {
    "id": "46d3866e-e400-4fd6-bba2-f18887c0aa66",
    "title": "Implement scaffolding strategies and supports that provide equitable access to grade-level content.",
    "content": "Title: Implement scaffolding strategies and supports that provide equitable access to grade-level content.\n\nContent: “Enhancing Writing Proficiency through a Literacy Learning Cycle” Learning Walk Observation Tool that aligns with this session’s focus on developing multilingual learners’ writing through integrated reading, writing, and language instruction.This version is streamlined for field-based walkthroughs, focusing on how teachers:\n\nImplement scaffolding strategies and supports that provide equitable access to grade-level content.\n\nUse knowledge-building activities to deepen conceptual understanding across modalities.\n\nEmploy reading protocols and mentor texts to examine genre purpose, organization, and language features.\n\nGuide students through the writing process, from modeled and joint construction to independent composition.\n\nFacilitate reflection, feedback, and revision as part of the literacy learning cycle.\n\nLearning Walk Tool: Enhancing Writing Proficiency through a Literacy Learning Cycle\n\nPurpose:To observe how teachers implement the literacy learning cycle to strengthen students’ writing proficiency and language development. The focus is on how instruction integrates reading and writing to build genre knowledge, supports students in analyzing and producing texts, and fosters a recursive process of drafting, feedback, and revision that promotes growth and confidence as writers.\n\nTeacher Name\n\nDate of Observation\n\nObserver Name\n\nScaffolding and Supports\n\nFocus Area &amp; Look Fors\n\nEvidence/Notes\n\nScaffolding strategies enhance access to grade-level content (e.g., asset-based language, safe learning environment, visual/linguistic supports, peer interaction, translanguaging).\n\nBuilding Knowledge\n\nFocus Area &amp; Look Fors\n\nEvidence/Notes\n\nFocus Area &amp; Look Fors\n\nInstructional activities build knowledge through multiple modalities and activate prior learning.\n\nStudents use, hear, and see the language associated with the topic.\n\nSupporting Reading\n\nFocus Area &amp; Look Fors\n\nEvidence/Notes\n\nFocus Area &amp; Look Fors\n\nMentor texts highlight purpose, organization, and language features of genre.\n\nModeled/shared reading includes comprehension questions and language exploration.\n\nReading groups and collaborative reading deepen comprehension and analysis.\n\nExploring a Genre\n\nFocus Area &amp; Look Fors\n\nEvidence/Notes\n\nFocus Area &amp; Look Fors\n\nMentor texts highlight the purpose, organization, and key language features of a genre.\n\nTeachers facilitate language-focused conversations and analysis.\n\nSupporting Writing\n\nFocus Area &amp; Look Fors\n\nEvidence/Notes\n\nFocus Area &amp; Look Fors\n\nModeled, joint, and collaborative writing make writing processes visible and scaffold text construction.\n\nUsing a Genre\n\nFocus Area &amp; Look Fors\n\nEvidence/Notes\n\nFocus Area &amp; Look Fors\n\nWriting routines enable independent construction, feedback, reflection, and publishing.\n\nOptional Rating Scale\n\nDomain\n\n1 -\n\nEmerging\n\n2 -\n\nDeveloping\n\n3 -\n\nApplying\n\n4 -\n\nExtending\n\nScaffolding and supports\n\nBuilding Knowledge\n\nSupporting Reading\n\nExploring a Genre\n\nSupporting Writing\n\nUsing a Genre\n\nObserver Information\n\nObserver: ___________________________\n\nDate: ___________________________\n\nGrade Level / Content Area: ___________________________\n\nObservation Length: ___________________________",
