  {
    "id": "a135463f-8e30-411f-a044-f8374286c037",
    "title": "6.1_Learning_Walk_Reformatted",
    "content": "Title: 6.1_Learning_Walk_Reformatted\n\nContent: “Enhancing Writing Proficiency through a Literacy Learning Cycle” Learning Walk Observation Tool that aligns with this session’s focus on developing multilingual learners’ writing through integrated reading, writing, and language instruction.  This version is streamlined for field-based walkthroughs, focusing on how teachers:  •  Implement scaffolding strategies and supports that provide equitable access to grade-level content.  •  Use knowledge-building activities to deepen conceptual understanding across modalities.  •  Employ reading protocols and mentor texts to examine genre purpose, organization, and language features.  •  Guide students through the writing process, from modeled and joint construction to independent composition.  •  Facilitate reflection, feedback, and revision as part of the literacy learning cycle.  Learning Walk Tool: Enhancing Writing Proficiency through a Literacy Learning Cycle  Purpose:  To observe how teachers implement the literacy learning cycle to strengthen students’ writing proficiency and language development. The focus is on how instruction integrates reading and writing to build genre knowledge, supports students in analyzing and producing texts, and fosters a recursive process of drafting, feedback, and revision that promotes growth and confidence as writers.  Teacher Name  Date of Observation  Observer Name  Scaffolding and Supports  Focus Area & Look Fors  Evidence/Notes  Scaffolding strategies enhance access to grade-level content (e.g., asset-based language, safe learning environment, visual/linguistic supports, peer interaction, translanguaging).  Building Knowledge  Focus Area & Look Fors  Evidence/Notes  Focus Area & Look Fors  Instructional activities build knowledge through multiple modalities and activate prior learning.  Students use, hear, and see the language associated with the topic.  Supporting Reading  Focus Area & Look Fors  Evidence/Notes  Focus Area & Look Fors  Mentor texts highlight purpose, organization, and language features of genre.  Modeled/shared reading includes comprehension questions and language exploration.  Reading groups and collaborative reading deepen comprehension and analysis.  Exploring a Genre  Focus Area & Look Fors  Evidence/Notes  Focus Area & Look Fors  Mentor texts highlight the purpose, organization, and key language features of a genre.  Teachers facilitate language-focused conversations and analysis.  Supporting Writing  Focus Area & Look Fors  Evidence/Notes  Focus Area & Look Fors  Modeled, joint, and collaborative writing make writing processes visible and scaffold text construction.  Using a Genre  Focus Area & Look Fors  Evidence/Notes  Focus Area & Look Fors  Writing routines enable independent construction, feedback, reflection, and publishing.  Optional Rating Scale  Domain  1 -  Emerging  2 -  Developing  3 -  Applying  4 -  Extending  Scaffolding and supports  Building Knowledge  Supporting Reading  Exploring a Genre  Supporting Writing  Using a Genre  Observer Information  ●  Observer: ___________________________  ●  Date: ___________________________  ●  Grade Level / Content Area: ___________________________  ●  Observation Length: ___________________________ ",
