  {
    "id": "39078d85-983c-42a6-9cfb-c10964466332",
    "title": "Supporting Students with Limited or Interrupted Formal Education",
    "content": "Title: Supporting Students with Limited or Interrupted Formal Education\n\nContent: Supporting Students with Limited or Interrupted Formal Education\n\nLearning Walk Observation Tool\n\nTeacher Name\n\nDate of Observation\n\nObserver Name\n\nIdentifying and Understanding SLIFE Needs\n\nSystems are in place to support SLIFE.\n\nComments\n\nTools or processes used to identify SLIFE.\n\nInstruction or materials that incorporate students’ backgrounds, languages, and experiences.\n\nTeacher awareness of socio-emotional factors impacting SLIFE.\n\nEngagement and Encouragement Strategies\n\nActivities are designed to make learning accessible, meaningful, and relevant.\n\nComments\n\nthere is evidence of scaffolding, visual supports, and hands-on learning opportunities.\n\nthere are opportunities for SLIFE to build relationships and develop trust with peers and educators\n\ninstructional tasks connect to students’ lives and experiences.\n\nvisuals, realia, or manipulatives are used to support comprehension.\n\nthere are structured opportunities for peer interaction and collaborative learning.\n\nInformed Instructional Programming\n\nInstructional programs support the needs of SLIFE.\n\nComments\n\ndifferentiated instruction is tailored to individual student profiles.\n\nformative and summative assessments are used to monitor progress.\n\nprograms balance foundational skills with content learning.\n\ninstructional programs flexible and responsive to SLIFE’s unique needs?\n\nSLIFE are given opportunities for accelerated learning or targeted intervention?\n\nStudent Agency\n\nStudents take ownership of their learning.\n\nComments\n\nstudents are encouraged to monitor their own progress using the learning intentions and success indicators.\n\nstudents reflect on their learning and identify next steps\n\nstudents have opportunities to make choices in how they demonstrate their understanding",
