    "id": "3e043cde-6026-46b6-8a14-32a1be769965",
    "title": "CHECKLIST FOR REVIEWING DRAFTED ITEMS:",
    "content": "Title: CHECKLIST FOR REVIEWING DRAFTED ITEMS:\n\nContent: CHECKLIST FOR REVIEWING DRAFTED ITEMS:  Needs Revisions  Meets  Expectations  Check for content relevance and DOK  Does the item target particular knowledge, skills, or abilities that is/are essential to the intent of the standard and element?  Does the overall item (inclusive of distractors) present a question/task at the intended DOK level?  Comments:  Check item structure and components  If a stimulus is used, is the content necessary for students to answer the question, accessible, and clearly presented?  Are all distractors plausible and reasonable with only one correct answer choice?  Do distractors have parallel structure and are they listed in an appropriate order?  Comments:  Check for excess difficulty  Are there any vocabulary terms that could be simplified?  Are there formulas or other resources that could be provided?  Are directions needed? And if so, are the directions clear?  Comments:  Check language  Is the question or task focused, clear, and understandable?  Does the item use plain language that is written in an appropriate and respectful tone?  Does each answer choice fit grammatically with the question?  Comments:  Check for bias and sensitivity  Does any part of the item include language that could be offensive or negative toward a particular religion, disability, ethnicity, etc?  Does the item favor students with or rely on knowledge of particular life backgrounds and experiences?  Does the item context require specialized knowledge outside of the content being assessed (e.g. surfing, horseback riding, motorcycle parts, etc.)  Comments:  Check appropriateness for audience  Are examples and contexts appropriate for the student audience?  Does the item respect, value and affirm the diversity of the student population?  Comments:  Include any additional comments or feedback here: ",
