  {
    "id": "5149fa0a-730c-4713-aaa5-f6bdb3cd6d04",
    "title": "Title: (Part 2/2)",
    "content": "The presentation will address alignment Challenge 1, as described by Fulmer et al (JRST, 2018), related to identification of appropriate referents and comparands for alignment judgement as well as alignment Challenge 2, related to defining and judging alignment of three-dimensional standards.  Although this session focuses on the alignment of NGSS with a statewide summative assessment, the overall alignment concepts are also relevant to the relationships between standards and other forms of assessment as well as between standards and instructional practice. Establishment of appropriate alignment criteria for new science assessments will promote equitable access to high-quality learning experiences for all students. Appropriate alignment criteria will also help ensure the assessments are yielding meaningful data about student achievement as relates to new science standards. This presentation will be especially relevant to states and test development contractors who need practical approaches for evaluating alignment of assessments with the NGSS and other Framework-based standards.",
