    "id": "2dc3126e-5213-46f5-aecb-b0809ba9bad3",
    "title": "Title:",
    "content": "Title:\n\nAlignment Analysis of a Framework-Based Statewide Summative Science Assessment with Corresponding Standards (such as NGSS): Results and Recommendations\n\n90-minute symposium\n\nSubmitter – Sara Christopherson, WCEPS\n\nPresenters:\n\nTimothy Butcher\n\nBrian Reiter\n\nJon Cohen\n\nSara Christopherson\n\nTopic Strands:\n\nHigh-quality assessments\n\nEquitable accountability\n\n[other options are: Effective uses of data; continuous evaluation and improvement; meaningful communication of student and school outcomes]\n\nProposal Summary (147 words; 150 words max):\n\nReleased and exemplar tasks for Framework-based science assessments suggest a wide range of interpretation regarding the expectations of the corresponding science standards. Without valid alignment criteria to ensure that all students are being supported in meeting the same high standards, the NGSS and other Framework-based standards risk failing to achieve the desired impact on advancing science education for all students (Fulmer, et al, 2018...",
