  {
    "id": "375eddb7-1016-447a-8999-eab40b7b4c63",
    "title": "WebbAlign DOK PD for Fayette County CTE: March 15, 2022 Session Evaluation Responses (Part 2/2)",
    "content": "Recognizing DOK as a component of the assessment process. I am better at identifying DOK in classroom activities.\n\nDOK explanation\n\nBlueprint helped me to understand that I was following the standards for the tests and as we assigned DOK levels I understood the levels.\n\nMany aspects were valuable to me.\n\nRevisiting assessments on a regular basis is very important\n\nItem Writing and evaluation\n\nThe structure of my questions and having the correct number of each DOK level in my assessments.\n\nHow other schools operate.\n\nAgain, clear and concise assessment questions\n\nIt was good to be reminded of the equity of learning for all students, regardless of which school in our county they attend. This is what makes the work we did today so important.\n\nBouncing my ideas off of my colleagues\n\n10. In what way(s) do you view educational assessment differently after participating in the March 15 PD session?\n\nDOK\n\nI want to be intentional about assessing what is intended to be assessed\n\nThe importance of planning assessments and reevaluating them as time goes on.\n\nmaking sure all standards are covered for a unit test\n\nEnsuring that I am assessing the DOK level of the standard.\n\nBeing descriptive and specific is key\n\nevaluation is necessary to help communicate on common ground and allow for equitable experiences\n\nMore thought into making my test\n\nAs an educator I need to be efficient in my determination of standards with proper DOK evaluations.\n\nThere are different ways to view the same question.\n\nDOK are not performance levels.\n\nLooking at the wording of questions and how they apply to the answer we are looking for\n\nBetter appreciation of the necessity of having and following standards\n\nLinking the question to the DOK\n\nMore seriously\n\nI can see a more scientific perspective on how test questions are developed.\n\nLook at Test Questions in a more detailed manner\n\nAssessments should be designed more intentional and with great thought.\n\nWe must ensure that we are inclusive and that all the question meet it's intended purpose.\n\nIt has increased my knowledge in this area of concern.\n\nI believe you need common goals for all the school\n\nI will be more aware of creating items more intentionally.\n\nEvaluating questions\n\nhelping evaluate current assessments\n\nI took a class in measurement and evaluation. This was a good review.\n\nI felt much more confidant after.\n\nWe feel more connected as a group of teachers that teach the same subject\n\nContinually perfecting my assessments is the buy in I left with\n\nbut this improved my ability at item analysis.\n\nCareful consideration of standards with DOK\n\nThe need to re-access your assessments is important.\n\nI learned the most from good test design.\n\nRecognizing that DOK does not have anything to do with student ability\n\nvery good.\n\nMaking sure my questions are understood by all.\n\nAll documented.\n\nVery in depth\n\nTo ensure equity of learning for all students in our county, I can see the importance of working together with my colleagues to create meaningful, standards-based, common assessments for our students. I was also reminded to be aware of how biases, poorly-worded questions, etc. can affect student performance and to keep that in mind while drafting assessment questions.\n\nMore confident\n\nI will consider DOK in writing assessment questions going forward.\n\nConnection with the standards\n\n12. Any other feedback or comments are welcomed here!\n\nThank you!\n\nSara is excellent.\n\nthank you for all your work.\n\nThank you for organizing this.\n\nI would appreciate the opportunity to collaborate with the other JROTC unit as well as with Aviation\n\ngood\n\nI would have liked for the \"new teachers\" to have a session on this so I did not have to explain the process to them.\n\nThank you for a great PL\n\nMore time to collaborate with my colleagues\n\nI thought this pd went very well.\n\nThank you for your hard work!\n\nGreat Job!\n\nThank you for the invitation.\n\nWisconsin Center for Education Products &amp; Services\n\n1213 N. Sherman Ave., #322   Madison, WI 53704  877-272-5593   WebbAlign@wceps.org   www.webbalign.org\n\nWisconsin Center for Education Products &amp; Services\n\n1213 N. Sherman Ave., #322   Madison, WI 53704  877-272-5593   info@wceps.org   www.wceps.org",
