  {
    "id": "0a711a82-b730-4678-8bb9-c378d5ae4178",
    "title": "Debrief: Eden Prairie WebbAlign DOK PD December 8, 2022 (Part 2/2)",
    "content": "A next session is scheduled for February 9, 2023. In this session, it may be helpful to emphasize that, with practice, it should be possible to fairly consistently distinguish between and among the DOKs of expectations and tasks. If determining the complexity is challenging, it may be helpful to rework the language of the expectations or tasks, to ensure the intended complexity of engagement is clear. Examples of academic standards that are DOK 1, 2, 3, and 4 could help to illustrate the different categories of expectations. An example of how to structure a lesson evaluation through the DOK lens could also be presented. If there is interest in a focus on lesson evaluation (or assessment evaluation, etc), specific considerations can be shared (and, potentially, refined by participants for Eden Prairie-specific use). Continued emphasis on the unit of analysis (the content of curriculum materials) may help promote calibration in understanding.\n\nAdditional topics may include further exploration of the relationships and differences between and among task complexity, learning progressions, and achievement. Future PL sessions may include collaborative work time for educators to use DOK to evaluate the complexity of relevant academic standards, compare the DOK of standards with and derivative learning targets (and essential questions, etc. as applicable) within their planning materials (e.g. scope and sequence, lesson plans, assessments – of all types) adjusting as needed, consider strategies for promoting complex engagement for all students, including eliminating difficulty barriers to allow access to the intended task complexity. Collaborative work time would focus overall on supporting ongoing improvement through self-evaluation of materials to promote alignment or coherence between and among the standards, learning targets, activities, assignments, and other learning opportunities, and assessments. Eden Prairie will work to define the goals and desired outcomes of future sessions in collaboration with WebbAlign.\n\nWisconsin Center for Education Products &amp; Services\n\n1213 N. Sherman Ave., #322   Madison, WI 53704  877-272-5593   WebbAlign@wceps.org   www.webbalign.org\n\nWisconsin Center for Education Products &amp; Services\n\n1213 N. Sherman Ave., #322   Madison, WI 53704  877-272-5593   info@wceps.org   www.wceps.org",
