  {
    "id": "24fa84c7-5930-468d-9f04-826e097cef7d",
    "title": "Administering WIDA MODEL Online: Grades 1–12 (Part 2/7)",
    "content": "Technology Requirements (1 of 2)  WIDA Consortium / MetriTech  Test Administrator Workstation Requirement OS Compatible Browser(s) Hardware Requirements Minimum Screen Size Microsoft Windows XP SP2 or newer •   Microsoft Internet Explorer 10 or greater (Internet Explorer 10 is not supported on Windows XP or Windows Vista) • Google Chrome Version 6 or greater • Apple Safari Version 5.1  • Mozilla Firefox 4.0 or greater •Minimum RAM: 1GB of available RAM •Headset/speakers recommended for audio playback of practice test Dependent on test definition— minimum 1024x768 Apple OS X 10.6 Snow Leopard) or greater •   Apple Safari Version 5.1 or greater • Mozilla Firefox 4.0 or greater • Google Chrome Version 6 or greater •Minimum RAM: 1GB of available RAM •Headset/speakers recommended for audio playback of practice test Dependent on test definition— minimum 1024x768 iPad Apple iOS 6.0 or greater  Apple Safari  •External Keyboard recommended for text entry •Headset/speakers recommended for audio playback of practice test 10 inch (not iPad Mini) Chromebook   OS 33 or Greater Chrome Headset/speakers recommended for audio playback of practice test 10 inch or greater with a screen resolution that supports the test definition—minimum 1024x768 Windows Surface Tablet Windows 8 or greater •   Microsoft Internet Explorer 10 or greater (Internet Explorer 10 is not supported on Windows XP or Windows Vista) • Google Chrome Version 6 or greater • Apple Safari Version 5.1  • Mozilla Firefox 4.0 or greater •External Keyboard recommended for text entry •Headset/speakers recommended for audio playback of practice test Minimum resolution 1024x768\n\nTechnology Requirements (2 of 2) WIDA Consortium / MetriTech  Student Workstation Requirement OS Compatible Browser(s) Hardware Requirements Minimum Screen Size Microsoft Windows XP SP2 or newer Student Browser Required •Minimum RAM: 1GB of available RAM •Headset/speakers recommended for audio playback of practice test 1024x768 Apple OS X 10.6 Snow Leopard) or greater Student Browser Required Minimum Ram: 1GB; headset recommended for audio playback.  1024x768 iPad Apple iOS 6.0 or greater Student Browser Required (Not available at this time) External keyboard recommended for text entry (On-screen keyboard functionality will work); headset recommended for audio playback 10 inch (not iPad Mini) Chromebook   OS 33 or Greater Student Browser Required Headset/speakers recommended for audio playback of practice test 10 inch or greater with a screen resolution that supports the test definition—minimum 1024x768 Android 4.0  Ice Cream Sandwich or newer Student Browser Required (Not available at this time) External keyboard recommended for text entry (On-screen keyboard functionality will work); headset recommended for audio playback 9.2 inch or greater with a screen resolution that supports the test definition—minimum 1024x768 Student Browser Available for Download under Training Materials -&gt; Administration Files\n\nTutorials and Intro Screens Available for Listening and Reading Designed to show students the layout of the screens and how to navigate through the test.  Tutorials are optional sessions that can be be viewed prior to testing sessions. Students watch and listen to tutorials. Intro Screens are the first part of the Listening and Reading Tests. Students interact with these screens; the screens include practice items.  WIDA Consortium /  MetriTech\n\nFor all domains: Test Administrators should have a computer with internet connectivity, logged in to the TAI.  For Listening, Reading, and Writing administration: Test Administrators should ensure that the testing room has enough computers (or space for computers if students are using laptops), each connected to the internet. For Speaking Administration: Test administrators should sit next to the student, so the computer screen is visible to the TA and student. Test Administrators should be on the side with the mouse (as applicable).   Setting up the Testing Room (1 of 2) WIDA Consortium /  MetriTech\n\nTraining Objectives To understand the purposes, organization, and administration procedures of WIDA MODEL   Online   for Grades 1–12. To understand the reasons and procedures for administering WIDA MODEL Screener. To know how to record and interpret scores. WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nPost a  “ Testing: Please Do Not Disturb ”  sign outside the door Provide reading materials for students who finish early Setting up the Testing Room (2 of 2) WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nWIDA MODEL   Speaking Domain Test WIDA Consortium / MetriTech",
