  {
    "id": "78321a4a-ed49-4611-9c01-cafa68b9f772",
    "title": "Administering WIDA MODEL Online: Grades 1–12 (Part 1/7)",
    "content": "Administering WIDA MODEL Online: Grades 1–12\n\nThe WIDA ELD Standards Standard 1 -  SIL : English language learners communicate for  SOCIAL AND INSTRUCTIONAL  purposes within the school setting. Standard 2  –  LoLA :  English language learners communicate information, ideas, and concepts necessary for academic success in the content area of  LANGUAGE ARTS. Standard 3 –  LoMA :  English language learners communicate information, ideas, and concepts necessary for academic success in the content area of  MATHEMATICS. Standard 4 –  LoSC :  English language learners communicate information, ideas, and concepts necessary for academic success in the content area of  SCIENCE. Standard 5  –  LoSS :  English language learners communicate information, ideas, and concepts necessary for academic success in the content area of  SOCIAL STUDIES. WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nEnglish Language Proficiency Levels 6 ENTERING EMERGING DEVELOPING EXPANDING 1 2 3 4 5 BRIDGING REACHING WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nPerformance Definitions for the Levels of English Language Proficiency WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nENTERING EMERGING DEVELOPING EXPANDING BRIDGING 1 2 3 4 5 Listening/Reading Step 2: Low Listening/Reading Step 2: Mid Listening/Reading Step 2: High WIDA Consortium / MetriTech  How WIDA MODEL Test Items Adapt to   Student Proficiency\n\nTest Administration Overview WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nTesting Materials &amp; Equipment Test Administrator Interface (TAI)  https://wida-model.metritechtesting.com Student Testing Platform-  accessed via Student Secure Browser, downloaded from the TAI Headphones Speaking Test Administrator Script  for the grade cluster being administered For Grades 1-2 and 3-5,  a   Writing Student Response Form for each student WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nTest Administrator Interface HTTPS://wida-model.metritechtesting.com WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nStudent Testing Platform WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nTraining Materials WIDA Consortium / MetriTech  Test Administration Manual :  Details administration procedures for all parts of the assessment Administering WIDA MODEL Online PowerPoint Summarizes the most important information about the assessment. Can be used by districts, schools, teachers who are training others on how to administer WIDA MODEL Online User’s Guide to the Test    Administrator Interface Detailed information about how to use all aspects of the TAI\n\nGrade-Level Cluster Specific Training Materials Writing Rater Training Manual  Provides anchor papers and additional writing samples to assist in rating student writing  Administering &amp; Scoring the WIDA MODEL Writing Section  Provides details about administering Writing and additional examples of student writing responses  Scoring the WIDA MODEL Speaking Section Includes benchmark speaking samples with rationales to assist with calibrating raters Practice Scoring WIDA MODEL Speaking Section  Includes additional speaking samples for independent practice WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nDo not post these materials to public websites or forums. Contains confidential information. Confidentiality Statement\n\nTest Security To maintain the validity of the WIDA  MODEL   assessment and the test results, it is important to keep all of the test materials confidential.  WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nAdministration Sequence WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nIndividual vs. Group Administration Speaking must be administered one-on-one. Listening, Writing, and Reading are group-administered tests. However, you can create test sessions with a single student. WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nScreener vs. Summative You must select which form of WIDA MODEL (Screener or Summative) the student is taking before creating test sessions.  Use the User’s Guide to the Test Administrator Interface for details on how to assign a test form to a student.\n\nAdministration Times Domain Test Approximate  Administration Time Administrative  Format Summative Screener Speaking Up to 15 minutes Up to 15 minutes Individual Listening Up to 30 minutes Up to 15 minutes Group  or Individual Writing Up to 30 minutes Up to 30 minutes Group  or Individual Reading Low: Up to 20 minutes Mid: Up to 25 minutes High: Up  to 25 minutes Up to 15 minutes Group  or Individual WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nTest Scheduling- Summative and Screener For scheduling purposes, test administration can be completed in four sessions conducted  no more than two days apart.  The sessions should be divided as follows:\t Session 1:  Speaking  Session 2 : Listening Session 3 : Writing Session 4 : Reading The Domain Tests must be administered in this order.  WIDA Consortium / MetriTech",
