  {
    "id": "a640793f-b5c3-4b9f-8411-77ded884a237",
    "title": "Administering WIDA MODEL Online: Grades 1–12 (Part 6/7)",
    "content": "Writing Domain Test: Quick Score After the student completes the Writing Domain Test, the TA skims over the student ’ s writing (either typed or handwritten) and establishes an initial rating (Quick Score) of High, Mid, or Low. The Quick Score scoring criteria is located under  Test Session Progress Monitoring WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nEntering Writing Scores WIDA Consortium / MetriTech  Once the student has completed testing – select  Manage Students  from the  Students  menu Select the student to be scored In the Test History table, in the “Scoring” column, click on the link to add the Part B Final Score. If you need to add a score for Part A, click on that link after you’ve scored Part B.\n\nEntering Writing Scores Review and score the student writing according to the Writing Rubric For students in Grades 6-12, you can see the keyboarded response via the TAI.  For students in Grades 1-5, you must refer to the Student Response Form.  WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nEntering Writing Scores Select the solid score from the pull down menu on the left Select the adjustment score from the pull down menu on the right if an adjustment is appropriate WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nWIDA MODEL   Reading Domain Test WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nReading Domain Test Overview Format:  Multiple Choice Group administered Student records answers in the Student Test Platform Scoring : Test Platform captures student answers Time : Up to 25 minutes Required Materials: Student Test Platform, logged in for the student Headphones for each student Test Administrator Interface WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nReading Domain Test Procedures Follow the same steps as those outlined in the Listening section: Find the test session in the Test Administrator Interface Print the roster with student log in information Log each student in to the secure browser on their workstation After logging in, each student clicks on START TEST.  In the TAI, click on “Proctor” and then “Start Test” Under no circumstances may the TA read any passage, question, or response option to a student. Doing so would invalidate the test scores. WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nSample Reading Item  WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nEnding the Test WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nAfter Test Administration Log the students out of the Student Test Platform Make sure that all domains of the test have been completed.  In the TAI, select  Students  and then  Manage Students Comprehensively evaluate the student’s writing and input their score into the Test Administrator Interface WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nIdentification:  Identify   potential candidates for ELL and/or bilingual services Determine academic English Language Proficiency (ELP) level:  Find ELP levels of students new to the school or district Provide guidance in instructional placement:  Utilize results to place students into the type of instructional services and determine the amount of support needed Serve as an interim benchmark:  Provide data to inform instructional planning Purposes of WIDA MODEL Online – Summative  WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nInterpreting WIDA MODEL   Results WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nScore Reports Student Roster Report Individual Student Report Parent/Guardian Report WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nStudent Roster Report WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nIndividual Student Report WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nParent/Guardian Report WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nInterpreting WIDA MODEL   Results If WIDA MODEL   is being used to determine eligibility for ELL services, check with your state and district guidelines for placement criteria. Remember, WIDA MODEL   is only one of multiple criteria for decision making. Educator judgment should also be taken into account. Refer to  The English Language Learner CAN DO Booklet  and the  WIDA   English Language Proficiency Standards and Resource Guide (2007),  both available at  www.wida.us , for ideas on differentiating instruction for ELLs based on their performance on WIDA   assessments. WIDA Consortium / MetriTech\n\nQuestions or Comments? For more information, please contact the WIDA   Client Services Center: 866-276-7735 or  help@wida.us WIDA Consortium,  www.wida.us WIDA Consortium / MetriTech  MetriTech, Inc., www.MetriTech.com\n\nMODEL Summative vs. MODEL Screener   WIDA Consortium / MetriTech  Purpose Summative Screener Identification of  a student needing ELL services Yes Yes Determine  a student’s ELP level on the WIDA scale Yes Yes Provide guidance on the amount and type of English language  support that may be needed   Yes No To serve  as an interim benchmark assessment Yes No To exit  a student from and ELL program* Yes No *Information about a student’s English proficiency level obtained from taking the WIDA MODEL summative assessment may be used as part of the decision‐making process to exit a student from ELL services. It should not be the sole factor in making this important decision .",
