    "title": "Debrief: Eden Prairie WebbAlign DOK PD February 9, 2023",
    "content": "Title: Debrief: Eden Prairie WebbAlign DOK PD February 9, 2023\n\nContent: Debrief: Eden Prairie WebbAlign DOK PD February 9, 2023\n\nOn Febrary 9, 2023, instructional coaches from Eden Prairie Schools participated in a 6-hr professional learning session facilitated by Sara Christopherson, Director of WebbAlign. The leadership team and benefit from established norms that promote constructive discussion.\n\nTo what extent did you find the work with standards arranged by anchor area and proficiency scale to be helpful? Please explain a little...and give examples if possible.\n\nVery helpful in terms of explanation to teachers\n\nI found it helpful, as we move from state standard to classroom practice this is an important process to ensure that learning experiences and assessment of learning are aligned with the learning that is expected.\n\nVery helpful. What really helped was of there was debate or lack of clarity, think about what you want to communicate to teachers.\n\nI think it is always helpful to have collective dialog with one another to build our continued understanding.\n\nI think it is helpful to start to ensure that we are aligning curriculum and instruction to the complexity in the standards, rather than only pushing teachers to think about the rigorous tasks we can offer our students.\n\nVery helpful to better connect how these relate\n\nVery. I appreciated unpacking the difference between standards and tasks and the way all align.\n\nI enjoyed the first activity of comparing and naming the different levels of DOK. That helped me see it across contexts and get a better understanding and definition for each. I think the intent of standards is up for interpretation, so it gets tricky to accurately identify the levels without conversation.\n\nI found it helpful to unpack the learning in that way. I think I still have questions especially as I am very engrained in this work, I am wrestling with thinking through the aspects that seem to be left for interpretation. I think spending more time with it will certainly help.\n\nVery helpful, this is work we need to do if we want to build alignment and consistency in our district\n\nAny other feedback or comments are welcomed here!\n\nThank you! Very worthwhile.\n\nThank you\n\nThank you!\n\nThanks for allowing time for productive struggle\n\nThank you for your time!\n\nWisconsin Center for Education Products &amp; Services\n\n1213 N. Sherman Ave., #322   Madison, WI 53704  877-272-5593   WebbAlign@wceps.org   www.webbalign.org\n\nWisconsin Center for Education Products &amp; Services\n\n1213 N. Sherman Ave., #322   Madison, WI 53704  877-272-5593   info@wceps.org   www.wceps.org",
