  {
    "id": "19d0dc4a-12d3-49de-b326-b1182fd9f885",
    "title": "A directory of the Proposal Submission Requirements is given below. (Part 5/7)",
    "content": "Team meeting with Collaborative Director and other stakeholders to reflect on school year 2025–2026 and plan for school year 2026–2027.\n\nSection E – Supplier Profile\n\nA. The Wisconsin Center for Education Products &amp; Services (WCEPS) was founded November 23rd, 2010 by friends of the University of Wisconsin-Madison. The first full-time employee came on board in June of 2011.\n\nB. WCEPS meets a growing demand for bringing education research and development to the general public through our partnership with the University of Wisconsin-Madison, a world-class research institution. WCEPS is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization located at 1213 N Sherman Ave #322, Madison, WI 53704. We offer a range of educational products and services including CARE Coaching, WebbAlign, and the Comprehensive Assessment of Leadership for Learning (CALL). We employ 12 full-time staff and contract with dozens of experts in the field of education across the United States.\n\nC. The main contacts for work with Denver Public Schools will be Yvonne Williams, Vice President of Educator Engagement, Sara Christopherson, Director of WebbAlign, Margarita Marrero, Associate Director of CARE Coaching, Dr. Ryan Rumpf, Lead CARE Coach, and Colleen LeCompte, CARE Coach based in Denver. Matt Messinger, Executive Director of WCEPS, supports this work. Our team specializes in advancing school initiatives, with a focus on promoting educational system coherence and equipping teachers with strategies and tools to support all learners. After initial goal-setting work, we will identify the specific Coaches who will best support the needs of Denver Public Schools.\n\nResumes of key leadership are provided as an attachment to this proposal. Brief bios of key staff are provided below.\n\nYvonne Williams, M.S. Bilingual Education, is Vice President of Educator Engagement at WCEPS. Yvonne leads a team of 35 highly skilled coaches who support schools across the country in implementing WCEPS programs, providing tailored guidance and fostering lasting growth. Yvonne’s personal and professional journey is a testament to resilience and passion. Born in Chihuahua, Mexico, she moved to the United States at age 5, her experiences as an English language learner shaped her commitment to a positive impact in the field of education. With over 30 years in the field, Yvonne has worked with diverse student populations across all grade levels, PK to high school, advocating for the success of learners and their families.\n\nPrior to her current role, Yvonne spent three transformative years at WIDA as a Professional Learning Specialist, contributing to educator development on a global scale. She is also the architect of a nationally recognized coaching program at WCEPS, designed to provide ongoing, collaborative support for educators, moving beyond traditional professional development to foster lasting change in classrooms. While guiding the coaching work to include university credit.\n\nSara Christopherson, M.S. Curriculum and Instruction, is Director of WebbAlign. Sara has worked with assessment developers, educational publishers, and teachers on instructionally embedded assessments, interim assessment, and summative assessments since 2001. Drawing on her background in curriculum and instruction, as well as communications and educational publishing, Sara led the build-out of a popular professional development program, offered through WCEPS, to help educators, educational publishers, assessment developers, and other stakeholders to enhance and strengthen their use of Depth of Knowledge (DOK), understanding of alignment, interpretation of curriculum standards, and overall assessment literacy in support of a coherent system that supports all learners.  Sara is an active participant in the ongoing conversations in the field and presents regularly at national conferences and meetings.\n\nMargarita Marrero, M.S. Educational Adminstration, is Associate Director of CARE Coaching at WCEPS. Margarita has 16 years of experience in public education with a passion and focus on improving school systems to integrate literacy and content instruction to provide access and equity to English Learners. Her experience includes serving as a secondary math consultant for the Region 19 Education Service Center in El Paso, Texas. She has taught Spanish and math at a dual-language elementary school in Miami, Florida, as well as high school math in El Paso, Texas. She has served on campus leadership teams as an instructional coach for a public high school and as an assistant principal for a 6-12 all-girls college preparatory public school.",
