  {
    "id": "d49cfc8f-5eac-408a-9f50-f6ec3d0d2761",
    "title": "Proposal: WebbAlign DOK Professional Learning for (Part 1/2)",
    "content": "Proposal: WebbAlign DOK Professional Learning for\n\nFayette County Public Schools Career &amp; Technical Education Teachers - School Year 2021-2022\n\nFayette County Public Schools Contact: Lisa Collins, Director of Career &amp; Technical Education (collins.lisa@mail.fcboe.org; 770-500-0445)\n\nWebbAlign Contact: Sara Christopherson, Director of WebbAlign (sara.christopherson@wceps.org; 608-698-1966)\n\nProposal below. Adjustments, additions, clarifications, etc. are welcome for all steps.\n\nParticipants\n\nSchedule\n\nGoals and Proposed Plan\n\nLisa, all CTE educators (~70)\n\nJuly 27, 2021\n\nGoals: Collect pre-session perspectives on topics related to complexity and DOK. Use pre-reading materials and discussion prompts to start small group conversations about DOK.\n\nPlan: Provide materials via online webspace. Teachers will access materials on their own devices, read, respond individually to questions, and then discuss responses during their July planning meeting. Sara will provide Lisa with recorded introduction to help kick off the work.\n\nSara, Lisa, all CTE educators (~70)\n\nSeptember 7, 2021\n\n8:15 am – 3:30 pm ET\n\nGoals: Introduce/review DOK and contextualize its use within an aligned standards-based education system; work toward calibration of participant understanding and application of DOK. During small group work time, teams will use a consensus process to assign DOKs to the standards for their course(s). If time allows, groups can use the DOK lens to start to look at scope and sequence components.\n\nPlan: Conduct a remote interactive workshop followed by supported small group work time.\n\nLisa, all CTE educators (~70)\n\nIn advance of March 15\n\nGoals: Share information about basic assessment literacy including assessment purpose and design, score interpretation and use, etc. with a focus on the DOK lens to help promote alignment and to separate complexity from other interfering factors. Provide item/task writing tips and best practices, along with examples.\n\nPlan: Teachers complete self-paced online modules (2-3 hours) related to basic assessment literacy and item-writing best practices.\n\nSara, Lisa, all CTE educators (~70)\n\nMarch 15, 2022\n\n8:15 am – 3:30 pm ET\n\nGoals: Continue to work toward calibration of participant understanding and application of DOK by using DOK to evaluate assessment items with a focus on coherence/alignment. During small group work time, teachers will make progress on unit assessments (specifics TBD after discussion with Lisa).\n\nPlan: Conduct an in-person interactive workshop followed by supported small group work time.\n\nDebriefing phone call\n\nSpring 2022\n\nDebrief of SY2021-2022 work, plan for SY2022-2023.\n\nLinks for online materials to come. For all sessions, teachers should bring a device they can use to access online PD materials. They also need to be able to access their standards, scope and sequence documents, and any existing unit assessment materials.\n\nIn-person sessions on September 7, 2021 and March 15, 2022 will be held at:\n\nCenter of Innovation\n\n440 Hood Avenue\n\nFayetteville, GA, 30214\n\nScreen/projector and audio required for in-person sessions with IT support available if needed. Ideally, teachers would be seated at tables in 4-5 person groups to facilitate small group discussions during the interactive presentation. For team work time, groups can remain in the same room or move into separate rooms if preferred.\n\nContext:\n\nThe overarching goals of this work are grounded in continuous improvement and fostering of teamwork + rich conversations across the district for CTE teachers, similar to the types of collaborative work that occurs in PLCs. In the 2021-2022 school year, teachers will work together, using common assessments as an anchor for their conversations on continuous improvement. Use of DOK will help to focus teachers on standards interpretation and alignment of assessments with the standards (and, later, other components of the curriculum, too). In the 2022-2023 school year, teachers will continue to refine unit assessments, and expand their focus to (begin to) include relationships between standards, learning targets, essential questions, activities, rubrics, etc within their scope and sequence documents, revising as needed. Work may occur online and/or in person.\n\nProposal: WebbAlign DOK Professional Learning for\n\nFayette County Public Schools Career &amp; Technical Education Teachers March 20, 2023\n\nFayette County Public Schools Contact: James Stanford, Coordinator, Career &amp; Technical Education (stanford.james@fcboe.org; 770-716-1209)\n\nWebbAlign Contact: Sara Christopherson, Director of WebbAlign (sara.christopherson@wceps.org; 608-698-1966)\n\nProposal below. Adjustments, additions, clarifications, etc. are welcome for all steps.\n\nParticipants\n\nSchedule\n\nGoals and Proposed Plan\n\nSara, James\n\nIn advance of March session",
