    "id": "2149e26e-7411-41e7-b781-f5d08f4e1c0a",
    "title": "2022 _WIDA MODEL Paper for Licensing-FINAL-PWC (Part 6/9)",
    "content": "Thematic Organization Test items for WIDA MODEL™ are organized into sets of 3-4 questions based on a topic or unifying theme. Items within the set progressively become more linguistically demanding. 27\n\nSequence of Administration        Page 4\n\nSequence of Administration\n\nhttps://bit.ly/MODELPAPER\n\nIndividual &amp; Group Administration Grades 1-2:  ALL Domains: 1 on 1\n\nAdministration Times 31\n\nRead each item as scripted.  Read all  bolded  text (in  black  and  blue  items).                     Read the script at a steady pace, following the pause guidelines in the script. Using the Script\n\nListening Script 33 Part A: Classroom\tL Look at the big picture .  Point to the picture.   It is a picture of a classroom.  PAUSE. Use the picture to help you answer the questions. Go to the top of the next page.  Not find number 1. Look at the small pictures below number 1. Pause to make sure the student is in the right place. If he or she is not, direct the student to number 1. Number 1 The children write with a pencil.  PAUSE. Find the picture of the pencil. Record the student response in the Student Response Booklet. If necessary, say:  Point to the picture that goes with what I say. Begin reading here. Read the  bold  text aloud. Do NOT read non-bolded text. Indicates level  (low, mid or high) Bold blue  text should be read aloud Begin each item by reading the  bolded  number aloud.  During the testing session, if the student does not respond as expected, use this scripting.\n\nSpeaking Script 34 T1 Q1: (Point to the BOOK)  What is this? Q2: (Point to the APPLE)  What is this? Q3: (Point to SCISSORS)  What are these? Q4: (If necessary)  What other things do you see in this picture? EXPECT Singles words and phrases; highest frequency language; comprehensible when memorized. Score student response in the Student Response Booklet. This shows the proficiency level of this speaking task. Unlike other bolded text, do not read this aloud Multiple questions per task are in  bolded blue text. EXPECT box show expectations at the word/phrase, sentence, and discourse dimension Do NOT read non-bolded text.\n\nMoving On Criteria 35\n\nSetting up the Room TESTING:  Do Not Disturb\n\nMODEL Screener is denoted with an orange bar on the page,  as seen in the margin of Test Administrator Script on the left. Materials for MODEL Screener\n\nThis placement box shows the test administrator what to do during administration of MODEL Screener after the student is finished with writing and has taken Reading Step 1 Placement Boxes for MODEL Screener 38\n\nTest Administration Manual Section 1: Introduction Test Components Domain Tests and Sequence Section 2: Accessibility and Accommodations Page 5\n\nObjectives: Participants will be able to Discuss the features of WIDA MODEL  Describe the procedures for test administration Explain test administration and scoring for: Speaking, Listening, Writing &amp; Reading Create and generate Score Reports for WIDA MODEL Paper 4 Page 3\n\nAccommodations  Test Directions Presentation Format Setting Format Timing/Scheduling Response Format Other Test Administration Considerations 40\n\nAdministering the  Speaking  Domain for  WIDA MODEL Paper\n\nSpeaking Domain Format :  Individually administered in an adaptive interview format Time :  Up to 15 minutes per student Scoring Resources :  Speaking Rubric and EXPECT Boxes Scoring :  Meets, Approaches or ?\n\nSpeaking Script Grade Cluster Specific Read each item as scripted Use only English Scripted parts should  not  be written out for students Follow the pacing guidelines 43\n\nSpeaking Domain Required Materials Test Administrator Script Student Response Booklet Two sharpened pencils 44 Page 5\n\nMODEL Speaking Test Navigation Begin the Speaking Section by administering Part A, T1 It is mandatory to administer at least T1 for each part. Score for each task (as a whole) determines whether the next task is administered. Test ends when response fails to meet expectations.  45\n\nMODEL Speaking Test Navigation Grades 1-5 Grades 6-12\n\nSpeaking Domain Test\n\nScoring Speaking 48 Definitions Meets Meets all task level expectations in quantity and quality Approaches Approaches task level expectations but falls short in quantity and/or quality; no response; response in a language other than English. ? Unsure if  response meets or approaches; Move on to the next task , and them go back to designate “Meets” or “Approaches”\n\nRecording Scores 49 Page 6 Parts and Task Levels Scores\n\nWIDA MODEL Assessment\n\nAll questions in a task aim to elicit speech at one particular proficiency level Tasks include multiple questions Test ends when response fails to meet expectations at a given level Speaking Rubric\n\nSpeaking Rubric Page 28",
