    "content": "Task Level 3 Expectations Linguistic Complexity Vocabulary Usage Language Control Simple and expanded oral sentences; responses show emerging complexity used to add detail General and some specific language related to the content area; may search for needed vocabulary at times When communicating in sentences, is generally comprehensible and fluent; communication may from time to time be impeded by searching for language structures or by phonological, syntactic, or semantic errors, especially when attempting more complex oral discourse\n\nLevel 3 Task – Grades 1-2 (Clearly point out the HAT, the SCARF, and the GLOVES.) Now look at the hat, the scarf, and the gloves. Q1:  Do these things go together?  (Pause) (If “Yes”)  How do they go together? (If “No”)  Why don’t they go together? Q2: (If necessary)  How are they different? Q3: (If necessary)  Can you tell me anything else?   (OR)  Can you give me more details?   Response 1:",
