    "id": "5e9f1738-7b5b-49a3-88ef-f0facf2b3ed5",
    "title": "2022 _WIDA MODEL Paper for Licensing-FINAL-PWC (Part 7/9)",
    "content": "The scoring sheet should be filled out for each task administered to the student. Any task not administered should be left blank. Record Scores in the Speaking Scoring Table If a “?” is marked for a task,  administer the following task and return to mark the one with a “?” with a score (Meets or Approaches); it is not necessary to erase the mark in the “?” column. Page 6\n\nSample Speaking Script and Picture Cue This is what the student sees on the screen This is what the test administrator reads\n\nMODEL Paper: How to Read the                           Test Administrator Script Bold   black  text is read out loud Instructions are detailed within a set of parenthesis Instructions for scoring the student and advancing through the script are detailed in the EXPECT and MOVING ON boxes. 54\n\nProvide limited reinforcement of their oral responses. Give  nonjudgmental , concise encouragement such as,  “ Good job, ”  or  “ Okay. ” Anything you say should be positive, though never evaluative Reinforcing Student Responses\n\nAdministering the  Listening  Domain for  WIDA MODEL Paper\n\nListening Section  Format:   Multiple Choice Individually administered Student responds by pointing or saying letters Time:   Up to 30 minutes Scoring:   Answer Key Required Materials:  Student Response Booklet Test Administration Script Pencils Page 7\n\nConsists of:  Listening Step 1 and Step 2 Step 1 has four items – all students complete Step 2 has three starting points  (Low, Mid, or High) ,   determined from Speaking and Listening  Low is composed of 9 items Mid is composed of 12 items High is composed of 12 items Format of the Listening Section\n\nStudents:  Indicate their answers by pointing or saying the letter answer choice Test Administrators: Record student responses in the Listening Section of the Student Response Booklet Pause after an item is read Listening Section Procedures\n\nMODEL Paper Page 5\n\nListening Script Grades 3-5\n\nTest Administrators:  Record student responses in the Student Response Booklet.  Listening Step 1 Page 7\n\nNumber of correct answers on Listening Step 1 Number of Speaking tasks scored “Meets” Listening Step 2: Placement Criteria Placement guidelines are located in the Student Response Booklet Page 7\n\nRecord the student’s response as the items are administered. After the student completes the whole test, go back and score using the key in the scoring table. Listening Step 2: Scoring Page 7\n\nOccur at the beginning of the section, after the introduction Help students understand the structure of the test Are scripted and must be administered Are not scored Listening Section Practice Items\n\nAdministering the  Writing  Domain for  WIDA MODEL Paper\n\nFormat :   Constructed responses Time:  Up to 30 minutes Scoring:  “Quick Score” criteria (during)* and Writing Rubric (after) Writing Section Overview Page 8 *Quick score is only used to determine placement on the Reading domain assessment\n\nFormat:   Constructed responses Time:  Up to 30 minutes Scoring:  “Quick Score” criteria (during) and Writing Rubric (after) Writing Section Overview Page 8\n\nPart A *   Open-ended questions/prompts Student reads some text with the test administrator and responds in single words, phrases, or short sentences. Part B   Consists of a constructed response task designed to allow students to demonstrate their ability to write beyond single words and short phrases  Writing Section Organization *All students take Part A. If their responses include single words, phrases, or simple sentences, they move to Part B.\n\nACTIVITY: Writing Section Organization Find the Test Administration Manual. Turn to Section 4: Writing Section Administration and Scoring. Read through the section up to Administering Part B. Be prepared to share your most significant understanding or ask a clarifying question .\n\nMODEL Paper Page 5\n\nStudent Response Booklet Writing Item Part A-Grades 3-5 Test Administrator’s Script\n\nSample Writing Item Part B This is the story the student sees.  Test Administrator reads the prompt and story aloud to the student. 71\n\nStudent pages for planning and writing Sample Writing Script Part B\n\nScoring Writing Part B is scored first. Score Part A  if : Student does not advance to Part B. The response on Part B is not ratable.  Response in Part B receives a score of less than  3.\n\nAdministering the Reading  Domain for WIDA MODEL Paper\n\nFormat:    Multiple choice Administered individually or small groups (up to 5) Student records answers in the Student Response Booklet Scoring:  Answer keys in Test Administrator Manual Time:  Up to 25 minutes Reading Section Overview Page 9\n\nStep 1  composed of four items – all students complete Step 1 Step 2  has three starting points ( Low, Mid or High )  Placement is determined using the Writing Quick Score and results from Reading Step 1 Reading Step 2: Low is composed of 9 items Reading Step 2: Mid is composed of 12 items Reading Step 2: High is composed of 12 items Reading Section Format",
