  {
    "id": "52654aa9-fdf6-47d3-a73e-a79716c38eb6",
    "title": "Debrief: Eden Prairie WebbAlign DOK PD May 4, 2023",
    "content": "Title: Debrief: Eden Prairie WebbAlign DOK PD May 4, 2023\n\nContent: Debrief: Eden Prairie WebbAlign DOK PD May 4, 2023\n\nThe May 4 PD session included extended work time for participants to define and refine a focus for application of DOK to existing work. One group worked to add questions for use in the context of teacher evaluation that would help to focus attention on consideration of complexity of engagement for students as well as worked to think about follow-up supports depending on teacher responses. Another group worked to plan out an approach for assigning DOK to academic standards in order to anchor course development work as well as communication with teachers. A third group worked to incorporate a consideration of complexity of engagement with ideas related to building a thinking classroom. To what extent did you find the selected topic group work to be helpful? Please explain a little, give examples if possible, and share any ideas about ways in which group work could be more helpful for your practice.\n\nIt was nice to have choice and lots of time to work together and figure it out\n\nI found it helpful as it was relevant and contextual to our current situation. It feels good to move into a space of progress.\n\nAppreciated the opportunity to authentically apply to our current work\n\nSo appreciated the wrestle of these big concepts and collaboration among our tables and teams. I’m excited to continue to work through to find impactful and practical actions.\n\nReally helpful in that there was time to work through issues and how to put into practice. Even though we didn’t get a lot “done,” it was good to have that time to talk and think through\n\nIt was very helpful to engage in dialogue and wrestle around the utilization of DOK for particular purposes within the system. It allowed for opportunities to think about what goals need to be achieved and how to potentially engage in change initiatives.\n\nI appreciate the wrestle we had about difficulty, complexity and sophistication of thinking in the context of our math standards and the types of tasks we ask students to engage with. I found the time valuable and my understand deepened as a result of our collective work.\n\nIt helped me think of ideas on how to include elements of DOK, such as complexity in my specific questioning that I will use in conversations with teachers - this could lead to learning and more culturally proficient practices :)\n\nThe selected topic group work was extremely relevant and timely. We were able to spend time with the BTC framework and think about the intricacies in the planning and intentionality needed to make sure we have included rigor and authenticity, been mindful of increasing complexity and difficulty, and sophistication of thinking. Our table conversation was so helpful and our collective experiences and ideas were integral to my learning today. Thank you!\n\nAny other feedback or comments are welcomed here!\n\nReally appreciate all we’ve learned from you!!\n\nThanks for a thought provoking day!\n\nThanks! :)\n\nThank you!\n\nThank you for the complex learning activities - my brain has been effectively stretched and the teachers I work with will benefit from that :)\n\nWisconsin Center for Education Products &amp; Services\n\n1213 N. Sherman Ave., #322   Madison, WI 53704  877-272-5593   WebbAlign@wceps.org   www.webbalign.org\n\nWisconsin Center for Education Products &amp; Services\n\n1213 N. Sherman Ave., #322   Madison, WI 53704  877-272-5593   info@wceps.org   www.wceps.org",
    "document_type": "docx",
    "file_name": "Eden Prairie Debrief May 4 2023 Session_for AI tool training.docx",
