  {
    "id": "3b565adf-b94d-470f-95e3-0b41f22e2e04",
    "title": "WebbAlign DOK PD for Fayette County CTE: September 7, 2021 Session Evaluation Responses (Part 1/2)",
    "content": "WebbAlign DOK PD for Fayette County CTE: September 7, 2021 Session Evaluation Responses\n\nTotal responses: 49\n\nParticipants reported that the session greatly enhanced their understanding of DOK and helped them better understand the standards for their courses. Participants thought the online format for the PD was very well managed.\n\nIt was great to collaborate with my cohorts from the county.\n\nI was really pleased with this PD. It was very informative. I know so much more about DOK than I did at 8:30 am today.\n\nGreat Job!\n\nvery convenient!\n\nThe process was handled very well today.\n\nVery Beneficial\n\nThe online aspect was handled well. Breakout rooms allowed teachers of similar subjects to discuss DOK levels as they apply specifically to our standards.\n\neverything worked amazingly well\n\nWell done.\n\nIt worked well. Insightful conversations were had as a group and within breakout rooms.\n\nNo issues. Easy to move from group to group\n\nThe breakout rooms worked well for the purposes of the PD\n\nIt was very well managed. I liked having people give quick responses at the beginning and watching the words scroll by looking for patterns.\n\nThe zoom sessions worked great particularly when the PD leaders joined sessions to participate in unique and specific questions\n\nVery structured. Good explanation of the content.\n\nThe training was seamless and broken up nicely.\n\nIt was managed well. Thank you for the interactivity.\n\nWell organized PD\n\nI like that we were able to get into breakout rooms with other teachers in our pathway.\n\ngood\n\nVery effective.\n\nIt was informative and allowed everyone to remain safe.\n\nGreat information and useful\n\nIt was just as productive as in person.\n\nI think the online aspect when really well.\n\nI thought that Ms. Christopherson was quite clear on the expectations and the explanations of DOK, and I learned quite a bit .\n\nIt allowed everyone in a cluster to come together and work together.\n\nVery well organized. The speaker was effective and energetic.\n\nThe breakout sessions were helpful.\n\nI think it went smoothly and was informational.\n\n5. Which part of today’s session was most helpful for you? Explain why.\n\nDelving into the standards-We are both relatively new, so it was enriching.\n\nThe time in Breakout groups was the most helpful, particularly the afternoon one which was a smaller and more relevant group.\n\nGoing through the standards with common like teachers.\n\nDiscussion with breakout groups\n\nBreak out rooms\n\nOverview of process (top half)\n\ni enjoyed the whole group meeting\n\nUnderstanding the importance of complexity when distinguishing between the levels and working through a set of standards with district colleagues...after we agreed on a shared interpretation\n\nThe detailed discussion with break out group about assignment of DOKs.\n\nBreak down of the 4 DOK's\n\nThe afternoon session that allowed me to work with colleagues teaching the same standards was the most helpful in giving me more insight to our standards and how the DOK levels apply to each one.\n\ndifferentiating between DOK levels\n\nworking collaboratively with the other teachers\n\nBreak-out rooms with our content partners. Applying the DOK to our actual standards was very beneficial.\n\nThe breakout room conversation in the afternoon was most important - having discussion as to how DOK relates to our specific standards.\n\nProviding time for us to discuss with our team the first year course and the definitions of the levels\n\nDOK Conceptual Category Definitions\n\nWorking within the pathway to discuss DOK of standards.\n\nBreakout group discussions\n\nGoing through my course standards with my colleagues\n\nDeeper understanding of DOKs. When we develop assignments and assessments, we know better to apply the appropriate level of challenge or complexity,\n\nCollaborating with other teachers is always helpful.\n\nWorking with my county counterparts.\n\nGetting the knowledge as a whole group and then applying it with our content in small groups. Being able to discuss with our small group contents is so important.\n\nThe breakout sessions were most helpful\n\nHaving the breakout sessions.\n\nIt was great to have a conversation with peers to interpret the standards. interesting to hear how they interpret them.\n\nThe breakout sessions were productive.\n\nThe DOK definitions resource was probably the most helpful piece of information today.\n\ncollaborating\n\nAfternoon working with the group\n\nMorning Session. Getting the explanation of the different levels.\n\nThe further breakdown and discussion of how to evaluate the DOK of a standard.\n\nAfternoon to speak with counter parts\n\nDiscussing standards with colleagues\n\nassigning the levels to the elements\n\nThe ability to have the discussions about the standards with other teachers across the district as we don't have a common PLC.\n\nI think going though the DOK levels was really helpful.",
