  {
    "id": "ef20f46a-92d7-452d-9d18-1bd56bc1addf",
    "title": "WebbAlign Case Study for site_scc",
    "content": "Title: WebbAlign Case Study for site_scc\n\nContent: WCEPS uses diverse expertise to continue thought leadership in the field on topics of content alignment and Depth of Knowledge (DOK).  (OR) WCEPS uses diverse expertise to continue to evaluate and promote alignment in educational materials.  History  Dr. Norman Webb helped develop what is now the most widely used alignment methodology along with a tool for evaluating cognitive complexity through content analysis: the Depth of Knowledge (DOK) framework.  Attention to and evaluation of alignment helps promote coherence in education systems.  DOK is grounded in the language of today's academic content standards and helps to differentiate complexity from difficulty in educational expectations and tasks.  The DOK tool allows educators to communicate effectively, consistently and efficiently about the content complexity of learning expectations, instructional materials and assessment items.  Challenge  How can states, districts, schools, content developers, and others be supported in their use of DOK and Webb alignment methodologies?  Solution  WCEPS developed a program to continue the work of Dr. Norman Webb and his Depth of Knowledge framework.  Developed a brand – WebbAlign  ▪  Worked with attorneys to trademark WebbAlign  Developed the Depth of Knowledge (DOK) Partner Program for content developers:  ▪  Partners pay for annual training and content analysis  ▪  Once completed, they pay for the right to display this seal  Continued and expanded alignment work:  ▪  Providing content alignment analyses for states, content developers, and other stakeholders.  ▪  Continued participation at national meetings and conferences  Invested in creating professional learning to deliver to K-12 Schools:  ▪  Developed interactive PD for teachers, coaches, and administrators.  ▪  Supported schools in working toward  goals for improved student experience and outcomes.  Impact  As these offerings were implemented WebbAlign began to grow and increase impact. Since its inception, WebbAlign has supported:  eight productive DOK Partnerships  dozens of successful alignment studies, providing critical validity evidence and constructive feedback  well-received professional learning in collaboration with dozens of schools  WebbAlign has also continued to contribute to the field through:  over ten presentations at national conferences  formal and informal publications  hosting national expert panel to provide input and update key resources ",
