    "id": "90ccbae4-cfe8-4ae5-b183-0d8db81ce11c",
    "title": "Proposal: WebbAlign Professional Learning for (Part 1/3)",
    "content": "Proposal: WebbAlign Professional Learning for\n\nEden Prairie Schools\n\nEden Prairie Schools Main Contacts: Robb Virgin, Executive Director of Personalized Learning and Lisa Birno, Director of Curriculum and Learning (Lisa_Birno@edenpr.k12.mn.us)\n\nWebbAlign Main Contact: Sara Christopherson, Director of WebbAlign (sara.christopherson@wceps.org)\n\nProposal below. Adjustments, additions, clarifications, etc. are welcome for all steps.\n\nThe work outlined below constitutes a first phase of work with Eden Prairie Schools, focused on the overarching goal of building a shared foundation among leadership for conceptual understanding of the ideas of cognitive complexity and Depth of Knowledge (DOK). As part of this first phase, district stakeholders will provide input to collaboratively design subsequent phases of work. Subsequent phases will be focused on application to practice, customized for Eden Prairie Schools.\n\nParticipants\n\nSchedule\n\nGoals and Proposed Plan\n\nSara, Lisa, Robb\n\nCOMPLETED and ONGOING- Summer, 2022 and Fall, 2022\n\nGoals: Discuss high-level needs and potential plans PD sessions. Provide background and context for Eden Prairie Schools.\n\nPlan: phone call to discuss plans and preparations; additional calls as needed moving forward to identify specific goals and logistical needs\n\nSara, Lisa\n\nON HOLD – can include later if warranted\n\nGoals: Review and provide input on the language used within district materials related to curriculum planning to ensure consistency in messaging with future DOK PD.\n\nPlan: Preview materials in advance. Hold a 1-day remote meeting to debrief on any recommendations and suggested considerations, discuss any questions that arise, etc.\n\nSara, Lisa, Robb, teacher leaders\n\nDecember 8, 2022\n\nGoals: Introduce/review DOK and contextualize its use within an aligned (coherent) standards-based education system; work toward calibration of participant understanding and application of DOK; differentiate between difficulty and complexity; consider common misconceptions about DOK and their implications on teaching and learning.\n\nPlan: Conduct an interactive in-person workshop/meeting.\n\n~1 hr Debriefing phone call – Sara + Lisa and/or Robb\n\nFollowing December sessions – could be in-person on Dec 9 or via phone anytime\n\nDebrief of 2022 work, set plans for next-phase support.\n\nDistrict Information / Context for Work: Eden Prairie educators have been using DOK in the context of/along with the Rigor/Relevance matrix and a district-developed Authenticity Grid. Eden Prairie is fortunate to have strong leadership and vision through the Department for Personalized Learning as well as embedded support for teachers via Instructional Excellence Coordinators (IECs) who facilitate PLCs and assist with curriculum writing and instructional practices, etc. IECs also help support the effective implementation of district initiatives, including the use of DOK.\n\nAfter observing some differences in interpretations/misinterpretations, understanding, and use of Webb’s Depth of Knowledge (DOK), Eden Prairie reached out to the WebbAlign team of the non-profit Wisconsin Center for Education Products and Services (WCEPS). WCEPS is affiliated with the Wisconsin Center for Education Research (WCER) and is named after Dr. Norman Webb, who developed the DOK language system and serves as advisor to the WebbAlign program. WebbAlign can support Eden Prairie in shared goals of working toward more consistency in the use of DOK as intended by the developers. Professional learning (PL) will help to build a shared conceptual understanding of Webb’s DOK as a language system to evaluate and communicate about complexity in educational materials, help educators calibrate their interpretation of the DOK categories (levels) and foster appropriate and effective application of DOK to practice.",
