  {
    "id": "dbd67f32-cf72-4902-bfdf-042704857d4a",
    "title": "Proposal: WebbAlign Professional Learning for (Part 3/3)",
    "content": "After observing some differences in interpretations/misinterpretations, understanding, and use of Webb’s Depth of Knowledge (DOK), Eden Prairie reached out to the WebbAlign team of the non-profit Wisconsin Center for Education Products and Services (WCEPS). WCEPS is affiliated with the Wisconsin Center for Education Research (WCER) and is named after Dr. Norman Webb, who developed the DOK language system and serves as advisor to the WebbAlign program. WebbAlign can support Eden Prairie in shared goals of working toward more consistency in the use of DOK as intended by the developers. Professional learning (PL) will help to build a shared conceptual understanding of Webb’s DOK as a language system to evaluate and communicate about complexity in educational materials, help educators calibrate their interpretation of the DOK categories (levels) and foster appropriate and effective application of DOK to practice.\n\nFuture PL will include collaborative work time for educators to use DOK to evaluate the complexity of relevant academic standards, compare the DOK of standards with and derivative learning targets (and essential questions, etc. as applicable) within their planning materials (e.g. scope and sequence, lesson plans) adjusting as needed.\n\nCollaborative work time will focus overall on self-evaluation of materials to promote alignment or coherence between and among the standards, learning targets, activities, assignments, and other learning opportunities, and assessments.\n\nPlanning, follow-up, and check-in meetings as needed\n\nCustomization of sessions to Eden Prairie needs\n\nSession development and preparation (spring working meeting + 1-day PL sessions for up to 50 participants)\n\nMaterials can be provided electronically (or printed by Eden Prairie) at no cost. If desired, WCEPS/WebbAlign can print and ship handouts at cost.\n\nScreen/projector and audio required for in-person sessions with IT support available if needed. Ideally, participants would be seated at tables in 4-5 person groups to facilitate small group discussions during the interactive presentation.\n\nThe work outlined below constitutes the second session of a first phase of work with Eden Prairie Schools, focused on the overarching goal of building a shared foundation among leadership for conceptual understanding of the ideas of cognitive complexity and Depth of Knowledge (DOK). As part of this first phase, district stakeholders will provide input to collaboratively design subsequent phases of work. Subsequent phases will be focused on application to practice, customized for Eden Prairie Schools.\n\nParticipants\n\nSchedule\n\nGoals and Proposed Plan\n\nCont’d from Dec. 8, 2022\n\nFebruary 9, 2023\n\nGoals: Continue to build understanding of DOK and calibrate on its use. Differentiate between task difficulty and complexity, including the way(s) in which text/context complexity differs from the complexity of engagement with the text/context; use DOK to promote coherence within existing anchor standards/benchmarks/proficiency levels documents.\n\nPlan: Conduct an interactive in-person workshop/meeting.\n\nDebriefing phone call – Sara + Lisa\n\nFollowing Feb sessions\n\nDebrief of work to date, set plans for next-phase support.\n\nTravel expenses\n\nPlanning, follow-up, and check-in meetings as needed\n\nCustomization of session to Eden Prairie needs\n\nWisconsin Center for Education Products &amp; Services\n\n1213 N. Sherman Ave., #322   Madison, WI 53704  877-272-5593   WebbAlign@wceps.org   www.webbalign.org\n\nWisconsin Center for Education Products &amp; Services\n\n1213 N. Sherman Ave., #322   Madison, WI 53704  877-272-5593   info@wceps.org   www.wceps.org",
