  {
    "id": "66d5273a-56e9-4d3d-b80d-999244ab4fe8",
    "title": "Proposal: WebbAlign Professional Learning for (Part 2/3)",
    "content": "Future PL will be planned in collaboration with Eden Prairie leadership with a goal of incorporating DOK into existing systems and processes – e.g. curriculum review cycles, lesson planning / PLC work, teacher evaluation conversations (that may include consideration of planned vs enacted lessons), assessment planning and evaluation, etc. Future PL may include collaborative work time for educators to use DOK to evaluate the complexity of relevant academic standards, compare the DOK of standards with and derivative learning targets (and essential questions, etc. as applicable) within their planning materials (e.g. scope and sequence, lesson plans, assessments – of all types) adjusting as needed, consider strategies for promoting complex engagement for all students, including eliminating difficulty barriers to allow access to the intended task complexity. These considerations apply across special education considerations, including for advanced learners. In all cases, we are working to provide access to relevant complex work. For advanced learners, we want to make sure we are allowing opportunities for more complex engagement and not just harder work. Collaborative work time will focus overall on supporting ongoing improvement through self-evaluation of materials to promote alignment or coherence between and among the standards, learning targets, activities, assignments, and other learning opportunities, and assessments.\n\nA possible next-step session would include two days with coaches, with time for both calibration work and standards analyses through the DOK lens.\n\nMaterials can be provided electronically at no cost. Screen/projector and audio required for in-person sessions with IT support available if needed. Ideally, participants would be seated at tables in 4-5 person groups to facilitate small group discussions during the interactive presentation. For purposes of both efficiency and camaraderie, it is recommended to provide lunch for participants.\n\nThe work outlined below constitutes a first phase of work with Eden Prairie Schools, focused on the overarching goal of building a shared foundation for conceptual understanding of the ideas of cognitive complexity and Depth of Knowledge (DOK). As part of this first phase, district stakeholders will provide input to collaboratively design subsequent phases of work. Subsequent phases will be focused on application to practice, customized for Eden Prairie Schools.\n\nParticipants\n\nSchedule\n\nGoals and Proposed Plan\n\nSara, Lisa\n\nSpring-Summer, 2022\n\nGoals: Come to consensus on high-level plans for summer 2022 in-person PD sessions and the structure/dates for SY2022-2023 sessions.\n\nPlan: phone call to discuss plans and preparations; additional calls as needed moving forward to identify specific goals and logistical needs\n\nSara, Lisa\n\nAugust 12, 2022\n\nGoals: Review and provide input on the language used within district materials related to curriculum planning to ensure consistency in messaging with future DOK PD.\n\nPlan: Preview materials in advance. Hold a 1-day remote meeting to debrief on any recommendations and suggested considerations, discuss any questions that arise, etc.\n\nSara, Lisa, IECs, open invite for district administrators (Total TBD – up to ~50 participants)\n\nSeptember 22, 2022\n\nGoals: Introduce/review DOK and contextualize its use within an aligned (coherent) standards-based education system; work toward calibration of participant understanding and application of DOK; differentiate between difficulty and complexity; consider common misconceptions about DOK and their implications on teaching and learning.\n\nPlan: Conduct an interactive in-person workshop/meeting.\n\n~1 hr Debriefing phone call – all stakeholders\n\nFollowing September sessions\n\nDebrief of Summer / Dall 2022 work, set plans for next-phase support.\n\nDistrict Information / Context for Work: Eden Prairie educators have been using DOK in the context of/along with the Rigor/Relevance matrix and a district-developed Authenticity Grid. Eden Prairie is fortunate to have Instructional Excellence Coordinators (IECs) that provide support for teachers (via PLCs ) with curriculum writing and instructional practices, etc. IECs also support the effective implementation of district initiatives, including the use of DOK.",
