  {
    "id": "d505c129-19e5-4c6a-b266-18d812e7bda0",
    "title": "Proposal: WebbAlign Professional Learning for (Part 2/2)",
    "content": "In earlier discussions, Patrice and Sara discussed an overarching goal to move forward existing work with performance assessments. Two main goals were 1) to begin calibrating conceptual understanding of alignment and cognitive complexity and 2) to draft and trial a transferrable framework that supports evaluation of performance assessment tasks with attention to alignment considerations. A framework could help promote consideration of validity evidence based on test content (along with other important evaluative considerations). For example, a framework might help teachers focus on evaluation of the relationships between the inferences that are intended to be made based on the assessment task(s), the content of the tasks themselves (and the corresponding opportunities provided for students), and the intended assessment target(s). The proposed framework could be shared by SILs, principals, APs, and instructional coaches at the schools to help support these efforts. Development of this tool will be informed by review of existing district materials as well as input from Patrice. If this work is still of interest, it could be a focus for SY2025–2026.\n\nWisconsin Center for Education Products &amp; Services\n\n1213 N. Sherman Ave., #322   Madison, WI 53704  877-272-5593   WebbAlign@wceps.org   www.webbalign.org\n\nWisconsin Center for Education Products &amp; Services\n\n1213 N. Sherman Ave., #322   Madison, WI 53704  877-272-5593   info@wceps.org   www.wceps.org",
