  {
    "id": "02cafb82-c301-4340-91a2-3240ee585b72",
    "title": "Proposal: WebbAlign Professional Learning for (Part 1/2)",
    "content": "Proposal: WebbAlign Professional Learning for\n\nSchool District of Greenfield\n\nSchool District of Greenfield Main Contact:\n\nPatrice Ball, Director of Secondary Learning (pball@greenfield.k12.wi.us)\n\nWebbAlign Main Contact:\n\nSara Christopherson, Director of WebbAlign (sara.christopherson@wceps.org)\n\nProposal below. Adjustments, additions, clarifications, etc. are welcome for all steps.\n\nDistrict Information / Context for Work: Greenfield is fortunate to have an established culture of ongoing improvement and collaboration, strong leadership and vision, as well as embedded support for teachers via Secondary Instructional Leaders (SILs) who help with effective implementation of district initiatives, including recent work with performance assessments. As part of these efforts, Greenfield educators worked with Jay McTighe, using the UBD framework for development. To date, work on these assessment tasks has focused on important considerations including authentic learning / connections to the real world, student engagement, and differentiating and personalizing tasks to incorporate student voice (not just choice).\n\nGoals for ongoing improvement include attending to vertical articulation of tasks across the grades 6–12 sequence and attention to validity evidence based on test content. It has been observed that there is a need to ensure that the tasks remain anchored in the intended purposes and uses of the assessments, closely linked to the assessment targets. Because these assessments are being used to make consequential decisions (at least in some cases) it is particularly important that the assessments are meaningful and appropriate to support these decisions.\n\nA 2-day Greenfield educator-driven “unconference” style work session is scheduled for 8 am to 4 pm on August 20 and 21, 2025. Educators will engage in a variety of interactions during these two days, based on self-identified goals/needs. Patrice Ball, Director of Secondary Learning, requests facilitation/support for a space focused on consideration of cognitive demand and DOK consistency. A portion of August 20 will be designed to support coordinated work that can promote calibration between/among Greenfield educator teams in their understanding of complexity and the use of DOK as a common language. This work will be grounded in activities that help to surface educators’ ideas and promote discussion of differences in perspective. For the remainder of August 20 and all of August 21, the WCEPS/WebbAlign leads/coaches will provide collaborative support for educators as they work. (Details to be decided collaboratively.)\n\nTo help our team prepare, Patrice will share examples of unit assessments/plans. Most educators will be working on common formative assessments this summer.\n\nCost: Total cost for work outlined in this proposal is $13,250 inclusive of:\n\nTwo WCEPS team members facilitating / supporting work on Aug. 20-21, 8am – 4 pm\n\nFacilitator preparation time\n\nAll travel expenses (regional travel only)\n\nPlanning, follow-up, and check-in meetings as needed\n\nParticipants\n\nSchedule\n\nGoals and Proposed Plan\n\nSara + Patrice\n\nPeriodic planning meetings, as needed\n\nGoals: Plan for August 20 and 21 in-person work\n\nPlan: Discuss and decide on overall goals and structure for summer working meetings.\n\nSara, Tim C., Patrice (Optional)\n\nOnline meetings to prepare for August work\n\nGoals: Prepare for August 20 and 21 in-person work\n\nPlan: Review and discuss shared materials, plan for summer working meetings.\n\nSara, Tim C., Patrice, Secondary Instructional Leaders (SILs)\n\nAugust 20 and 21\n\n8 am –4 pm\n\n(In person)\n\nGoals: Contextualize idea of complexity and use of DOK within an aligned (coherent) standards-based education system; work toward calibration of participant understanding and application of DOK; differentiate between difficulty and complexity; consider common misconceptions about DOK and their implications on teaching and learning. Provide personalized support for educators as they work.\n\nPlan: Conduct an interactive in-person workshop/meeting; provide personalized support for educators.\n\nSara + Patrice\n\nFollowing August sessions\n\nDebrief of August work, set plans for SY2025–2026.",
