hink repetition means?  DOK 1 Highlight all the words you see repeated in the sentences below.  They didn’t hurry now for they were so very, very tired! And they were cross—oh so cross!  DOK 2 DOK 1  Read the sentences above. Explain what is happening in the story.  What is the literary device called repetition?  Many different systems exist to describe content complexity. These systems…  are used in different contexts.  are used for different purposes.  have different numbers of levels/categories.  Would one of these systems work in the context of evaluation of alignment?  Bloom’s Revised Taxonomy (2001) Cognitive Process Dimension  OLD  NEW  Knowledge  Remember  Comprehension  Understand  Application  Apply  Analysis  Analyze  Synthesis  Evaluate  Evaluation  Create  DOK Framework  Bloom’s Taxonomy  Based in cognitivism and contemporary understandings about the nature of learning  Based in behaviorism, with revisions intended to reflect current understandings of learning.  Based on a constructivist model of learning. Reflects a contemporary understanding of learning as a process of linking to networks of ideas. All categories of complexity are considered valuable as they combine to build proficiency.  Structure implies that the higher the level of complexity, the more valuable the performance.  Assignment of DOK takes into account actions as well as the structure of the content area, the  content students engage with, students’ prior knowledge, and students’ existing conceptual ecology.  Focused on using actions (verbs) to assign levels of complexity.  Definitions for each DOK category are tailored to different subjects, recognizing the inherent differences in learning processes, approaches, goals, etc. between and among disciplines.  Does not distinguish between subject areas.  Differentiates complexity from difficulty (and from other related factors)  Does not differentiate between difficulty and complexity.  Has a rationale for the number of levels. (Necessary and sufficient)  Has no rationale for the number of levels.  Hess’ Cognitive Rigor Matrix  Bloom’s  Revised  Taxonomy of  Cognitive  Process  Dimensions  Webb’s Depth-of-Knowledge (DOK) Levels  Level 1  Recall &  Reproduction  Level  Thinking/ Reasoning  Level 4 Extended Thinking  Remember  Understand  Apply  Analyze  Evaluate  Create  Source: https://www.karin-hess.com  →  Through the DOK lens, learning is NOT conceptualized as a linear progression of lowhigh complexity.  Why use DOK to evaluate complexity?    Rationale for 4 levels    Can be used reliably, consistently    Based on contemporary learning models    Takes into account multiple factors that contribute to content complexity    Recognizes inherent differences in the structure of different disciplines  Provides a common language that applies to today’s education landscape",
