    "content": "Building Community with Multilingual Learners through Family Engagement  Yvonne Williams  Director of ML Educator Engagement  WCEPS  Overview  This session explores the value and components of effective family partnerships across the school community. Allowing educators to reflect on the definition of engagement, our own experiences, and how to consider who defines engagement. Creating an environment that leverages families as a reliable resource to engage students, support families, and honor culture creates a successful school vision. After completing this workshop, participants will be able to:  Define Family Engagement• Consider research that supports family engagement • Create a vision/mission for family engagement for class/school•  © 2024 CARE Coaching  CARE Coaching  A Brief History of the Wisconsin Center  for Education Products and Services  Who’s in the room?  Elementary teachers PK-5 Middle School teachers 6-8 High School teachers 9-12 Elementary Admin Middle School Admin H...",
