    "content": "Designing Multi-Modal Instruction to Meet the Needs of Multilingual Learners  CARE Coaching  A Brief History of the Wisconsin Center for Education Products and Services  Overview  To meet the needs of multilingual learners, educators must provide multimodal instruction using Universal Design for Learning principles and scaffolding techniques to make grade-level learning accessible to students at all levels of English language proficiency.  After engaging in this learning opportunity, participants will be able to:  ▪  Describe the principles of UDL and their connection to scaffolding techniques  ▪  Develop and deliver multimodal instruction  ▪  Design learning opportunities that leverage learners’ strengths, interests and preferences  Reflect and Plan  People forget 40% of what they have learned after 20 minutes and 77% of what they learned after six days.  (http://www.festo-didactic.co.uk/gb-en/news/forgetting-curve-its-up-to-you.htm?fbid=Z2IuZW4uNTUwLjE3LjE2LjM0Mzc).  People forget 50...",
