    "id": "cf2d6b70-8e8f-4e04-ac47-6f2512207c53",
    "title": "Ability to Provide Ongoing Services",
    "content": "Title: Ability to Provide Ongoing Services\n\nContent: Ability to Provide Ongoing Services\n\nWe offer and implement the following strategies to measure success and promote sustained implementation of workshop content:\n\n1. Participant Surveys\n\nWe Measure Success with Surveys by:\n\nA Pre-and Post-Survey Comparison: Comparing baseline data from pre-surveys with feedback from post-event surveys to assess growth in understanding or application of concepts.\n\nResponse Rates Analysis: Tracking the percentage of participants completing surveys to measure engagement. We aim for a completion rate of 70% or higher.\n\nQualitative Feedback Evaluation: Analyzing open-ended responses for recurring themes, specific praise, or suggestions for improvement.\n\nNet Promoter Score (NPS): Including the question &quot;How likely are you to recommend this session to a colleague?&quot; to quantify participant satisfaction and provide facilitators’ feedback.\n\nActionable Insights: Identifying how feedback directly informs changes to future sessions or programs, indicating responsiveness to participant needs.\n\n2. Learning Walk Tools for School Leaders (or for us to provide feedback)\n\nWe Measure Success with Learning Walk Tools by:\n\nAdoption Rate: Tracking how many school leaders are actively using the learning walk tools in their observations and reflections.\n\nQuality of Feedback Provided: Assessing the specificity and alignment of feedback given by leaders using the tools against best practices and/or rubrics based on workshop objectives.\n\nTeacher Impact Surveys: Conducting surveys with teachers to understand how feedback from learning walks informs their instructional practices.\n\nAlignment to Goals: Reviewing how learning walk outcomes align with district or school improvement goals (e.g., instructional focus areas).\n\n3. Follow-Up Virtual Sessions\n\nWe Measure Success with Follow-Up Sessions by:\n\nAttendance and Retention Rates: Tracking participant attendance over multiple sessions and identifying retention trends.\n\nActionable Implementation: Using follow-up discussions or surveys to measure how attendees have applied concepts or strategies learned in prior sessions.\n\nEngagement Metrics: Assessing participation during sessions through questions asked, polls completed, or collaborative activities.\n\nGoal Achievement Check-Ins: Incorporating goal-tracking tools or reflections for participants to report progress since the last session.\n\nFeedback from Session Summaries: Collecting feedback on session structure, content relevance, and delivery effectiveness to ensure continuous improvement.\n\nThese strategies ensure we measure impact, promote accountability, and foster sustainable implementation, and the strategies provide both quantitative and qualitative data to gauge success and inform iterative improvements.",
