    "id": "ee3d1eac-a085-4ff3-a460-069dbb1b83a6",
    "title": "WIDA MODEL | WIDA",
    "content": "Skip to main content Resources/RecursosWIDA Store Select a State: Member/State Pages Alabama Alaska Bureau of Indian Education Colorado Delaware Department of Defense Education Activity District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Kansas Kentucky Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Missouri Montana Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico North Carolina North Dakota Northern Mariana Islands Oklahoma Palau Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota U.S. Virgin Islands Utah Vermont Virginia Washington Wisconsin Wyoming Login WIDA Secure Portal WIDA AMS MODEL Online Unsure? Go to the Login page Menu Close Assess CloseAssessWIDA ACCESSPreparing for ACCESS TestingACCESS Test Practice and Sample ItemsACCESS Scores and ReportsWIDA Alternate ACCESSPreparing for Alternate ACCESS TestingAlternate ACCESS Sample ItemsWIDA ScreenerWIDA Screener Paper Score CalculatorWIDA Screener for Kindergarten Score CalculatorWIDA Alternate ScreenerWIDA Alternate Screener Score CalculatorAccessibility and AccommodationsBuilding a WIDA AssessmentWIDA MODELWIDA MODEL OnlineWIDA MODEL PaperWIDA MODEL for KindergartenWIDA MODEL Score CalculatorTechnologyAssessment Training Revised ACCESS gets released in the 25-26 WIDA testing year Learn About Revised ACCESS Teach CloseTeachUnderstanding Multilingual LearnersCreating a Welcoming ClassroomEngaging Families and CommunitiesUnderstanding What Students Can DoCan Do DescriptorsReading with Multilingual LearnersLanguage for LearningTeaching in PreK-3Teaching en EspañolMarco ALEMarco DALESupporting Multilingual Learners With DisabilitiesTeaching with StandardsELD Standards FrameworkStandards in ActionFeatured Educator Start using the brand-new WIDA Language Charts Read the article Grow CloseGrowProfessional Learning by TopicSelf-Paced WorkshopsWIDA WebinarsWIDA Annual ConferenceWIDA at ConferencesWIDA School Improvement System 2026 WIDA Annual ConferenceSeptember 15-18, St. Louis, MO Submit a Proposal Research CloseResearchResearch AreasCurrent Grants and ProjectsAccessible PathwaysALTELLAResearch PublicationsAbout CloseAboutMission and HistoryFederal Law and Policy FoundationsTeamsLeadershipStaff DirectoryPartnersWIDA ConsortiumWIDA Consortium Membership BenefitsWIDA FellowsWIDA EspañolCareersWhy Work at WIDA?Dassler InternshipWIDA Summer Research InternshipContact UsMedia Resources Expert educators of multilingual learners share their tips with WIDA Founder and Director Tim Boals. Conversations with Educators NewsResources Resources/RecursosWIDA Store WIDA MODEL Assess WIDA MODEL WIDA MODEL has moved!Learn about the move MODEL assessments are designed to measure students' progress in English language development.WIDA MODEL (Measure of Developing English Language) is a suite of English language proficiency assessments for grades K-12. As a flexible, on-demand language proficiency assessment, WIDA MODEL can be administered at any time during the school year, depending on the needs of the district, school, teacher or student. Scores can be used to predict student performance on ACCESS for ELLs.Visit the WIDA Store to purchase WIDA MODEL for your school(s). Features WIDA MODEL (grades 1-12) is available in both online and paper formats. WIDA MODEL for Kindergarten is a paper-based test.MODEL test items are written to WIDA's five English Language Development (ELD) Standards:Social and Instructional LanguageLanguage of Language ArtsLanguage of MathematicsLanguage of ScienceLanguage of Social StudiesTests are divided into five grade-level clusters:KindergartenGrades 1–2Grades 3–5Grades 6–8Grades 9–12Each test assesses the four language domains of Listening, Reading, Speaking and Writing. Purpose and Use WIDA MODEL can be used toDetermine real-time English language proficiency level scores for studentsServe as an interim assessment during the school yearMeasure and monitor student progress over timeInform instructional planning as well as curricular and programming decisionsPredict student performance on ACCESS for ELLs Scores WIDA MODEL scores are reported for all four domains (Listening, Reading, Speaking, Writing). In addition, score reports include three composite scores:Oral Language50% Listening50% SpeakingLiteracy50% Reading50% WritingOverall35% Reading35% Writing15% Listening15% Speaking Assessments in the WIDA MODEL Suite WIDA MODEL OnlineWIDA MODEL Online is a computer-based, semi-adaptive English language proficiency assessment for students in grades 1-12. This on-demand assessment can be administered up to two times a year to monitor students’ progress. WIDA MODEL Online WIDA MODEL PaperWIDA MODEL Paper is a paper-based, semi-adaptive English language proficiency assessment for students in grades 1-12. This assessment can be administered up to two times a year to monitor students’ progress. WIDA MODEL Paper WIDA MODEL for KindergartenWIDA MODEL for Kindergarten is a paper-based English language proficiency assessment administered individually to students in a game-like, interactive format. This on-demand assessment can be administered up to two times a year to monitor students’ progress. WIDA MODEL for Kindergarten Related Resources Predict student performance on WIDA ACCESS: WIDA MODEL is an interim assessment that can provide insight into how students will perform on ACCESS. Learn More About ACCESS and MODEL Using WIDA MODEL to support instructional planning: In this Focus Bulletin, we aim to help readers better understand how WIDA MODEL test scores may be used to support instructional planning decisions for multilingual learners and their teachers. Read the Focus Bulletin Interpretive Guide for Score Reports: The WIDA MODEL Interpretive Guide for Score Reports Grades K-12 describes the scores reported for WIDA MODEL, including how to interpret scale scores and proficiency level scores. Get the Interpretive Guide “We use MODEL because it allows us to have authentic conversations about the strengths of our students. In a system where our students are often measured by only one data point from a state assessment, MODEL offers great information about ELs focusing on the things that really matter. In our efforts to build the capacity of leaders, MODEL has served as the catalysts to support leaders of ELs across many schools.\"-Office of English Learner Programs and Services Director, Virginia “The WIDA MODEL Assessment has better allowed us as a district to determine how schools are performing with their English Language Development Program. We are able to, on an ongoing basis, make decisions about how language programming is delivered across grade levels and schools in real time. We are also able to communicate with families about their children’s language development several times a year. Content, ESOL teachers and administrators are able to use real time language data ... [and] triangulate it with content data to make sound instructional decisions based on individual student strengths.”-ESOL Supervisor of Curriculum Instruction, Accountability and Assessment, Maryland",
