    "id": "7d98ce21-6639-4ad0-b67d-2a76bfcf53d8",
    "title": "WebbAlign  About Dok Explained",
    "content": "A WCEPS Program Webb's DOK Explained Grounded in the language of the academic standards, the DOK framework differentiates complexity from difficulty. Use of DOK supports content analyses of educational materials. Used appropriately, DOK is a powerful tool that can inform instructional design and content development to elicit thinking that is as cognitively demanding as the expectations in the corresponding learning targets.Depth of Knowledge (DOK) is a tool that allows educators to communicate effectively, consistently, and efficiently about the content complexity of learning expectations, instructional materials, and assessment items. We are the only organization that works directly with Dr. Norman Webb, who developed the DOK language system. We use the Webb DOK framework to support educators, districts, assessment developers, states and others to evaluate and improve assessments using DOK and ultimately inform alignment of all parts of the education system.Learn more about how we can help you use DOK to inform your work:For districts and educatorsFor State departments or education representativesFor educational content providers",
