    "id": "15f511b3-636b-442e-9247-59d98bc1ceff",
    "title": "CALL Featured in UW-Madison School of Education",
    "content": "Description: CALL was featured in an online publication from UW-Madison's School of Eduction. \"Answering a ‘CALL’: School of Education research leads to business embraced by educators nationwide\"\n\nBack to Articles Categories: All updates news USBE WestEd School Improvement Personalized Learning Long Distance CALL Virtual Online Remote CALL Featured in UW-Madison School of Education Categories: News Updates Share Laurel White, writer for the UW-Madison School of Education's online publication, focused on the development and growth of CALL since its inception. Laurel spoke with Principle Investigators Richard Halverson and Carolyn Kelley, CALL Project Director Mark Blitz, WCEPS Director Matt Messinger, IES Education Research Analyst Katina Stapleton, and many of the CALL educators that have used the system in Utah, Mississippi, and Pennsylvania. Read about the growth of CALL from UW-Madison to today.",
