  {
    "id": "c408bac6-d56a-4c41-b042-f20f5c5ff8aa",
    "title": "Features Search And Notes",
    "content": "Description: Callsurveyv2\n\nLearn More > Features > Search and Notes Search and Notes The Comprehensive Assessment of Leadership for Learning (CALL) is organized into Domain and Subdomain practices, each of which has a construct label. However, there are other themes and ideas that permeate throughout the CALL items. Users can use the \"Search\" function to search by keyword or terms found in the constructs. They can then see the results of that search.Also, users can add \"notes\" into the system in any of the data blocks. This allows for an interactive approach to examining the CALL action-based data. School and district leaders can add comments, pose questions, and interact with each other through this function. These notes can be visible to other users who have access to the same report. Peers who have access to the report can respond to the comments and questions, which creates an opportunity for a dialogue around the data. Or, notes can be visible only to the note-writer for their own personal thoughts and ideas about the data.Learn more about the Search and Notes features:",
    "document_type": "website",
    "file_name": "Features Search And Notes.html",
