    "id": "f76d61cd-c77b-4095-8a3a-56523b9bc66a",
    "title": "Newcomer Success | Events | WCEPS Pathways",
    "content": "Description: Join WCEPS for a CARE Coaching session, Catching a Moving Target: Newcomer Success by Design based on the book written by Ryan Rumpf.\n\nNewcomer Success Workshops Catching the Moving Target: Guiding Newcomers to Mastery In-Person Workshops IN-PERSON WORKSHOPS Overview:This session is based on the book Catching the Moving Target: Guiding Newcomers to Mastery and offers compelling and practical steps for educators, leaders and decision-makers seeking to redesign how schools welcome and support newcomer multilingual learners. The comprehensive and customizable model combines research-informed, practice-proven approaches to both cognitive development and second language acquisition. After experiencing this session, participants will be prepared to go beyond compliance to create intentional, mastery-based learning opportunities that nurture language development, academic growth and emotional well-being from day one. Objectives: Describe key practices for providing a Soft Landing to Newcomer Students and Families Understand the principles of a mastery-based system Plan for applying a mastery-based learning cycle that integrates accessible language and content Meaningfully assess progress across a student’s learning journey ​This session comes with a hard copy of Catching the Moving Target: Guiding Newcomers to Mastery. Current schedule 2025 December 5, 20258:00am-3:30pm US Central TimeRitenour Center for Educational Excellence10901 St. Henry LaneSt. Ann, MO 63074 Located less than 10 minutes from St. Louis Lambert International Airport. IN-PERSON WORKSHOPS December 5, 2025 (St. Ann, MO; St. Louis area)8:00am-3:30pm US CT Rescheduled – new date coming soon! COST $600 REGISTRATION Register Now Events Interested in professional development opportunities for educators? Explore our events or contact us to set up a workshop designed for your team! Find an event Learning Library The WCEPS Pathways Learning Library provides free access to articles, v