    "content": "Description: Join WCEPS for CARE Coaching events designed to improve multi instruction to meet the needs of all learners. Virtual and in-person events available.\n\nMulti-Modal Instruction Workshops Designing Multi-Modal Instruction to Meet the Needs of Learners in a K-12 Setting Virtual and In-Person Options Overview Participants examine the principles of Universal Design for Learning as a framework for differentiating instruction in ways that engage all learners in grade-level content by providing multiple means of representation, expression, and engagement. After engaging in this learning opportunity, participants will be able to: Plan instruction that differentiates the presentation of content, meaning-making processes, and ways to demonstrate learning Leverage students’ strengths, interests, readiness, andlearning preferences Current schedule 2026 March 3, 2026 Albuquerque, NM8:30pm – 4:30pm US MT March 24, 2026 (virtual)3:00pm – 6:00pm US CT April 2, 2026 (virtual)7:00pm – 10:00pm US CT May 14, 2026 (virtual)8:30am – 11:30am US Central May 15, 2026 (virtual)7:00pm – 10:00pm US Central IN-PERSON WORKSHOPS March 3, 2026 Albuquerque, NM (New Mexico Highlands University – Rio Rancho Campus, 1700 Grande Blvd. SE, Rio Rancho, NM 87124)8:30am-3:30pm US Mountain Time COST With Credit: $650 Without Credit: $600 REGISTRATION With Graduate Credit No Graduate Credit VIRTUAL WORKSHOPS March 24, 2026, 3:00pm-6:00pm US Central Time April 2, 2026, 7:00pm-10:00pm US Central Time May 14, 2026, 8:30am-11:30am US Central Time May 15, 2026, 7:00pm-10:00pm US Central Time COST $400 REGISTRATION Register Today Events Interested in professional development opportunities for educators? Explore our events or contact us to set up a workshop designed for your team! Find an event Learning Library The WCEPS Pathways Learning Library provides free access to articles, videos and downloadable PDFs to support student learning in your classroom. Learn More CARE Coaching CARE Coa