    "content": "Description: Join WCEPS for CARE Coaching events designed to improve mathematical reasoning in the classroom. Virtual workshops are for educators.\n\nMathematical Reasoning Workshops A Functional Approach to Language for Mathematical Reasoning Virtual Workshops Overview This workshop explores how mathematical reasoning and language development intersect through a functional approach. Participants will experience concrete-to-abstract learning strategies, analyze the language demands of mathematical tasks, and apply scaffolds to support multilingual learners in accessing rigorous content. Educators will leave with tools to integrate Key Language Uses (KLUs) and discourse strategies into their math instruction. After this workshop, participants will be able to: Describe the connection between mathematical reasoning and language development Identify and apply the Key Language Uses (Explain, Inform, Argue, Narrate) in math instruction Analyze math tasks for linguistic and conceptual demands Current schedule 2026 Coming soon! VIRTUAL WORKSHOPS Coming soon! COST $400 REGISTRATION Coming soon Events Interested in professional development opportunities for educators? Explore our events or contact us to set up a workshop designed for your team! Find an event Learning Library The WCEPS Pathways Learning Library provides free access to articles, videos and downloadable PDFs to support student learning in your classroom. Learn More CARE Coaching CARE Coaching is designed to help K-12 educators provide equitable educational opportunities for long-term learners through personalized coaching. Learn More Learning Library The WCEPS Pathways Learning Library provides free access to articles, videos and downloadable PDFs to support student learning in your classroom. Read More Contact Us CARE Coaching provides customized learning opportunities designed for administrators, teachers, school and district leaders. Ready to learn more? ×",
