    "id": "2d2cc984-74da-47fc-8269-1b724384544b",
    "title": "Depth of Knowledge (DOK) Workshops | Events | WCEPS Pathways",
    "content": "Description: Join WCEPS for a CARE Coaching session focused on Depth of Knowledge (DOK) . This virtual event is available for graduate credit.\n\nDepth of Knowledge (DOK) Workshops Unlocking Rigor: Practical Applications of Webb’s Depth of Knowledge Framework Virtual and In-Person Workshops Overview This session introduces Webb’s Depth of Knowledge (DOK) as a tool for understanding and evaluating cognitive complexity in educational materials. Participants explore the distinction between difficulty and complexity, clarify common misconceptions about DOK, and examine its application to teaching and learning within a coherent education system. Through analysis and practice, participants consider implications for curriculum, assessment, and instructional decision-making. The session equips participants to integrate DOK into their teaching practices. After this workshop, participants will be able to: Demystify DOK levels and uncover common misunderstandings. Apply the DOK framework meaningfully across classroom contexts. Explore high-leverage strategies for optimizing instructional decisions. Current schedule 2026 February 6 & 13, 2026 (virtual)8:30- 12:00 pm CT February 11, 2026El Paso, TX8:30 am – 3:30 pm US MT June 5, 2026San Antonio, TX8:00-3:00 pm US CT IN-PERSON WORKSHOPS December 3, 2025 (Education Service Center Region 19, El Paso, TX), 9:00am-4:00pm US Mountain Time Rescheduled for February February 11, 2026 (Education Service Center Region 19, El Paso, TX), 8:30am-3:30pm US Mountain Time June 5, 2026 (San Antonio, TX), 8:30am-3:30pm US Central Time COST With Credit: $650 Without Credit: $600 REGISTRATION With Graduate Credit No Graduate Credit VIRTUAL WORKSHOPS February 6 & 13, 2026, 8:30am-12:00pm US Central Time COST With Credit: $550 Without Credit: $500 REGISTRATION With Graduate Credit No Graduate Credit Events Interested in professional development opportunities for educators? Explore our events or contact us to set up a workshop designed 