    "title": "CARE Coaching Program Overview - Pathways",
    "content": "CARE Coaching overview for educators Care coaching, offered through the Wisconsin Center for Education products and Services, is designed to ensure that school and district-based educators are supported to provide equitable educational opportunities for learners of all backgrounds. CARE Coaching focuses on the Three Cs: Consulting, Coaching, and Continuous Learning. Our professional learning offerings are designed to help educators reflect on their current practices and implement research-based actions that lead to meaningful change. Contact us to learn more about CARE Coaching and the impact it can have on your learning environment. CARE Coaching: Supporting K-12 Educators Working with English Language Learners Download the Program Overview CARE Coaching: Supporting K–12 Classroom Educators Download the Program Overview CARE Coaching: Supporting K–12 Classroom International Educators Download the Program Overview Looking to learn more about CARE Coaching? Reach out to one of our experts to guide you on a pathway to success! Get started today Contact Us CARE Coaching provides customized learning opportunities designed for administrators, teachers, school and district leaders. Ready to learn more? ×",
