    "id": "1a1da33e-3c91-4733-ab46-edb0720ee9a6",
    "title": "Quick dips: Considering individual English learners’ needs - Pathways",
    "content": "How to best support English learners Teaching and supporting English learners (ELs) demands a specific knowledge base and a system for accurately identifying students who need additional services, such as Special Education or Gifted and Talented. Guiding questions What expertise can we leverage to develop a system for accurate identification? What structures do we need to implement and sustain this system? How can we ensure effective integration of multiple services and programs, including collaboration among specialists? Resources to help you consider individual English learners’ needs English Learner Toolkit: Chapter 6 (United States Education Department) Promising and Effective Practices for English Learners (National Academies of Sciences, Engineering, and Medicine) Identifying Multilingual Learners with Specific Learning Disabilities (WIDA Focus Bulletin) Identifying English Learners with Disabilities (Regional Education Laboratory: Northeast and Islands) Looking to learn more about CARE Coaching? Reach out to one of our experts to guide you on a pathway to success! Get started today Contact Us CARE Coaching provides customized learning opportunities designed for administrators, teachers, school and district leaders. Ready to learn more? ×",
