  {
    "id": "38e04928-3e3a-43b9-958f-1b3ed40f6618",
    "title": "CARE Coaching in action: Hall County School District Georgia - Pathways",
    "content": "CARE Coaching in action: Hall County School District (Georgia) Empowering Educators to Support Multilingual Learners Hall County School District in Georgia, where multilingual learners make up more than a quarter of the student population, partnered with CARE Coaching to strengthen teacher capacity and build confidence in meeting diverse student needs. Under the leadership of Anna Sargent, Director of Federal Programs, the district sought a solution that would provide practical, classroom-ready support for educators. CARE Coaching delivers high-energy, highly engaging sessions that model real-world strategies teachers can use immediately. Every session connects directly to state language standards and includes ready-to-implement resources to make application seamless. Hall County educators received: Classroom-ready strategies modeled in real time and proven effective with multilingual learners Practical resources including PowerPoints, bite-sized lesson materials and ready-to-use activities that can be brought into the classroom immediately Clear alignment to state language standards for consistent and compliant instruction Manageable learning cycles that help teachers absorb new practices, reflect, and implement confidently Strengthened instructional mindset that supports a unified approach to multilingual learner success Greater enthusiasm and clarity around how to meet the challenges of today’s classrooms A more prepared, more confident teaching force equipped to support every learner CARE Coaching helped Hall County Schools move forward with a shared purpose and goal for multilingual learner success, transforming educators’ mindsets and elevating instructional quality across the district. Looking to learn more about CARE Coaching? Reach out to one of our experts to guide you on a pathway to success! Get started today Contact Us CARE Coaching provides customized learning opportunities designed for administrators, teachers, school and district leaders. Ready to learn more? ×",
