    "id": "8e5baf5d-d607-42fa-9fb4-244c8e8f0ec1",
    "title": "CARE Coaching Needs Assessment (CCNA) | Services | Pathways",
    "content": "Description: The CARE Coaching Needs Assessment (CCNA) identifies strengths, uncovers growth areas, and guides education leaders with action-based data to support school improvement and professional development planning.\n\nCARE Coaching Needs Assessment (CCNA) Turn Insight Into Instructional Impact The CARE Coaching Needs Assessment (CCNA) identifies strengths, uncovers growth areas, and guides education leaders with action-based data to support school improvement and professional development planning. By focusing on the various tasks, practices, and processes across schools, the CCNA maintains the focus on the work through the assessment process, the data analysis, and the action planning. The CCNA gives educators shared, actionable starting points for improving instruction and supporting all learners. Overview The CCNA assessment activity focuses on multilingual learner support, while also covering broader practices that affect all students. This evidence-based tool measures key aspects of school-wide leadership practices that impact instruction. Through the CARE Coaching data process, school teams leverage the resulting action-based data to target improvement areas, identify professional learning needs, and create action-oriented improvement plans. How It’s Different Traditional climate surveys capture perceptions including how people feel about culture and environment. That’s important, but not always enough to guide instructional decisions. Educators need data that is task-oriented so that they can spend their time addressing needs rather than speculating what needs to be done for improvement.Surveys focused on specific individuals all reveal a fraction of the leadership story in schools. Leadership is not confined to one individual. By focusing on the leadership work across a school, the CCNA is capturing school-wide practices carried out by all educators and leaders in a given school. The CARE Coaching Needs Assessment focuses on what your team is doing and what they can do next to improve teaching and learning. It also integrates content on multilingual learners alongside general instructional practices, so you don’t need separate tools. Authentic Continuous Improvement Through the CARE Coaching process, after school teams have identified their needs, developed an action plan based on the specific areas identified within the CCNA report, and implemented the plan, they can re-assess those target areas after a given time (30, 60, or 90 days, for example). The system can create an individualized assessment of the target areas for ongoing improvement work. Move Beyond Compliance Many schools are compelled to assess their needs, conduct a survey, and develop an improvement plan. Rather than check those tasks off a to-do list, school leaders can take advantage of an opportunity to engage in a needs assessment by implementing one that checks the boxes AND supports their work as leaders, indicates how best to support educators, and ultimately works to enhance student learning. Whether you’re refining coaching plans, improving instruction, or strengthening support for multilingual learners, the CARE Coaching Needs Assessment provides the insight and clarity you need.Request a demo or explore a sample report today. CCNA Highlights Action-Oriented DataSchool teams receive data that is relevant to their work. More time is spent on next steps rather than speculating what the data means. Instructional Practice FocusCCNA focuses on what drives learning: planning, collaboration, feedback, and leadership routines that directly influence teaching. Actionable ReportingNo data-dump. School teams gain access to user-friendly interactive reports with prioritized actions and coaching suggestions, ready to use for PD planning and strategic next steps. Multilingual Learner SupportIncludes focused items and recommendations on how to better serve multilingual learners, while also providing strategies that benefit all students. Ideal for schools with diverse language backgrounds. Request a Demo Learn More about CARE Coaching What is CARE Coaching Needs Assessment (CCNA)? Looking to learn more about CCNA and how it helps educators support student success and school improvement with action-based data? Read the latest in our Learning Library. Read the article CARE Coaching CARE Coaching is designed to help K-12 educators provide equitable educational opportunities for long-term learners through personalized coaching. Reach out to one of our experts to guide you on a pathway to success! Connect with us Contact Us CARE Coaching provides customized learning opportunities designed for administrators, teachers, school and district leaders. Ready to learn more? ×",
