  {
    "id": "adb066a3-a5cd-4787-95e4-2b6f26b4ec92",
    "title": "CARE_Coaching_Flyer_8.5x11_June_2025_FINAL",
    "content": "Title: CARE_Coaching_Flyer_8.5x11_June_2025_FINAL\n\nContent: CARE Coaching, CARE Coaching, offered through the Wisconsin Center for Education Products and Services, is designed to ensure that school- and district-based educators are equipped to provide high-quality educational opportunities for all students. We use the C.A.R.E. model to cultivate engagement in professional learning that is: Collaborative, Actionable, Responsive, and Empowering.  CARE Continuous Learning  These opportunities help educators address the needs of all students, ensuring effective instructional practices.  FoundationalPrinciples  Pedagogical Practices  Literacy Development  Content-Based Instruction  Family Engagement  Special Populations  CARE Consulting  Expert CARE Coaches consult directly with school and district leaders to provide technical help and conduct program evaluations.  Program Evaluations  Compliance Site Visits  Classroom Learning Walks  Title III  Progress Monitoring  Academic Enrichment for MLs  CARE Coaching  CARE Coaches meet you where you are and help you reach your goals. They offer guidance, reflection, sharing, and goal-setting in both in-person and online sessions, working collaboratively with:  Teachers  Instructional Coaches  Team  Administrators and Leaders  Professional Learning  Communities  Contact Us to Get Started!  wcepspathways.org/coaching educators@wceps.org ",
