    "content": "Description: Here you will find resources to enhance your learning and understanding of our programs from blogs to videos.\n\nWELCOME TO THE Pathways Learning Library! The WCEPS Pathways Learning Library provides free access to articles, videos and downloadable PDFs to support student learning in your classroom. Each resource is designed to offer new perspectives for educators, enhance the classroom experience and positively impact student outcomes. Filters Audience Administrators Bilingual & Dual Language Educators Families & Parents Education Level Elementary Grades 6-12 Higher Ed Content Type Blog Flyer PDF Podcast Video Programs & Services CARE Coaching WebbAlign WIDA Licensed Offerings Tags Conference External Resource Tips and Dips Webinar Topics Assessments Cultural integration Family engagement Instructional strategies Language development Math Newcomer students Reading Writing UPCOMING EVENT Tips and Dips Webinar Series Valuable insights to support educators. A free monthly webinar series. View Event Details Feature Blog Educators Elementary Grades 6-12 CARE Coaching Instructional strategies April 14, 2025 Designing Powerful Outcomes: Integrating Language and Content through Specialist Roles Learn how crafting effective intended outcomes, including those that align content and language learning, can elevate student engagement and deepen academic achievement. A central strategy we focused on was using Specialist Roles to support content-rich learning environments. Read Full Post Recent Posts Video Administrators Educators Elementary Grades 6-12 CARE Coaching November 24, 2025 CARE Coaching in action: Hall County School District Georgia CARE Coaching in action: Hall County School District (Georgia) Empowering Educators to Support Multilingual Learners Hall County School District in Georgia, where multilingual learners make up more than a quarter… Read Full Post PDF Administrators Educators Elementary Grades 6-12 Higher Ed WebbAlign Instructional strategies October 28, 2025 WebbAlign – Evaluating Technical Quality in the Context of Assessment Innovation How do we evaluate the quality of innovative assessments, especially those designed to support deeper learning and instructional relevance? Read Full Post PDF Bilingual & Dual Language Educators Elementary Grades 6-12 CARE Coaching Cultural integration Instructional strategies August 29, 2025 CARE Coaching International CARE Coaching International, offered through the Wisconsin Center for Education Products and Services (WCEPS), equips international educators and school leaders with strategies to foster equitable educational opportunities for multilingual learners. Read Full Post Blog Bilingual & Dual Language Educators Elementary Grades 6-12 CARE Coaching Tips and Dips Instructional strategies August 26, 2025 Unlocking Newcomer Brilliance: From Soft Landings to Lasting Success Learn how crafting effective intended outcomes, including those that align content and language learning, can elevate student engagement and deepen academic achievement. A central strategy we focused on was using Specialist Roles to support content-rich learning environments. Read Full Post Blog Video Administrators Educators Elementary Grades 6-12 CARE Coaching Assessments August 26, 2025 The CARE Coaching Needs Assessment (CCNA): Action-Based Data for All Learn how crafting effective intended outcomes, including those that align content and language learning, can elevate student engagement and deepen academic achievement. A central strategy we focused on was using Specialist Roles to support content-rich learning environments. Read Full Post Blog Educators Elementary Grades 6-12 CARE Coaching Instructional strategies April 14, 2025 Designing Powerful Outcomes: Integrating Language and Content through Specialist Roles Learn how crafting effective intended outcomes, including those that align content and language learning, can elevate student engagement and deepen academic achievement. A central strategy we focused on was using Specialist Roles to support content-rich learning environments. Read Full Post Blog Video Educators Elementary Grades 6-12 CARE Coaching Tips and Dips Assessments Instructional strategies April 3, 2025 The Value of Collaborative Assessment and Reflection Dr. Ryan Rumpf, WCEPS CARE Coach, and Margarita Marrero Associate Director of CARE Coaching at WCEPS, explore the concept of backward design in education, emphasizing the importance of desired results, goals and acceptable evidence in learning. Read Full Post PDF Administrators Educators Elementary Grades 6-12 Higher Ed WebbAlign Instructional strategies April 2, 2025 WebbAlign – What is Depth of Knowledge (DOK)? Depth of Knowledge (DOK) developed by WebbAlign is a tool that allows educators to communicate effectively and efficiently about the content complexity of learning expectations and standards. Read Full Post Blog Video Educators Elementary Grades 6-12 CARE Coaching Tips and Dips Instructional strategies Language development April 1, 2025 The Value of Co-Planning to Impact Academic Performance – Effective Backward Design Dr. Ryan Rumpf, WCEPS CARE Coach, and Margarita Marrero Associate Director of CARE Coaching at WCEPS, explore the concept of backward design in education, emphasizing the importance of desired results, goals and acceptable evidence in learning. Read Full Post Video Educators Elementary Grades 6-12 CARE Coaching Tips and Dips Instructional strategies Language development March 6, 2025 The Principles of Dialogic Teaching Dr. Ryan Rumpf, WCEPS CARE Coach, explores the principles of dialogic teaching, a research-backed approach that puts oracy and collaborative dialogue at the heart of education. Read Full Post Contact Us CARE Coaching provides customized learning opportunities designed for administrators, teachers, school and district leaders. Ready to learn more? ×",
