    "id": "265bfc43-9f65-4fcf-9e3d-5828b58ef36d",
    "title": "ACCESS Test Practice and Sample Items",
    "content": "Description: Familiarize students with the kind of content they will encounter on the test and give them a chance to practice the different question types.Completing the practice items can be especially helpful for students who are new to the WIDA ACCESS Speaking test, but keep in mind that the first thing students do when they take the real test is complete these same practice items.\n\nSkip to main content Resources/RecursosWIDA Store Select a State: Member/State Pages Alabama Alaska Bureau of Indian Education Colorado Delaware Department of Defense Education Activity District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Kansas Kentucky Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Missouri Montana Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico North Carolina North Dakota Northern Mariana Islands Oklahoma Palau Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota U.S. Virgin Islands Utah Vermont Virginia Washington Wisconsin Wyoming Login WIDA Secure Portal WIDA AMS MODEL Online Unsure? Go to the Login page Menu Close Assess CloseAssessWIDA ACCESSPreparing for ACCESS TestingACCESS Test Practice and Sample ItemsACCESS Scores and ReportsWIDA Alternate ACCESSPreparing for Alternate ACCESS TestingAlternate ACCESS Sample ItemsWIDA ScreenerWIDA Screener Paper Score CalculatorWIDA Screener for Kindergarten Score CalculatorWIDA Alternate ScreenerWIDA Alternate Screener Score CalculatorAccessibility and AccommodationsBuilding a WIDA AssessmentWIDA MODELWIDA MODEL OnlineWIDA MODEL PaperWIDA MODEL for KindergartenWIDA MODEL Score CalculatorTechnologyAssessment Training Revised ACCESS gets released in the 25-26 WIDA testing year Learn About Revised ACCESS Teach CloseTeachUnderstanding Multilingual LearnersCreating a Welcoming ClassroomEngaging Families and CommunitiesUnderstanding What Students Can DoCan Do DescriptorsReading with Multilingual LearnersLanguage for LearningTeaching in PreK-3Teaching en EspañolMarco ALEMarco DALESupporting Multilingual Learners With DisabilitiesTeaching with StandardsELD Standards FrameworkStandards in ActionFeatured Educator Start using the brand-new WIDA Language Charts Read the article Grow CloseGrowProfessional Learning by TopicSelf-Paced WorkshopsWIDA WebinarsWIDA Annual ConferenceWIDA at ConferencesWIDA School Improvement System 2026 WIDA Annual ConferenceSeptember 15-18, St. Louis, MO Submit a Proposal Research CloseResearchResearch AreasCurrent Grants and ProjectsAccessible PathwaysALTELLAResearch PublicationsAbout CloseAboutMission and HistoryFederal Law and Policy FoundationsTeamsLeadershipStaff DirectoryPartnersWIDA ConsortiumWIDA Consortium Membership BenefitsWIDA FellowsWIDA EspañolCareersWhy Work at WIDA?Dassler InternshipWIDA Summer Research InternshipContact UsMedia Resources Expert educators of multilingual learners share their tips with WIDA Founder and Director Tim Boals. Conversations with Educators NewsResources Resources/RecursosWIDA Store ACCESS Test Practice and Sample Items Assess WIDA ACCESS ACCESS Test Practice and Sample Items Familiarize students with the kind of content they will encounter on the test and give them a chance to practice the different question types.Completing the practice items can be especially helpful for students who are new to the WIDA ACCESS Speaking test, but keep in mind that the first thing students do when they take the real test is complete these same practice items. ACCESS Online Give students the chance to learn about the test platform, practice answering the type of questions they’ll see on the test, and get to know the features and tools built in to the test platform. Modify the suggested scripting to fit the needs of your students.Preparing Students for ACCESS Online Sample ItemsSample items give students a chance to practice answering the type of questions they will see on the test at their grade-cluster level, and an opportunity to use the features and tools built in to the test platform. Suggested scripting is provided to help guide students through the sample items. Modify the suggested scripting to fit the needs of your students.Suggested Sample Item Script: ACCESS OnlineACCESS Online Sample ItemsPaper-format Writing Sample ItemsStudents in grades 1–3 always take the Writing test in a pencil-and-paper format, even though they complete the other domain tests in the online test platform.Grade 1, Tier A: Making a CardGrade 1, Tier B/C: David's IdeaGrades 2-3, Tier A: Reading TimeGrades 2-3, Tier B/C: Pond Animals Test DemoA test demo for each grade-level cluster shows students how to navigate different features of the test.Test DemoTest PracticeWhen students take the test, they start with practice items that help familiarize them with the test platform. Students may go through these practice items as many times as they like prior to testing day. Keep in mind that the practice items are not representative of the difficulty of scored test items – the test practice is simply a chance for students to use the test platform.ACCESS Online Test Practice (about 5-10 minutes) ACCESS Paper Give students a chance to practice answering the type of questions they’ll see and hear on the test.Preparing Students for ACCESS Paper Grade 1Grade 1, Tier A, ReadingGrade 1, Tier A, ListeningGrade 1, Tier A, SpeakingGrade 1, Tier A, WritingGrade 1, Tier B, ReadingGrade 1, Tier B/C, ListeningGrade 1, Tier B/C, SpeakingGrade 1, Tier B/C, WritingGrades 2-3Grade 2, Tier A, ReadingGrade 2, Tier A, SpeakingGrade 2, Tier A, WritingGrade 2, Tier B/C, ListeningGrade 2, Tier B/C, SpeakingGrade 2, Tier B/C, WritingGrade 3, Tier A, ReadingGrade 3, Tier A, SpeakingGrade 3, Tier A, Writing 1Grade 3, Tier A, Writing 2Grade 3, Tier B/C, SpeakingGrade 3, Tier B/C, WritingGrades 2-3, Tier A, ListeningGrades 2-3, Tier C, Reading Grades 4-5Grades 4-5, Tier A, ListeningGrades 4-5, Tier A, ReadingGrades 4-5, Tier A, WritingGrades 4-5, Tier B/C, ListeningGrades 4-5, Tier B/C, ReadingGrades 4-5, Tier B/C, WritingGrades 4-5, Tier B/C, SpeakingGrades 6-8Grades 6-8, Tier A, ListeningGrades 6-8, Tier A, ReadingGrades 6-8, Tier A, SpeakingGrades 6-8, Tier A, WritingGrades 6-8, Tier B/C, ListeningGrades 6-8, Tier B/C, ReadingGrades 6-8, Tier B/C, SpeakingGrades 6-8, Tier B/C, WritingGrades 9-12Grades 9-12, Tier A, ListeningGrades 9-12, Tier A, ReadingGrades 9-12, Tier A, SpeakingGrades 9-12, Tier A, WritingGrades 9-12, Tier B/C, ListeningGrades 9-12, Tier B/C, ReadingGrades 9-12, Tier B/C, Speaking ACCESS Braille Accommodation OverviewSample test items give students a chance to practice answering the types of questions they’ll get on the ACCESS assessments. Like the ACCESS tests, the braille sample items come with a choice of braille codes to meet individual student needs.You can download sample items to use with your students, including audio files for Listening items. Braille sample items with graphics are available as images for reproduction at your site. Braille sample items without graphics are available in Braille Ready Format (.BRF) files and can be downloaded and embossed. Physical copies of these materials are also provided in all braille kits.The sample items and their user guides are separated into grades 1–3, grades 4–5, grades 6–8 and grades 9–12. Select the appropriate grade-level cluster for your student. Use the Sample Items User Guide for Braille to administer the practice items to your student.To get started, read the Quick Start Guide: ACCESS Braille Sample Items. Grades 1-3Braille Sample Item Materials for Grades 1-3Grades 4-5Braille Sample Item Materials for Grades 4-5 Grades 6-8Braille Sample Item Materials for Grades 6-8Grades 9-12Braille Sample Item Materials for Grades 9-12",
