  {
    "id": "9c8aa84b-bd67-4bbf-83a2-e8b9b15c5828",
    "title": "WIDA Workshop info",
    "content": "Description: Workshops are one to two-day professional learning offerings that can be purchased by a school or district.\n\nWorkshopsWebinars and in-person workshopsWebinar limit: 50 registrationsWebinars will close when the maximum enrollment is reachedPUrchase vouchers for Future open enrollment Events here! Filters Use the filters to narrow down your selection. Webinar Scheduled Español English Assessment International Schools View All Planning with the WIDA ELD Standards Framework Facilitated eWorkshop (webinar series) This eWorkshop of three 1-hour sessions is designed for educators and leaders who are responsible for language development within content learning and implementation of the ELD Standards Framework. Participants will receive resources for using the ELD Standards Framework in instructional planning. Teams are strongly encouraged to attend the webinars together.Attendees will receive a certificate of attendance at the completion of this series for three hours of Professional Learning. Dates December 3-5, 2025: 2:30pm-3:30pm US Central Time January 13-15, 2026: 3:00pm-4:00pm US Central Time January 13-15, 2026: 7:00pm-8:00pm US Central Time February 3-5, 2026: 8:30am-9:30am US Central Time February 3-5, 2026: 10:00am-11:00am US Central Time March 30-31 and April 1, 2026: 3:00pm-4:00pm US Central Time March 30-31 and April 1, 2026: 7:00pm-8:00pm US Central Time April 29-30 and May 1, 2026: 8:30am-9:30am US Central Time April 29-30 and May 1, 2026: 10:00am-11:00am US Central Time May 11-13, 2026: 3:00pm-4:00pm US Central Time May 11-13, 2026: 7:00pm-8:00pm US Central Time June 22-24, 2026: 9:00am-10:00am US Central Time June 22-24, 2026: 11:00am-12:00pm US Central Time Tags English Scheduled Webinar International Interpreting ACCESS for ELLs Score Reports for Instruction (webinar) The ACCESS for ELLs Score Reports provide specific information on students’ academic English language proficiency. During this training, participants will explore how the WIDA Standards and Assessment System is connected to the ACCESS for ELLs score reports. Participants will examine the different types and uses of score reports. They will also make connections between the students’ proficiency scores and WIDA Performance Definitions.Note: This webinar is available for US Member Schools only. Dates December 2, 2025: 1:00pm-3:00pm US Central Time December 15, 2025: 3:00pm-5:00pm US Central Time Tags English Scheduled Webinar Assessment WIDA MODEL Online Test Administration Webinar Series This WIDA MODEL training webinar series of two 2-hour sessions is for educators who are preparing to administer the WIDA MODEL Online assessment for grades 1-12. WIDA MODEL can be used as an identification/placement assessment for newly enrolled ELLs or as an interim progress monitoring assessment. During this training, participants will learn how to administer and score each of the four domain assessments as well as how to navigate and perform key functions in the MODEL Online test management and rostering platforms. Dates December 8-9, 2025: 5:00am-7:00am US Central Time December 8-9, 2025: 3:00pm-5:00pm US Central Time January 20-21, 2026: 9:00am-11:00am US Central Time February 9-10, 2026: 3:00pm-5:00pm US Central Time March 10-11, 2026: 5:00am-7:00am US Central Time March 10-11, 2026: 9:00am-11:00am US Central Time April 8-9, 2026: 3:00pm-5:00pm US Central Time May 6-7, 2026: 9:00am-11:00am US Central Time June 9-10, 2026: 3:00pm-5:00pm US Central Time Tags Scheduled Webinar International Assessment Scaffolding Learning through Language (webinar series or 2-day workshop) This workshop provides educators with a fresh look at how to engage multilingual learners in rigorous content area learning with a balance of challenge and support. The purpose of the workshop is to encourage educators to consider classroom practices that move multilingual learning forward and upward together within the context of meaningful experiences where learning is mediated through language. Dates Denver, CO (Lowry Conference Center) - December 3-4, 2025 (2-day in-person) December 3-5, 2025: 6:00pm-7:30pm US Central Time Tags Scheduled English Webinar International Writing with Multilingual Learners in the Elementary Grades (2-day workshop) This two-day in-person workshop focuses on writing instruction that supports the use of the Teaching and Learning Cycle as a way to empower multilingual writers, not only to produce successful academic writing but, more importantly, to communicate effectively for a variety of purposes and different audiences. We want students to know how to leverage writing as a powerful tool to understand the world, express themselves effectively, learn from one another, and argue for the things they believe in. This vision requires intentional, language-focused instruction and is strengthened when it occurs through authentic writing tasks in the content areas. Dates Portland, OR - January 12-13, 2026 Louisville, KY - February 12-13, 2026 Hilo, Hawaii(University of Hawaii Community College) - March 25-26, 2026 Toms River, NJ - April 23-24, 2026 (Ocean County College Conference Center) Chicago, IL - April 30-May 1, 2026 (LOCATION COMING SOON) Chicago, IL - May 18-19, 2026 Seattle, WA - May 26-27, 2026 Dallas, TX - June 2-3, 2026 Boston, MA - June 23-24, 2026 Tags Scheduled International English WIDA Español: Desarrollando el español: Afirmando la experiencia bilingüe por medio del Marco DALE (1-day workshop) This one-day Spanish and English bilingual workshop will serve as an introduction to Marco DALE. Through an interactive and applied approach, participants will connect the pedagogical foundations of Marco DALE to inform instructional planning and engage in discussions and activities that leverage the pedagogical framework, tools, and resources. Participants will explore how WIDA frameworks and practices such as translanguaging and multiliteracy-focused teaching can be integrated into instruction to support the linguistic and cultural identities of diverse students and families. This workshop will be delivered primarily in Spanish. Dates Toms River, NJ - April 22, 2026 (Ocean County College Conference Center) Chicago, IL - May 20, 2026 Seattle, WA - May 28, 2026 Dallas, TX - June 4, 2026 Tags Scheduled International Español WIDA Español: Desarrollando el español: Introducción al Marco DALE (1/2-day workshop) This half-day Spanish and English bilingual workshop serves as an abbreviated introduction to Marco DALE. Through an interactive and applied approach, participants will connect the pedagogical foundations of Marco DALE to inform instructional planning and engage in discussions and activities that leverage the pedagogical framework, tools, and resources. This workshop is delivered primarily in Spanish. Tags International Español Enseñando en español: Explorando identidades (90-minute webinar) Este taller virtual utiliza un enfoque interactivo y práctico para analizar la importancia de reconocer la diversidad del español en la enseñanza del mismo en espacios bi/multilingües. A través de ejemplos interactivos, los participantes explorarán el Marco de referencia de las artes del lenguaje del español de WIDA (Marco ALE). Específicamente, el taller se centrará en la importancia de respetar e incorporar la diversidad del español en la planificación intencional y eficaz de su enseñanza utilizando el Marco ALE. También, se dará consideración a la equidad y el empoderamiento de maestros y estudiantes en la enseñanza del español. Este taller se entrega en español. En Español Enseñando en español: Explorando identidades (taller virtual - 90-minutos) Este taller virtual utiliza un enfoque interactivo y práctico para analizar la importancia de reconocer la diversidad del español en la enseñanza del mismo en espacios bi/multilingües. A través de ejemplos interactivos, los participantes explorarán el Marco de referencia de las artes del lenguaje del español de WIDA (Marco ALE). Específicamente, el taller se centrará en la importancia de respetar e incorporar la diversidad del español en la planificación intencional y eficaz de su enseñanza utilizando el Marco ALE. También, se dará consideración a la equidad y el empoderamiento de maestros y estudiantes en la enseñanza del español. Este taller se entrega en español. Dates January 14, 2026: 1:00pm-2:30pm US Central Time March 18, 2026: 5:00pm-6:30pm US Central Time May 20, 2026: 9:00am-10:30am US Central Time June 3, 2026: 1:00pm-2:30pm US Central Time Tags Scheduled International Español Webinar Enseñando en español: El Marco ALE en acción (90-minute webinar) Este taller virtual utiliza un enfoque interactivo y práctico para conectar las prácticas teóricas y pedagógicas de la enseñanza de las artes del lenguaje del español. A través de ejemplos interactivos, los participantes explorarán la aplicación del Marco de referencia de las artes del lenguaje del español de WIDA (Marco ALE). Específicamente, el taller se centrará en la importancia de utilizar a la misma vez las tres hebras del Marco ALE para la planificación intencional y eficaz de unidades y lecciones de las artes del lenguaje del español. También se pondrá énfasis en las oportunidades para utilizar el translenguaje en espacios educativos bi/multilingües.Este taller se entrega en español. En Español Enseñando en español: El Marco ALE en acción (taller virtual - 90-minutos) Este taller virtual utiliza un enfoque interactivo y práctico para conectar las prácticas teóricas y pedagógicas de la enseñanza de las artes del lenguaje del español. A través de ejemplos interactivos, los participantes explorarán la aplicación del Marco de referencia de las artes del lenguaje del español de WIDA (Marco ALE). Específicamente, el taller se centrará en la importancia de utilizar a la misma vez las tres hebras del Marco ALE para la planificación intencional y eficaz de unidades y lecciones de las artes del lenguaje del español. También se pondrá énfasis en las oportunidades para utilizar el translenguaje en espacios educativos bi/multilingües.Este taller se entrega en español. Dates January 21, 2026: 1:00pm-2:30pm US Central Time March 25, 2026: 5:00pm-6:30pm US Central Time May 27, 2026: 9:00am-10:30am US Central Time June 17, 2026: 1:00pm-2:30pm US Central Time Tags Scheduled International Español Webinar Enseñando en español: Explorando identidades y El Marco ALE en acción (1/2-day workshop) Enseñando en español: Explorando identidades y El Marco ALE en acción (1/2 day in person) Tags International Español ← Previous 1 2 Next → COOKIE NOTICE: We use cookies on this site to enhance your experience and improve our marketing efforts. By continuing to browse without changing your browser settings to block or delete cookies, you agree to the storing of cookies and related technologies on your device. UW Madison Privacy Policy. Got it!",
