    "id": "c9876dc5-067a-4377-a691-eba3fb559af9",
    "title": "AIW Institute",
    "content": "An introduction to AIW for Japanese educators January 7, 2021 | M. Bruce King Dr. Bruce King, AIW Institute director, and Taka Yamamoto, recent graduate student at the University of Wisconsin, will offer a 3-part seminar with Japanese educators in January, 2021. The introductory seminar will focus on the negative impacts of traditional curriculum and instruction and the over-emphasis on testing, and address the ways Authentic Intellectual Work can support powerful, equitable 21st century education. Author M. Bruce King Director, AIW Institute",
