  {
    "id": "30211dda-c678-4542-a037-32467a1f2488",
    "title": "AIW Institute",
    "content": "AIW In the fieldNews and Information about the work of the AIW Institute The Student Engagement Crisis In their new book, Jenny Anderson and Rebecca Winthrop address the crisis of teen disengagement. It's a great time to for authentic teaching and learning. (Read more) Substantive Conversations across the Curriculum A recent study by University of Wisconsin-Madison doctoral student Nicole Marble (Director of Secondary Education, Wauwatosa WI School District) documents how one high school successfully supported their teachers’ professional growth in order to effectively implement AIW’s instructional standard of substantive conversation in all subject areas. (Read more) An introduction to AIW for Japanese educators Building Bridges, Not Borders AIW Institute Director, Dr. M. Bruce King, and Associate Director, Dr. Laura Lang, of the AIW Institute recently published an article with colleagues in Jerusalem, Israel in the Journal of Research in International Education. (Read more) Independence Day reading What a long, strange, inspiring year it's been. This spring has been hard. Incredibly hard. But you, our AIW partners, have inspired us with much hope for what is possible in the coming years. (Read more) An Exciting New Collaboration: AIW and Urban Indigenous Arts & Sciences A Transatlantic (AIW) Partnership Nurturing Teacher Leadership \"AIW is the game changer\" - Jeff Ladson, Instructional Coach (Indianola, Iowa) \"We use the AIW instructional rubrics every single day.\" Mike Maddox, Principal (Pike County Middle School, Georgia) The Scoring Process Recent Posts The Student Engagement Crisis Substantive Conversations across the Curriculum An introduction to AIW for Japanese educators Building Bridges, Not Borders Independence Day reading What a long, strange, inspiring year it's been. An Exciting New Collaboration: AIW and Urban Indigenous Arts & Sciences A Transatlantic (AIW) Partnership Nurturing Teacher Leadership \"AIW is the game changer\" - Jeff Ladson, Instructional Coach (Indianola, Iowa) \"We use the AIW instructional rubrics every single day.\" Mike Maddox, Principal (Pike County Middle School, Georgia) The Scoring Process",
