000\r\nWell, then, the next week we had a Poc meeting of professional learning, and we found out that at the district level that they don't want them getting any part of the test in their 1st language, because it's not what they're going to see on Georgia milestones.\r\n\r\n01:27:13.000 --> 01:27:16.000\r\nOur State assessment. And so they're making them take.\r\n\r\n01:27:16.000 --> 01:27:18.000\r\nEverything, in English.\r\n\r\n01:27:18.000 --> 01:27:26.000\r\nAcross the board because they want the raw data. So these kids are like, and I mean, they're lengthy. I mean, like my 5th graders were doing a test today, and it was.\r\n\r\n01:27:26.000 --> 01:27:38.000\r\n18 different questions, and it was multiple passages with like comprehension questions that go with it. Some of them have more than one answers which they totally don't get like. It's just.\r\n\r\n01:27:38.000 --> 01:27:39.000\r\nIt's a lot.\r\n\r\n01:27:39.000 --> 01:27:43.000\r\nIt's a lot like I'm struggling. I told my bot.\r\n\r\n01:27:43.000 --> 01:27:57.000\r\nYeah. Go ahead.\r\n\r\n01:27:57.000 --> 01:27:58.000\r\nYes.\r\n\r\n01:27:58.000 --> 01:28:01.000\r\nI was going to, I was going to add, that's kind of something happening here in Texas as well, and I know something that does help. And it was mentioned a little bit in the chat as well is to A, and it does involve a lot of planning because you're learning a new curriculum as you're kind of going through it, just barely staying above water and then trying to meet the needs of all kids.\r\n\r\n01:28:01.000 --> 01:28:02.000\r\nSo.\r\n\r\n01:28:02.000 --> 01:28:04.000\r\nI got bubbles right now. I'm not even above.\r\n\r\n01:28:04.000 --> 01:28:06.000\r\nYeah, you're kind of like.\r\n\r\n01:28:06.000 --> 01:28:23.000\r\nSo I know that's something that that is helpful is to narrow down. And and I think it's what everyone is referring to as well, narrow down your standards, and even know your State assessment to narrow down the most important things.\r\n\r\n01:28:23.000 --> 01:28:30.000\r\nOkay.\r\n\r\n01:28:30.000 --> 01:28:37.000\r\nYeah.\r\n\r\n01:28:37.000 --> 01:28:38.000\r\nRight.\r\n\r\n01:28:38.000 --> 01:28:50.000\r\nSome some state assessments do have blueprints, and and it's not teaching to the test. I think sometimes people get scared about that, because I think it's teaching to the test. But when you have to meet the needs of all students, you have to know what the priority is. And well, that's that's basically it. You have to know what the priority is. So I know that's something that helps is really knowing kind of the weight of the standards. If that makes sense.\r\n\r\n01:28:50.000 --> 01:28:51.000\r\nYeah.\r\n\r\n01:28:51.000 --> 01:28:53.000\r\nWhich most of the classroom teachers have the essential standards that they've unpacked so I can get with them and get that copy.\r\n\r\n01:28:53.000 --> 01:28:57.000\r\nThat's a good idea.\r\n\r\n01:28:57.000 --> 01:29:00.000\r\nYeah.\r\n\r\n01:29:00.000 --> 01:29:03.000\r\nOkay.\r\n\r\n01:29:03.000 --> 01:29:04.000\r\nOkay.\r\n\r\n01:29:04.000 --> 01:29:13.000\r\nYes, yes, and that way you're clear on the goal. Sometimes it's even down to the verb like, are they needing to identify this are they needing to describe? Are they comparing and contrasting? So the more narrow and the the clearer the goals are. I think it helps you kind of move through the curriculum. If that makes sense kind of move through that heavy water.\r\n\r\n01:29:13.000 --> 01:29:18.000\r\nYes, like, if they're identifying. I don't really need them to write a paragraph about it.\r\n\r\n01:29:18.000 --> 01:29:19.000\r\nExactly.\r\n\r\n01:29:19.000 --> 01:29:23.000\r\nI wanted to ask, because you guys have all these standards and state assessments.\r\n\r\n01:29:23.000 --> 01:29:34.000\r\nI. This is my 1st year as a librarian, and they the librarian before me, just left in the middle of the year last year, and they had no one fill the spot.\r\n\r\n01:29:34.000 --> 01:29:38.000\r\nAnd so everything was just piled up. It was horrible, disorganized.\r\n\r\n01:29:38.000 --> 01:29:44.000\r\nAnd then also, I wasn't the one who got to clear out the library work rooms and the file cabinets.\r\n\r\n01:29:44.000 --> 01:29:45.000\r\nOh no!\r\n\r\n01:29:45.000 --> 01:29:48.000\r\nSo like I don't have any of that stuff.\r\n\r\n01:29:48.000 --> 01:30:00.000\r\nAnd I haven't been included. We are getting a new reading program. We just got it and stated,\r\n\r\n01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:01.000\r\nI love it. You are.\r\n\r\n01:30:01.000 --> 01:30:12.000\r\nStarting on the second quarter. It's the AR reading program, and I was like, not a part of the meeting, or like, I'm not a part of the El meetings or the language arts meetings. Do you guys think it would be good if I request to be a part of those.\r\n\r\n01:30:12.000 --> 01:30:14.000\r\nAbsolutely.\r\n\r\n01:30:14.000 --> 01:30:16.000\r\nYeah.\r\n\r\n01:30:16.000 --> 01:30:17.000\r\nYeah.\r\n\r\n01:30:17.000 --> 01:30:19.000\r\nI would think so. I know our our media specialists, I know, is super involved with our reading interventionist, and especially with the AR program.\r\n\r\n01:30:19.000 --> 01:30:31.000\r\nAnd so, like, our kids have various goals. And so at certain point levels, or whatever they get different rewards. And they have a cart that goes around. They make a big deal out of it. But yeah, like all the people who are involved in reading any any capacity, or you know.\r\n\r\n01:30:31.000 --> 01:30:32.000\r\nOkay, cause. They just.\r\n\r\n01:30:32.000 --> 01:30:33.000\r\nSpecialists like. They all work together.\r\n\r\n01:30:33.000 --> 01:30:42.000\r\nYeah, cause they just so one of the terminologies. I'm very specific about my words, but they call it uncertified staff or support staff.\r\n\r\n01:30:42.000 --> 01:30:43.000\r\nOkay.\r\n\r\n01:30:43.000 --> 01:30:51.000\r\nAnd I'm in that. But I I went to school for it. I've done trainings. I've also done volunteer work like my whole life for it. So it's kind of.\r\n\r\n01:30:51.000 --> 01:31:02.000\r\nI feel like they're not taking the role seriously. So like, I'm kind of curious, like of like professional like development. And you know, bringing that up to them.\r\n\r\n01:31:02.000 --> 01:31:03.000\r\nI would just tell them you have all the books.\r\n\r\n01:31:03.000 --> 01:31:06.000\r\nI think anytime that you can advocate.\r\n\r\n01:31:06.000 --> 01:31:07.000\r\nLike I have the books. How can I encourage them?\r\n\r\n01:31:07.000 --> 01:31:12.000\r\nYeah, I think anytime that you can advocate.\r\n\r\n01:31:12.000 --> 01:31:17.000\r\nIf you can advocate, and there's a lot of things you might not be able to control. But if you can.\r\n\r\n01:31:17.000 --> 01:31:24.000\r\nSpeak up and advocate and say, You know, this is what the research says. Maybe we need to be a little bit more aligned here or there.\r\n\r\n01:31:24.000 --> 01:31:26.000\r\nAnd then I think that's.\r\n\r\n01:31:26.000 --> 01:31:34.000\r\nThat's awesome, you know. We need to be advocates for all students.\r\n\r\n01:31:34.000 --> 01:31:35.000\r\nThank you.\r\n\r\n01:31:35.000 --> 01:31:36.000\r\nAnd thank you for staying late.\r\n\r\n01:31:36.000 --> 01:31:38.000\r\nCool.\r\n\r\n01:31:38.000 --> 01:31:39.000\r\nThis is very helpful.\r\n\r\n01:31:39.000 --> 01:31:40.000\r\nYeah, so this is an amazing after party. But I need to go.\r\n\r\n01:31:40.000 --> 01:31:41.000\r\nThank you guys, I really appreciate that.\r\n\r\n01:31:41.000 --> 01:31:42.000\r\nYeah, I know, I'm like, what.\r\n\r\n01:31:42.000 --> 01:31:43.000\r\nNo, I was hoping.\r\n\r\n01:31:43.000 --> 01:31:44.000\r\nI know drinks on me, though I'm good.\r\n\r\n01:31:44.000 --> 01:31:47.000\r\nThis is a great after party.\r\n\r\n01:31:47.000 --> 01:31:48.000\r\nGreat questions.\r\n\r\n01:31:48.000 --> 01:31:49.000\r\nThanks a lot.\r\n\r\n01:31:49.000 --> 01:31:50.000\r\nThank you.\r\n\r\n01:31:50.000 --> 01:31:51.000\r\nThank you.\r\n\r\n01:31:51.000 --> 01:31:52.000\r\nYou so much. Yup! I'll run to.\r\n\r\n01:31:52.000 --> 01:31:53.000\r\nThank you. This was wonderful.\r\n\r\n01:31:53.000 --> 01:31:54.000\r\nI'm looking forward to the next one, for sure.\r\n\r\n01:31:54.000 --> 01:31:55.000\r\nThank you. Yes, it's a great group, and great questions.\r\n\r\n01:31:55.000 --> 01:31:56.000\r\nOkay, well, I I will get off here now. Thank you all for the great information.\r\n\r\n01:31:56.000 --> 01:31:59.000\r\nThanks.\r\n\r\n01:31:59.000 --> 01:32:03.000\r\nAnd thank you for sending all the resources. I do appreciate that, too.\r\n\r\n01:32:03.000 --> 01:32:04.000\r\nThank you.\r\n\r\n01:32:04.000 --> 01:32:05.000\r\nAnd someone was asking about the survey.\r\n\r\n01:32:05.000 --> 01:32:09.000\r\nI get so caught up. It's nice to review things afterwards.\r\n\r\n01:32:09.000 --> 01:32:10.000\r\nY'all have a good night. Thank you.\r\n\r\n01:32:10.000 --> 01:32:11.000\r\nAlright, and I, recent. Thank you. Have a good night.\r\n\r\n01:32:11.000 --> 01:32:13.000\r\nGreat.\r\n\r\n01:32:13.000 --> 01:32:16.000\r\nWe sent this survey in case still needed that.\r\n\r\n01:32:16.000 --> 01:32:18.000\r\nYeah, I'm just not again.\r\n\r\n01:32:18.000 --> 01:32:21.000\r\nRhonda, did you have a question.\r\n\r\n01:32:21.000 --> 01:32:23.000\r\nYeah, for some reason we can't hear you. Are you on mute.\r\n\r\n01:32:23.000 --> 01:32:25.000\r\nOh, yeah, I think Rhonda's.\r\n\r\n01:32:25.000 --> 01:32:28.000\r\nCan you hear her?\r\n\r\n01:32:28.000 --> 01:32:33.000\r\nYes, I. The chat should be transcribed.\r\n\r\n01:32:33.000 --> 01:32:36.000\r\nThere's so much on here.\r\n\r\n01:32:36.000 --> 01:32:37.000\r\nYes, Jenny, I saved it.\r\n\r\n01:32:37.000 --> 01:32:38.000\r\nThat we need to share. Oh, Rhonda, we can't hear you.\r\n\r\n01:32:38.000 --> 01:32:41.000\r\nWe can't hear you at all, Rhonda.\r\n\r\n01:32:41.000 --> 01:32:43.000\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n01:32:43.000 --> 01:32:45.000\r\nIt shows that you, unmuted, but then unmuted it. We don't.\r\n\r\n01:32:45.000 --> 01:32:48