    "content": "Title: Nov 18, 2024 |\n\nContent: Nov 18, 2024 |  **Planning for Montgomery County w/Noelia Gonzalez (for 1…  Attendees: (<mailto:margarita.marrero@wceps.org>)Margarita Marrero (<mailto:noelia_c_gonzalez@mcpsmd.org>)Gonzalez, Noelia C (<mailto:nora.delgado@wcepspl.org>)Nora Delgado  WCEPS Professional Development Planning Document  Summary of  PD Plan  District:  Date of Call:  Workshop Title & Description:  Maintaining a School-Wide Focus on English Learner success through collaboration  Date(s) of Event(s)/Time  Dec 19, 2024  Time: (include time zone): 8:30-3:30pm (1 hour)  Location(s) of Event(s) or confirmation of zoom registration received  15 W. Gude, Rockville, Maryland 20850 3rd floor  PD Facilitator Contact Information  Nora Burton, CARE Coach  773-556-3243  LEA Contact(s) cell number  Noelia Gonzalez, Instructional Specialist and ELD Coach  Participants  K-5  Anticipated Numbers  Max 50 (currently about 23 signed up)  Position(s) of Participants:  Open to all elementary - usually, mostly ELD but staff PD teachers, and reading specialists may sign up  Logistics  Best airport  Any hotel recommendations  Parking  Building entrance  Technology set up  Site context  ELD is mostly push-in - moving the needle more for co-teaching. Dual Language program (TWI) - another program and group of teachers. A few have signed up.  Airport - Reagan, Dulles, Just north of DC area  Tech - Smartboard, desktop, and HDMI chord are available Building entrance - Security is downstairs and can let in  Goal & How will it be measured?  WCEPS survey - self-assessment for participants  Any additional  notes/questions  Content of the session:  MCPS teachers do have some proficiency with the PLDs and KLUs. Elevating the past work and expanding such as looking at a KLU and what it looks like at each level is a good next step for them.  MCPS is working on and promoting making language visible in instruction. Teachers are familiar with the PLDs, a quick overview will still b