  {
    "id": "0114fac1-faf1-493d-bd7d-92142ae5f1ce",
    "title": "Nov 6, 2024",
    "content": "Title: Nov 6, 2024\n\nContent: Nov 6, 2024  WCEPS  School/District Educators  Yonne Williams – Director of MLL Educator Engagement  Margie Marrero – Associate Director of CARE Coaching  Bryant Jensen,  Professor at BYU  Meeting Overview  Introductions  Immediate questions: What are your needs?  Looking for training to understand the new WIDA framework and grow capacity and understanding for TESOL program  How many Educators? Small group - 6 - 20  ○  Dates: February (suggesting February 7)  ●  Goal: Build understanding of the WIDA ELD Framework (2 days hosted at BYU, one day 6 hours in person, 3 2-hour follow up webinars to address implementation)  ●  Coaching Session  ○  Domain Variety/Topics: Building Capacity for the ELD Framework  ■  Agenda and Objectives  ●  Logistics (Quote to follow)  ●  Total Cost: Quote to follow.  ●  WCEPS Location Needs:  ●  A teaching room for in-person (tables that each seat 4, AV)  Notes/Minutes  Topic idea: Functional approach to language within genre families (building capacity workshop)  Could use applying the framework resource so teachers can use for what it will look like with lesson planning  Budget - The department chair is supportive  If we go to them 5-6 participants - including supervisors for EL practicum; 5 partner districts could be invited  Two-day training  Most EL courses are run by adjunct faculty who come from the district  The second day can allow time for participants to make meaning - this can be chunked into 3 2-hour sessions to allow time for processing and questions to be addressed about implementation  Can figure out a $6500 per day  Agenda descriptions - will send  A one-day workshop with 3 2-hour follow-ups  Tentative February timeframe ",
