  {
    "id": "0c1e6f1f-f1b2-4738-bb6f-ddbed5350f91",
    "title": "Notes - __Noble Planning w_Caitlin",
    "content": "Title: Notes - __Noble Planning w_Caitlin\n\nContent: Dec 4, 2024 | (<https://www.google.com/calendar/event?eid=NjM4bWFkaHRzcGwzMWJlcWxqOGxxazFqMmwgbWFyZ2FyaXRhLm1hcnJlcm9Ad2NlcHMub3Jn>)**Noble Planning w/Caitlin  Attendees: (<mailto:casheridan@nobleschools.org>)Sheridan, Caitlin (<mailto:margarita.marrero@wceps.org>)Margarita Marrero  CARE Coaching PD Plan Multimodal  District: Noble Schools  Date of Planning Call:  Workshop Title:  Designing multimodal instruction to meet the needs of English Learners  Date(s) of Event(s)  Dec 13, 2024  Start/End Time:  10:10-11:40am 12:20-1:50pm  Location(s) of Event(s)  Any details to location? Can I arrive an hour prior to start time?  Chicago Bulls College Prep location  Location:  Chicago Bulls College Prep  2040 W Adams St.  Chicago, IL 60612  PD Facilitator Contact Information  Margie Marrero  915-309-2923  LEA Contact(s) cell number  Caitlin Sheridan  773-505-7466  Workshop description  90-minute workshops - 1 am session and 1 pm  Workshop materials  Padlet  ESOL/ELL Support  Are the ESOL/ELL Educators co-teaching or do they have a session with students? Please provide details  Workshop outcomes  See agenda below  [Ask LEA to share her for vision or main goals for this session] Multimodal concept (student-centered learning goal)  One in-depth strategy and time to discuss how it fits into the classroom  Students do the cognitive lift  Anticipated numbers  [Max 45]  Position(s) of participants  1st session - currently 10 people including multilingual coordinators and general content area teachers  2nd session - 3 currently (deadline is Friday) - 1 is ML Coordinator, ESL teacher and 1 content teacher  Teaching/Learning context  [e.g., LIEP program, co-teaching, exit criteria, student grouping, etc.]  Set up of learning space/Travel  Hotel - by Westloop area  Uber and public transportation  (street parking)  Recommend flying into O’hare blueline takes downtown  Text Caitlin when I’m at the front of the building  Entrance is on Adams street (use front entrance on Adams)  Send anything ahead like padlet or if decide on virtual handout  Materials Requested (in-person)  Projector, screen, speakers  Sticky chart paper, sticky notes, enough markers for groups of 4  Internet access  Tables set up to sit 4-5 educators per table  Questions from the LEA  WCEPS Professional Development Planning Document ",
