  {
    "id": "6a4d7c28-4327-41d1-bdd2-66327eb47e92",
    "title": "Coaching Overview: Pre-planning call August 2, 2024 for October 10 coaching event",
    "content": "Title: Coaching Overview: Pre-planning call August 2, 2024 for October 10 coaching event\n\nContent: Coaching Overview: Pre-planning call August 2, 2024 for October 10 coaching event  WCEPS  School/District Educators  Yvonne Williams – Director of MLL Educator Engagement Marisa Silva – WCEPS CARE Coach  (202) 744-8277  Adefule, Kunbi <kadefule@nobleschools.org  Training Location Details – TBD; Additional planning call forthcoming following receipt of  P.O.  #2 (see Action Items below)  {School building TBD, but both coaches will be in the same building on all 3 district coaching dates}  Address: Special Instructions (entry): Coaches request access to the learning space approximately 1 hour before the session begins, if possible. Technology: Projector, speakers Room setup: TABLE GROUPS OF 4 Supplies / materials: chart paper, markers,  highlighters, post its, and blank printer paper Participants should each have a laptop / computer / tablet.  Meeting notes  Introductions  Overview  How many Educators? (not over 50 per session) LEA anticipates using classrooms as presentation spaces, in which case participant groups would be capped at approximately 30.  Any additional needs or considerations?  This academic year (2023-2024) has been the first year that language objectives are utilized district-wide (https://nobleschools.org) and support is needed for content area teachers in planning with ELD framework. Goal: Offer two 1-day in-person coaching events (2 coaches each day) during each Network PD Day in 2024-2025 o Dates: Quarter 1 Network PD Day: October 10, 2024 – Coaches TBD  o  Quarter 2 Network PD Day: December 13, 2024  o  Quarter 3 Network PD Day: February 13, 2024  o  See below for LEA’s selection of workshops as of August 2, 2024  Session Details – TBD during planning call for October 10 sessions  AM Session (start / end time)  Lunch (minimum of 1 hour)  PM Session (start / end time)  What are the particular grade-level bands, numbers, demographics?  SLIFE / Newcomers? Not many newcomers are present; many newcomers in the district arriving from Venezuela mostly have elementary age students (district-wide, this overall population is roughly 50 – largest clusters include Ukraine, Haiti, Colombia, Venezuela); several schools have zero newcomers. SLIFE population is also small.  District concerns or instructions: As of last academic year, focusing on multilingual learners was not a primary focus; there is a bit of reluctance on the part of some of the teachers.  Dates: Quarter 1 Network PD Day: October 10, 2024  ▪  1 coach, full-day session of Building Capacity to Bridge Content Learning and Language Development {this session is foundational, and primarily geared towards content teachers who are not familiar with the WIDA ELD 2020 Framework, and / or ELD teachers who desire a refresher  ▪  1 coach, full-day session of Applying the {WIDA 2020 ELD} Framework {this session is for those who are ready to roll up their sleeves and participate in a guided envisioning or re-envisioning of a past or future lesson or unit plan with content standards and language development in mind}  Quarter 2 Network PD Day: December 13, 2024  ▪  1 coach, full-day session of Integrating Content Learning & Language Development in Lesson Planning ▪ 1 coach, full-day session of Designing Multimodal Instruction to Meet the Needs of English Learners Quarter 3 Network PD Day: February 13, 2024  ▪  1 coach, full-day session of Engaging English Learners in Science Classrooms  ▪  1 coach, full-day session of Engaging English Learners in Social Studies Classrooms  Addendum: Additional Meeting held August 2, 2024  The district is in possession of an additional funding windfall and will use these funds to expand the professional learning offerings for 2024-2025. LEA requested a quote (sent 8/1/24) for 3 additional PD/Workshop sessions (on the same district dates as stated above). Quote was sent to Noble UIC College Prep (1231 S Damen Ave, Chicago, IL 60608).  Noble Schools’ goal and vision for the parallel sessions taught on 10/10, 12/13 and 2/13 is to improve best practices in ML instruction for their district’s teachers.  Action Items  ▪  Noble Schools should receive district funding for workshop 2 on October 10 by August 23, 2024, and will remit payment at that time for the second workshop  o  workshop 1 for October 10 was paid in full by May 31, 2024  ▪  WCEPS will confirm 2 coaches for October 10 coaching events and schedule a planning call once the funding for 10/10 workshop 2 is remitted  o  Planning call will likely be scheduled in the first half of September 2024  ▪  Marisa will send agendas for the October 10 offerings by COB August 2, 2024 ",
