  {
    "id": "e12a19c7-7fe9-4700-9ad4-604be23634c2",
    "title": "Applying the ELD Framework for Effective Instruction",
    "content": "Title: Applying the ELD Framework for Effective Instruction\n\nContent: Applying the ELD Framework for Effective Instruction  Description: This workshop build and extends the Building Capacity series, focusing on bridging content and language. Participants will delve into the four components of the 2020 framework, using a comprehensive instructional planning template to connect these components to their teaching practices. This template guides educators in integrating content and language, applying a functional approach to language, and using ELD standards to enhance student learning. This workshop can be an extension or as a stand alone to suport teachers in implementing the framework using a template to guide their planning and understanding.  By the end of this workshop, participants will be able to:  •  Utilize the instructional planning template to connect the four components of the 2020 framework to their instruction.  •  Integrate content and language effectively in their lesson plans.  •  Identify and align ELD standards with content learning objectives.  •  Determine key language uses connected to culminating activities.  •  Prioritize language functions and features within their teaching practices.  •  Use proficiency level descriptors to evaluate student work across three dimensions of language: discourse, sentence, and word/phrase. ",
