    "id": "b322e9b3-9e64-4a9d-8665-5c7e370e2c33",
    "title": "CARE Coaching Professional Learning Program Overview",
    "content": "CARE Coaching Professional Learning Program - Advancing Equitable Educational Opportunities\n\nCARE Coaching is a professional learning program through WCEPS designed to ensure educators provide equitable educational opportunities for multilingual learners. The CARE approach is: Collaborative, Actionable, Responsive, and Empowering.\n\nTHE THREE Cs OF CARE COACHING:\n1. Continuous Learning - Enable educators to meet needs of all learners with emphasis on multilingual learners\n2. Consulting - Highly qualified coaches consult with administrators for student success through technical assistance and program review\n3. Coaching - Meet you where you are and get where you want to go with guiding questions, reflection, sharing, and goal setting\n\nFOUNDATIONAL PRINCIPLES OFFERINGS:\n\nBuilding Capacity to Bridge Content Learning and Language Development\n- Explore connections between grade-level content standards and language development standards\n- Learn to provide equity and access through a functional approach to language learning\n- Make connections between content and language using language functions and features\n\nPromoting Equity through Culturally Responsive Pedagogy\n- Build shared understanding of equity\n- Describe impacts of culture on learning\n- Identify and describe components of culturally responsive pedagogy\n\nMaintaining School-Wide Focus on English Learner Success through Collaboration\n- Build common understanding of collaboration\n- Define types of educator collaboration\n- Explore collaborative practices and solutions to challenges\n\nUnderstanding Identification, Programming & Proficiency Levels (mainstream teachers)\n- Understand different types of English proficiency level scores\n- Use scores to inform instruction\n- Understand student processing and language production at five proficiency levels\n\nINSTRUCTIONAL DESIGN OFFERINGS:\n\nDesigning Multi-Modal Instruction to Meet Needs of English Learners\n- Describe principles of UDL (Universal Design for Learning)\n- Develop and deliver instruction addressing readiness within English proficiency levels\n- Design learning opportunities leveraging learners strengths, interests and preferences\n\nPromoting Autonomy through Formative Assessment Practices\n- Use learning goals and success criteria to clarify expectations\n- Engage students in meaning-making tasks supporting content learning and academic language development\n- Foster constructive feedback promoting student agency and self-regulated learning\n\nIntegrating Content Learning & Language Development in Lesson Planning\n- Develop instruction promoting student engagement and equitable access to grade-level concepts\n- Articulate learning goals and success criteria\n- Develop activities with multiple modes of communication and purposeful language use\n- Integrate varied supports based on student needs\n\nEngaging in Reflective Practice through Classroom-Based Data Analysis (2-day offering)\n- Reflect on instructional practices and identify changes\n- Determine data collection methods\n- Develop action plans\n- Analyze data to identify patterns and determine impact\n\nCONTENT-BASED INSTRUCTION:\n\nEngaging English Learners in Science Classrooms\n- Understand academic language expectations in science\n- Explore strategies for language-rich environment\n- Link content knowledge and academic language\n- Focus on genres to support academic discourse\n\nEngaging English Learners in Math Classrooms\n- Combine ELD Standards with Standards for Mathematical Practice (SMPs)\n- Understand and use academic language in math\n- Create language-rich environment\n- Apply language amplifications to math content lessons\n\nSPECIAL POPULATIONS:\n\nCreating an Inclusive Learning Environment (IEP focus)\n- Tailor instruction to variety of proficiency levels\n- Develop instruction addressing readiness within English proficiency levels\n- Design learning opportunities leveraging strengths, interests, and preferences\n\nEmpowering Newcomers for Academic Success\n- Describe elements of scaffolding for Newcomers\n- Incorporate strategies ensuring grade-level content accessible to Newcomers\n- Develop lessons with scaffolding and student supports for Newcomers\n- Leverage learners strengths, interests, and preferences\n\nSupporting Students with Limited or Interrupted Formal Education (SLIFE)\n- Define and recognize characteristics of SLIFE label\n- Determine how to engage SLIFE students in grade-level instruction\n- Use data to advocate for informed decisions about instructional programming\n- Discuss unique learning needs of SLIFE students\n\nFAMILY ENGAGEMENT:\n\nBuilding Community with Multilingual Learners through Family Engagement\n- Define family engagement\n- Consider research supporting family engagement\n- Examine cultural proficiency\n- Identify ways to extend learning\n- Create environment leveraging families as resources\n- Honor culture to foster inclusive learning community\n\nLITERACY DEVELOPMENT:\n\nEnhancing Writing Proficiency through Literacy Learning Cycle (1 & 2-day options)\n- Learn apprenticeship approach to writing instruction (Teaching and Learning Cycle)\n- Use mentor texts to explore purposes, structures and language features of genres\n- Plan joint text construction with students\n- Support independent writing\n- Engage students in drafting, reviewing, and revising\n\nDISCOURSE:\n\nThe Discussion Project\n- Learn research-based techniques for equitable, inclusive, engaging classroom discussion\n- Build and maintain community\n- Structure discussion and craft questions\n- Facilitate whole class interactions\n- Plan and assess discussion\n\nBILINGUAL OFFERINGS (Delivered in Spanish):\n\nLa Importancia de la ludica a traves de estrategias de ensenanza\n- Promover ensenanza ludica mediante estrategias de rigor y relevancia para estudiantes bi/multilingues\n- Aplicar estrategias pedagogicas bajo enfoque ludico centrado en contexto sociocultural y linguistico\n- Cambiar aspectos de ensenanza tradicionalista a ensenanza ludica de empoderamiento\n\nContact: Yvonne Williams - WCEPS Pathways for personalized guidance",
