    "title": "Logan Edwards - The Discussion Project",
    "content": "Description: Logan Edwards is a Curriculum Designer and Instructor for The Discussion Project. He is a trained diversity, equity and inclusion (DEI) workshop facilitator.\n\nSelect Page Leadership Logan Edwards Curriculum Designer & Instructor Logan Edwards is a professor/lecturer of health education and promotion, and a Master Certified Health Education Specialist (MCHES) registered by the National Commission for Health Education Credentialing (NCHEC). He was the recipient of his College of Education’s Teacher of Distinction Award, where he is recognized for specializing in effective teacher education, integrating mental health education into health education classrooms, and other public health, health equity, and behavioral health related topics. He is also a trained diversity, equity, and inclusion (DEI) workshop facilitator for higher education professionals with the National Coalition Building Institute (NCBI). Logan Edwards Curriculum Designer & Instructor Logan Edwards is a professor/lecturer of health education and promotion, and a Master Certified Health Education Specialist (MCHES) registered by the National Commission for Health Education Credentialing (NCHEC). He was the recipient of his College of Education’s Teacher of Distinction Award, where he is recognized for specializing in effective teacher education, integrating mental health education into health education classrooms, and other public health, health equity, and behavioral health related topics. He is also a trained diversity, equity, and inclusion (DEI) workshop facilitator for higher education professionals with the National Coalition Building Institute (NCBI). Discover more team members The Discussion Project is developed by leading educators at the University of Wisconsin-Madison. Coursework is designed to improve classroom discussion and leads to higher levels of engagement, belonging, and learning for students. Learn more about the leadership team and how they can help you