  {
    "id": "ec48737a-b777-4d4d-9fc5-6d899cabd11b",
    "title": "A A A CARE Coaching Advancing Equitable Educational Opportunities",
    "content": "A A A CARE Coaching Advancing Equitable Educational Opportunities  Program Overview  CARE Coaching, a professional learning program offered through the Wisconsin Center for Education Products and Services, is designed to ensure that district-and school-based educators provide equitable educational opportunities for multilingual learners. The CARE Coaching approach cultivates engagement in professional learning that is: Collaborative, Actionable, Responsive, and Empowering.  cormmur.iitY..  CARE Coaches foster meaningful relationships and develop productive partnerships that elicit the strengths, knowledge, and expertise of all participants, while providing opportunities for growth across the learning community.  The Three Cs of CARE Coaching  Continuous  Learning  Continuous learning opportunities enable educators to meet the needs of all learners with an emphasis on the unique needs of multilingual learners across K-72 classrooms.  Consulting  Highly qualified CARE Coaches consult directly with school-and district-level administrators to ensure the success of all students, including multilingual learners through various forms of technical assistance and program review and evaluation  Coaching  CARE Coaches meet you where you are and get where you want to go! During coaching sessions, whether in-person or on line, coaches offer guiding questions, opportunities for reflection, time for sharing and debriefing, and goal setting for ongoing work.  Foundational Principles  Topic: Building Capacity to Bridge Content Learning and Language Development  Description: Pa rtici pants explore connections between grade-level content standards and language development standards  through language expectations. Educators will consider how  to provide equity and access through a functional approach to  language learning.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Describe a language development framework  •  Make connections between content and language  •  Use lang. functions and features to establish learning goals  •  Design learning opportunities through a functional  approach to language learning  !Topic: Promoting Equity through Culturally Responsive Pedagogy  l  Description: Participants explore responsive pedagogical practices to meet the needs of culturally and linguistically diverse students.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Build a shared understanding of \"equity\"  •  Describe impacts of culture on learning  •  Identify and describe components of culturally responsive pedagogy  !Topic: Maintaining a School-Wide Focus on English Learner Success through Collaboration  l  Description: Participants explore components of a collaborative culture that support partnerships across the school community.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Build a common understanding of collaboration  •  Define types of educator collaboration  •  Explore collaborative practices  •  Consider challenges and explore solutions  !Topic: Understanding Identification, Programming & Proficiency Levels (mainstream teachers)  I  Description: Participants examine the different types of  English proficiency level scores, their use to inform instruction  and students' processing and language production at each of the five levels of English proficiency.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Build a common understanding of collaboration  •  Define types of educator collaboration  •  Explore collaborative practices  •  Consider challenges and explore solutions  Łr:ŁŁŁ11 Łl .. lllM:.l..Ł  Topic: Designing Multi-Modal Instruction to Meet the Needs of English Learners  Description: Participants examine several interconnected  elements of Universal Design for Learning in a practical  approach to planning and developing classroom-based  differentiation to make grade-level content accessible to  students at all levels of English language proficiency.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Describe the principles of UDL  •  Develop and deliver instruction that addresses readiness,  especially within the context of English proficiency levels  •  Design learning opportunities that leverage learners'  strengths, interests and preferences  Topic: Promoting Autonomy through Formative Assessment Practices  Description: Participants design effective classroom-based  formative assessments practices that enable them to gauge English learner student growth, at various English proficiency  levels and wide-ranging educational backgrounds, toward  mastery based on learning goals and success criteria, which students can also use to monitor their progress and self- assess.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Use learning goals and success criteria to clarify  expectations for content learning and language use  •  Engage students in meaning-making tasks that support  content learning and academic language development. •  Foster constructive feedback which promotes student agency and self-regulated learning.  Topic: Integrating Content Learning & Language Development in Lesson Planning  I Description: Participants learn how to develop instruction  that promotes student engagement, ensures equitable  access to grade-level concepts, and accelerates content  learning and language development.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Describe culturally responsive instructional practices •  Articulate learning goals and success criteria.  •  Develop activities with multiple modes of communication  and purposeful language use  •  Integrate varied supports based on student needs  Topic: Engaging in Reflective Practice through Classroom-Based Data Analysis (2-day offering)  Description: Participants examine their practice and its effect on student achievement. Classroom-based action research promotes equity through reflective pedagogical practice designed to improve teaching and learning. This session enables teachers to engage in purposeful reflection to identify changes that will promote growth that will positively impact outcomes for English learners.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Reflect on instructional practices  •  Identify a change in practice  •  Determine what type of data to collect  •  Develop an action plan  A follow-up workshop enables participants to:  •  Analyze data to identify patterns and determine impact  •  Determine next steps  Topic: Engaging English Learners in Science Classrooms  Description: Participants develop a common understanding of academic language expectations in science and explore strategies to foster a language-rich environment. Through hands-on experiments and analysis of language embedded within the content and practices, participants will have a deeper understanding of how to engage language learners of a variety of proficiency levels.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Describe the role of collaboration in science  •  Consider student assets for learning  •  Recognize the impact of race, culture, and language in the learning process  •  Link content knowledge and academic language  •  Focus on genres to support academic discourse  Topic: Engaging English Learners in Math Classrooms  Description: Participants will combine English Language Development Standards and Standards for Mathematical Practice {SMPs) for English Language Learners. Participants will work with other teachers to understand and use academic language in math, and discover how to create a language rich environment for their students. Participants will also analyze and apply the language and content of math to their own lessons.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Analyze Standards for Mathematical Practice {SMPs)  •  Connect ELD Standards to SMPs  •  Identify opportunities for language amplifications in a math content lesson  •  Apply language amplifications to an upcoming math content lesson  Topic: Creating an Inclusive Learning Environment (IEP focus)  Description: Participants will be introduced to foundational principles for making grade-level content accessible to students at all levels of English language proficiency.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Tailor instruction to a variety of proficiency levels  •  Develop and deliver instruction that addresses readiness, especially within the context of English proficiency levels  •  Design learning opportunities that leverage learners' strengths, interests, and preferences  Topic: Empowering Newcomers for Academic Success  Description:  NEW OFFERING: Description COMING SOON  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Describe elements of scaffolding for Newcomers  •  Incorporate strategies to ensure grade-level content is accessible to Newcomers  •  Develop lessons that incorporate scaffolding of content and student supports for Newcomers  •  Identify ways to leverage learners' strengths, interests, and preferences  Topic: Supporting Students with Limited or Interrupted Formal Education (SLIFE)  Description: Participants will be introduced to SLIFE (Students  with Limited and Informal Education). This session will help  recognize who these students are, explore supports for classroom and instructional support, and use data to make informed instructional decisions.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Define and recognize characteristics of a SLIFE label  •  Determine how to engage SLIFE students in grade level instruction  •  Use data to advocate with leaders on making informed decisions about instructional programming for SLIFE students or to discuss the unique learning needs of SLIFE  Family Engagement  Description: Participants explore the value of building community and examines the components of effective family partnerships. Content includes creating an environment that leverages families as reliable resources for engaging students and honoring culture to foster an inclusive learning community.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Define family engagement  •  Consider research that supports family engagement  •  Examine cultural proficiency  •  Identify ways to extend learning  Topic: Enhancing Writing Proficiency through a Literacy Learning Cycle (1 & 2-days available )  Description: Participants develop an apprenticeship approach to writing instruction known as the Teaching and Learning Cycle. It is a framework designed to scaffold academic writing instruction through interactive reading, academic discussions, and language development. It can be adapted to different grade levels and content areas, enabling English learners to become effective and informed writers across the curriculum.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Share understanding of how students write knowledgeably  •  Use mentor texts to explore the purposes, organizational structures and language features of specific genres  •  Plan for joint construct a text with students based on what was learned from various mentor texts  •  Support students with their independent writing  •  Engage students in drafting, reviewing, and revising  Discourse  Topic: The Discussion Project  Description: This highly interactive professional learning course provides research-based techniques to design and implement equitable, inclusive, and engaging classroom discussion. The course provides in-depth learning, focused on designing, implementing, and facilitating high-quality classroom discussion.  After participating in this workshop, participants will be able to ...  •  Build and maintain community  •  Structuring discussion and crafting questions  •  Facilitate whole class interactions  •  Plan and Assess discussion  Wisconsin Center for Education Products and Services {WCEPS) provides the Discussion Project with permission of the University of Wisconsin-Madison. Discussion Project and the Discussion Project logo are trademarks of the Board of Regents of the UW System.  Topic: La lmportancia de la ludica a traves de estrategias de ensenanza  Description:  NEW OFFERING: Description COMING SOON  Al termino de este taller los participantes podran:  •  Promover la ensenanza ludica mediante estrategias divertidas de rigor y relevancia para estudiantes bi/multilingues  •  Aplicar estrategias pedag6gicas en el aula bajo un enfoque ludico centrado en el contexto sociocultural y lingufstico de los estudiantes bi/multilingues  •  Cambiar aspectos de la ensenanza tradicionalista a una ensenanza ludica de empoderamiento ",
