    "id": "46945e47-22f0-457d-9178-93ca5bfea123",
    "title": "Terms",
    "content": "Description: Callsurveyv2\n\nTerms of UseWelcome to this website (\"Website\") provided by the Wisconsin Center for Education Products and Services (“WCEPS”) which provides access to the Comprehensive Assessment of Leadership for Learning (“CALL”). CALL is an online formative assessment tool designed to improve leadership for learning in schools. Your registration, access and use of CALL and this Website is subject to the following Terms of Service. Please read these Terms of Service carefully before using this Website or registering to access or use CALL, so that you fully understand your rights and responsibilities. These Terms of Service together with the CALL Privacy Policy constitute an agreement between you (and the school or district that you represent) and WCEPS regarding use of CALL and this Website.By accessing or using this Website or completing your registration for CALL, you agree to these Terms of Service. Please print a copy of these Terms of Service for your reference. If you do not agree to the following Terms of Service, do not access or use this Website and you will not be permitted access to CALL.AuthorityBy entering into these Terms of Service, you are representing to WCEPS that you have the right and authority to enter into these Terms of Service for the purchase of access to CALL, use of CALL and use of this Website on behalf of yourself and the school or school district that you represent.Modifications to Terms of ServiceWCEPS MAY REVISE THESE TERMS OF SERVICE AT ANY TIME. SHOULD ANY REVISIONS BE MADE, WCEPS WILL GIVE NOTICE TO YOU AND ALL USERS BY POSTING A NOTICE REGARDING THE REVISIONS ON THIS WEBSITE OR ONLINE VIA CALL PRIOR TO THEIR EFFECTIVE DATE, AND THE NEW REVISIONS WILL BE EFFECTIVE AS OF THEIR POSTING. BY ACCESSING OR USING THIS WEBSITE OR CALL AFTER SUCH REVISIONS ARE POSTED YOU AGREE AND CONSENT TO ALL SUCH REVISIONS.Site InformationInformation displayed on this Website or via CALL is subject to modification without notice. WCEPS reserves the right to modify such information without any obligation to notify past, current or prospective users. Some services may not be available in certain areas. WCEPS makes no representations that the materials on this Website or CALL are appropriate or available for use in any particular state or other countries besides the United States. Those who do access this Website or CALL are solely responsible for compliance with the laws of the state or country in which they reside. All offers set forth on this Website are void where prohibited, and are subject to the posting of any official rules pertaining to such offers.Privacy PolicyAccess to this Website and/or CALL may be monitored from time to time. Your use of this Website and/or CALL constitutes your consent to such monitoring and data collection as set forth in our Privacy Policy.RegistrationYou may request access to CALL using the Website registration process. If you request registration to access CALL(or such registration is requested on your behalf) and your registration is approved by WCEPS, you will be provided with access to CALL, a user name, and password via the email provided during registration. You are responsible for all activity under your user name. You have the sole responsibility for ensuring the confidentiality of the user name and password for your account. You agree to immediately notify WCEPS of any unauthorized use of your account or any user name assigned to your account and any other breach of security of which you become aware.PricesPrices remain valid while they are listed and offered on this Order Page. WCEPS reserves the right, without liability or prior notice, to revise or cease to make CALL available. The price of access to CALL will be the price posted on the Order Page as of the date of the order.TaxesYou are responsible for any and all sales, use, excise, and other taxes, import duties and charges levied as a result of your order.PaymentYou must submit the necessary credit card information when you place an order to access CALL. If the card information you submit is incorrect or invalid, your payment or order will not be processed. Payment is subject to the approval of the financial institution issuing the card. Neither WCEPS nor its third party payment processor has any responsibility or liability if the financial institution refuses to accept or honor your card for any reason. WCEPS works with a third party payment processor to help ensure the security of your credit card data as further set forth in our Privacy Policy. All fees are nonrefundable unless otherwise expressly stated in these Terms of Service.TerminationYou may terminate your account and access to CALL at any time. Furthermore, WCEPS can suspend or terminate your access to CALL at any time in the event that WCEPS ceases providing CALL as a service or WCEPS reasonably believes that you have breached these Terms of Service or any other posted terms. Our failure to enforce any right, or failure to take action against you regarding your breach of this Agreement will not be a waiver by us of any later right or breach and termination of your access does not preclude WCEPS from pursing other damages and causes of action.Intellectual Property RightsCopyright in CALL and related materials licensed by WCEPS are owned by Leadership for Learning LLC and used under exclusive license by WCEPS. The copyright owner reserves all rights in and to their copyrights All rights reserved.The content on CALL and this Website, including without limitation the text, trademarks, graphics, logos, button icons, images, video or audio clips, digital downloads, data compilations, software, the compilation of content, arrangement, organization, design, trade dress and look and feel of CALL is the property of WCEPS or its licensors. CALL and this Website may also contain various third-party names and marks that are the property of their respective owners. This intellectual property may be protected under applicable United States and international patent, copyright, trademark and other intellectual property laws.Any unauthorized use of the marks or of our copyrighted material or trade dress or any other intellectual property available on or through CALL or this Website is strictly prohibited and may be prosecuted to the fullest extent that the law provides.License to AccessAccess to CALL is limited to you and those personnel that are authorized by you. You may view, copy, print and use content contained on CALL solely for your own personal use, provided that: (1) it is used for informational and non-commercial purposes only; (2) no text, graphics or other content available from this CALL is modified or framed in any way; and (3) no graphics available from CALL are used, copied or distributed separate from accompanying text. The use of any content for commercial purposes is expressly prohibited. Nothing in this Agreement is intended to, or may be construed as, conferring by implication, estoppel or otherwise any license or other grant of right to use any patent, copyright, trademark, service mark or other intellectual property of WCEPS or any third party, except as expressly provided in this section.You may not use, copy, modify, distribute, translate, reproduce, republish, disassemble, reverse engineer, decompile, mirror, frame, hyperlink or transmit any of the content or materials of CALL or rent or sell use of or access to (such as on a time share or service bureau basis) CALL, or any of the content or materials on CALL. You may not permit third parties to access CALL or use any CALL content and may not make any other use of CALL or any CALL content except as set forth in this Agreement. You agree to use CALL and the Website for lawful purposes only. You may not post or transmit through CALL any material (i) that violates or infringes in any way upon the rights of others, (ii) that is unlawful, threatening, abusive, defamatory, invasive of privacy or publicity rights, vulgar, obscene, profane or otherwise objectionable, (iii) that encourages conduct that would constitute a criminal offense, give rise to civil liability or otherwise violate any law, or (iv) that contains advertising or any solicitation. Any conduct by you that, in our discretion, restricts or inhibits any other person from using or enjoying CALL will not be permitted.You understand and agree that WCEPS may terminate or otherwise deny your access to CALL and without notice in the event WCEPS believes in its sole discretion that (i) you have violated a provision of this Agreement, (ii) you have used or misused CALL in a manner that WCEPS has determined is unlawful, unethical or otherwise inappropriate, or (iii) such action is reasonably necessary to protect a third party or WCEPS or if such action is otherwise required by law. You acknowledge and agree (1) that your use of CALL is at your own discretion and risk, (2) that use of any material, information or data downloaded or otherwise obtained through the use of CALL is at your own discretion and risk, and (3) that you are solely responsible for any damage to your computer system for loss of data that results from the download of such material, information or data, and for any other form of damage that may be incurred.SupportSupport for use of CALL is available via the \"Help\" function.Survey ResponsesAll of the survey responses from your school submitted via CALL will be combined together and reported back to you to inform school improvement planning. You, as the school administrator, will not have any access to the name or any personally identifiable information that would allow you to identify any specific responses to the survey questions. In addition, data from your school that may contain personally identifiable information such as your name and email address will be combined with data from other schools for use in research studies on school leadership and school effectiveness by third party research partners (“Research Data”). Research Data may be transferred to such third party researchers either with or without the payment of a fee. Your name and the name of the school will not be identified in any subsequent reports or publications that result from this research. You expressly consent to our transfer, including sale, of Research Data to third party research partners for the purpose of conducting academic research.Warranty DisclaimerCALL, THE WEBSITE, AND ALL INFORMATION, SERVICES AND RELATED MATERIALS ARE PROVIDED \"AS IS,\" “AS AVAILABLE” AND “WITH ALL FAULTS.” WCEPS MAKES NO REPRESENTATION OR WARRANTY WHATSOEVER REGARDING THE COMPLETENESS, ACCURACY, CURRENCY, OR ADEQUACY OF, OR THE SUITABILITY, FUNCTIONALITY, AVAILABILITY, OR OPERATION OF CALL, THE WEBSITE, OR THE INFORMATION OR MATERIALS IT CONTAINS. TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMISSIBLE UNDER APPLICABLE LAW, WCEPS AND ITS RESPECTIVE AFFILIATES AND VENDORS, SPECIFICALLY DISCLAIM ALL WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, WITH RESPECT TO CALL, THE WEBSITE AND THE INFORMATION AND MATERIALS CONTAINED THEREIN, INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE AND NON- INFRINGEMENT AND ANY WARRANTIES ARISING FROM A COURSE OF DEALING OR USAGE IN TRADE. USE OF THE INTERNET IS INHERENTLY UNRELIABLE. AS A RESULT, WCEPS DOES NOT WARRANT THAT CALL OR YOUR ACCESS TO CALL WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED OR ERROR-FREE, THAT DEFECTS IN CALL WILL BE CORRECTED, OR THAT CALL OR THE SERVER THAT MAKES IT AVAILABLE ARE FREE OF VIRUSES OR OTHER HARMFUL COMPONENTS. WCEPS MAKES NO WARRANTIES OR REPRESENTATIONS REGARDING THE USE OR THE RESULTS OF THE USE OF THE MATERIALS IN CALL IN TERMS OF THEIR CORRECTNESS, ACCURACY, RELIABILITY, OR OTHERWISE.WHILE WCEPS TAKES COMMERCIALLY REASONABLE EFFORTS TO PROTECT THE PRIVACY AND CONFIDENTIALITY OF YOUR INFORMATION AND TRANSACTIONS, WCEPS CANNOT ENSURE ANY INTERNET TRANSACTION IS COMPLETELY SECURE. WCEPS AND ITS VENDORS USE INDUSTRY STANDARD TECHNOLOGY TO HELP PROTECT AGAINST THE LOSS, MISUSE AND ALTERATION OF THE INFORMATION UNDER WCEPS' CONTROL; HOWEVER, WCEPS DOES NOT GUARANTEE THAT SUCH LOSS, MISUSE OR ALTERATION WILL NOT OCCUR. YOU UNDERSTAND THAT USE OF THE INTERNET AND CALL IS AT YOUR OWN RISK. WCEPS IS NOT RESPONSIBLE FOR ANY VIRUS OR DAMAGE TO YOUR COMPUTER, COMPUTER SOFTWARE, OR ANY LOSS OF DATA THAT MAY RESULT FROM USE OF THE WEBSITE OR ACCESS TO ANY CONTENT OR SERVICES.Either CALL and/or the Website may be unavailable from time to time due to mechanical, telecommunication, software, and third-party vendor failures. WCEPS cannot predict or control when such downtime may occur and cannot control the duration of such downtime. As a result, WCEPS cannot and does not have any liability for such failures. No advice or information from WCEPS in any manner will create any warranty as to the Website or any product, service or material available through the Website, including without limitation CALL. If for any reason you are not satisfied with CALL or its content, your sole remedy is to cease using CALL or such content, even if such remedy should fail of its essential purpose. Applicable law may not allow the exclusion of implied warranties, so the above exclusion may not apply to you.LIMITATION OF LIABILITYIN NO EVENT WILL WCEPS OR ANY OF ITS RESPECTIVE VENDORS, AFFILIATES, OFFICERS, MEMBERS, REPRESENTATIVES, SUPPLIERS, DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, CONSULTANTS, OWNERS, OR AGENTS BE LIABLE FOR DAMAGES OF ANY KIND, INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION ANY DAMAGES FOR LOSS OF USE, DATA, INFORMATION, PROFITS, BUSINESS, REVENUE, EXPECTED SAVINGS OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION, OR ANY DIRECT, SPECIAL, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, EXEMPLARY, PUNITIVE OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES ARISING FROM OR OTHERWISE RELATED TO THE WEBSITE, CALL OR YOUR USE OF CALL, WHETHER SUCH DAMAGES ARE BASED IN TORT, CONTRACT, NEGLIGENCE, STRICT LIABILITY OR OTHERWISE, EVEN IF WCEPS HAS BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES OR SUCH DAMAGES WERE OTHERWISE FORESEEABLE. YOUR SOLE AND EXCLUSIVE REMEDY IN THE EVENT OF SUCH DAMAGE IS TO DISCONTINUE YOUR ACCESS TO AND USE OF CALL. NOTWITHSTANDING THE FOREGOING, IN ANY EVENT, THE AGGREGATE LIABILITY OF WCEPS FOR ANY REASON SHALL NOT EXCEED $100.00 US, EVEN IF SUCH REMEDY SHOULD FAIL OF ITS ESSENTIAL PURPOSE.IndemnificationYOU AGREE TO DEFEND, INDEMNIFY AND HOLD HARMLESS WCEPS AND ITS OFFICERS, DIRECTORS, REPRESENTATIVES, EMPLOYEES, CONSULTANTS, AND AGENTS FROM AND AGAINST ANY CLAIMS, ALLEGATIONS, DAMAGES, LOSSES, LIABILITIES OR EXPENSES (INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO ATTORNEYS' FEES) THAT WCEPS MAY SUFFER OR INCUR AS A RESULT OF (I) YOUR USE OR MISUSE OF CALL, (II) YOUR INFRINGEMENT OF ANY INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY OR OTHER RIGHT OF WCEPS, OR ANY OTHER PERSON OR ENTITY, (III) YOUR VIOLATION OF ANY APPLICABLE LAW, INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION ANY PRIVACY OR DATA SECURITY LAW OR (IV) YOUR VIOLATION OF THIS AGREEMENT. NOTWITHSTANDING THE FOREGOING, WCEPS RESERVES THE RIGHT TO PARTICIPATE IN THE DEFENSE OF ANY SUCH CLAIM, SUBJECT TO YOUR INDEMNIFICATION OBLIGATION.International Data Transfer“Personal Data” shall mean all personal data (as defined in the Data Protection Legislation) controlled by you which is processed by WCEPS in order to process the District’s order;“Provided Materials” means all materials, data and content owned and/or licensed by you which are made available to WCEPS in order to process your order;“Data Protection Legislation” means (i) any legislation in force related to the European Community's Directive 95/46/EC and Directive 2002/58/EC, including but not limited to the Data Protection Act of 1998 and the Privacy and Electronic Communications (EC Directive) Regulations 2003; (ii) from 25 May 2018 only, Regulation (EU) 2016/679 on the protection of natural persons with regard to the processing of Personal Data and on the free movement of such data (the \"GDPR\"); and (iii) any other legislation in force from time to time in the United Kingdom relating to privacy and/or the processing of Personal DataThe terms “process”, “data controller”, “data processor” and “data subject” shall have the meanings set out in the Data Protection Legislation.To the extent relevant, You shall comply with the Data Protection Legislation as regards the Personal Data. The parties agree that you shall be the data controller and WCEPS shall be a data processor of any District Personal Data. You warrant that your instructions to WCEPS in respect of the District Personal Data are lawful. 1. WCEPS shall to the extent it is acting as a data processor under the Agreement:1.1. comply with the requirements of the Data Protection Legislation when processing the Personal Data;1.2. only process Personal Data to the extent necessary to provide the services under this Agreement and to do so in accordance with your documented instructions, including with regard to transfers, unless required to do otherwise by applicable law. In which event, WCEPS shall inform you of the legal requirement before processing the Personal Data other than in accordance with your instructions, unless legally prohibited from doing so;1.3. ensure that its personnel are subject to appropriate obligations of confidentiality;1.4. taking into account the nature of the order, provide reasonable assistance to you, insofar as this is possible and at your cost, for the fulfilment of your obligations under the Data Protection Legislation in respect of data security; data breach notification; data protection impact assessments; prior consultation with supervisory authorities; and the fulfilment of data subject’s rights;1.5. taking into account the state of the art, the costs of implementation and the nature, scope, context and purposes of processing as well as the risk of varying likelihood and severity for the rights and freedoms of natural persons, have in place appropriate technical and organizational measures to ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk, and otherwise take all measures required under Article 32 of the GDPR;1.6. promptly notify you of any communication received relation to the parties’ obligations under the Data Protection Legislation with respect to Personal Data, including any communication from a data subject or supervisory authority; and1.7. upon termination of all services purchased from WCEPS, upon your request, return or delete the Personal Data, and delete any existing copies in its possession unless required to retain such Personal Data under applicable law.2. You consent to WCEPS engaging subcontractors to process the Personal Data on its behalf (“Sub-processors”). WCEPS shall ensure Sub-processors are subject to contractual obligations which are the same as or equivalent to those imposed on WCEPS under this Agreement. WCEPS shall inform you of any intended changes concerning the addition or replacement of any Sub-processor within a reasonable time and obtain the prior written consent of you prior to implementation of such change. In the event of your objection to such change, WCEPS shall make reasonable efforts to address your concerns (including making reasonable efforts to find an alternative Sub-processor). WCEPS shall be responsible for the performance of its Sub-processors.3. You acknowledges and agrees that Personal Data may be processed by Sub-processors outside the European Economic Area or the country where you are located in order to carry out the services purchased and WCEPS’s other obligations under this Agreement. WCEPS shall implement a data transfer solution to ensure any such transfers are compliant with the Data Protection Legislation.4. WCEPS shall use appropriate technical and organizational measures to protect Personal Data stored with WCEPS infrastructure against unauthorized and unlawful processing and against accidental loss, destruction, disclosure, damage or alteration, as notified to you in writing. You agrees that the technical and organizational measures are appropriate, taking into account the nature, scop...",
