    "id": "32f5b9f6-b868-4381-aa09-ce4bed185333",
    "title": "People",
    "content": "Description: Callsurveyv2\n\nPeople CALL Team Mark Blitz CALL Project Director at WCEPS Matt Messinger WCEPS Executive Director Bethany Parker WCEPS Director of Operations CARE Coaching Team The CARE Coaching Process at WCEPS combines practical data with personalized coaching sessions. Upon using tools such as CALL and WIDA SIS, our CARE Coaches work with school and district leaders to create supportive relationships that enable leaders to identify opportunities for growth and action steps for ongoing improvement. Yvonne Williams Director of MLL Educator Engagement at WCEPS, CARE Bilingual Coach: English/Spanish WestEd Team The CALL Team is proud to work with WestEd's School Improvement team in implementing Four Domains CALL, aligned to WestEd's Four Domains for Rapid School Improvement framework. The WestEd team provides invaluable support to state, district, and school leaders in leveraging CALL data to support continuous improvement planning. Contann Dabney School and District Senior Facilitator, Quality Schools and Districts Terry Hofer Director of School Improvement, WestEd Giselle Sherry-Marsh School Improvement Specialist, WestEd Principal Investigators CALL was developed as part of a 4-year grant from the Institute for Education Sciences (IES) in the US Department of Education. Researchers from the highly esteemed Department of Educational Leadership and Policy Analysis (ELPA) at the University of WisconsinMadison created, piloted, and validated the CALL survey and formative feedback system. Richard Halverson Professor, Department of Educational Leadership and Policy Analysis Wisconsin Center for Education Research University of Wisconsin – Madison Carolyn Kelley Professor, Department of Educational Leadership and Policy Analysis Wisconsin Center for Education Research University of Wisconsin – Madison",
