    "id": "fdb0aeaa-e2b6-4d82-aebf-cf57115d7110",
    "title": "Articles",
    "content": "Description: Callsurveyv2\n\nArticles Categories: All updates news USBE WestEd School Improvement Personalized Learning Long Distance CALL Virtual Online Remote Four Domains CALL at WestEd: What Leaders are Saying Categories: School Improvement Usbe West Ed Share School leaders share their experiences in using Four Domains CALL. Keep reading ... CALL Featured in UW-Madison School of Education Categories: News Updates Share CALL was featured in an online publication from UW-Madison's School of Eduction. \"Answering a ‘CALL’: School of Education research leads to business embraced by educators nationwide\" Keep reading ... USBE and WestEd Leaders on Four Domains CALL Share Tracy Vandeventer from the Utah State Board of Education and Terry Hofer from WestEd discuss the rollout of the Four Domains for Rapid School Improvement and Four Domains CALL in Utah. Keep reading ... WIDA SIS and CARE Coaching: What Educators are Saying Share Educators in School District 49 (CO) talk about their experience with WIDA SIS and the CARE Coaching Process. Keep reading ... Four Domains CALL in Utah Categories: School Improvement Usbe West Ed Share Keep reading ... Introducing: CALL for Personalized Learning Categories: Personalized Learning Share The CALL for Personalized Learning survey (CALL PL) has been developed specifically to evaluate eight key practices of personalized learning. CALL PL asks educators and leaders questions that evaluate the level of student choice and personalization. Upon completion, teachers receive individualized formative feedback, leaders get school and district level reports. Keep reading ... Moving Beyond Survival Mode In Schools | By Mark Blitz, CALL Project Director Categories: Long Distance Call Online Remote Virtual Share Times are challenging, especially \"in\" schools. And maintaining a school-wide focus on teaching and learning is more important than ever. Keep reading ... Long Distance CALL Categories: Long Distance Call Online Remote Virtual Share Long Distance CALL: a school-wide leadership assessment and feedback system for remote teaching and learning. Keep reading ... Supporting Leadership for Equity in Schools Cannot Stop Share Equity is not an afterthought or something we should work on \"if we have time.\" The L4L Coaching Team, with WIDA SIS, continues to work with schools to support leadership for teaching English Learners. Keep reading ... Tools for School Improvement in Our Current Situation and Beyond Share WIDA Professional Learning has a variety of offerings to support educators, education leaders, and multilingual learners during these unprecedented times and beyond. Keep reading ... Video: What is the WIDA School Improvement System (WIDA SIS)? Share This short video introduces the WIDA School Improvement System (WIDA SIS). Keep reading ... Short Demo of the WIDA SIS Online Reporting System Share The online reporting system for the WIDA School Improvement System (WIDA SIS) provides action-based data for supporting instruction of English Learners. Keep reading ... Progress Monitoring for Continuous Improvement: Utilizing Data from WIDA SIS Share The WIDA School Improvement System (WIDA SIS) is used to evaluate programs that focus on teaching and supporting ELs as well as monitoring progress over time. Keep reading ... \"This was not something that had been done before\": An Oral History of the Comprehensive Assessment of Leadership for Learning (CALL) | By Mark Blitz, CALL Project Director Share In celebration of the 10-year anniversary of the Comprehensive Assessment of Leadership for Learning (CALL), this oral history tells the origin story of CALL. Keep reading ... Recorded Webinar: The WIDA School Improvement System (WIDA SIS) Share WIDA SIS Webinar on August 15, 2019, 12:00 PM EST. Join Director of Consortium and State Relations, Jonathan Gibson, and WIDA SIS Project Director, Mark Blitz, to learn more about this new school improvement system. Keep reading ...",
